	quest.02BFE6EA90831AED.quest_subtitle: "Weight of a Thousand Burdens"
	quest.02BFE6EA90831AED.title: "Oath of the Overburdened Mind"
	quest.02C5ECCA9010AEA1.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.02C5ECCA9010AEA1.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.02CBB1D9A926F86B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Table Cloth&r"
		""
		"&7A block that combines item display and trading functionality. Can store and display up to four items, accessible by right-click. When multiple Table Cloths are placed adjacent, their textures will connect automatically.&r"
		""
		"&6Shop Function&r"
		"&7When used with &eStockbroker&r&7, it can create automated shops to sell items from your inventory to other players for a fee.&r"
		""
		"&6Setting Up Items for Sale&r"
		"&7To set up a shop, follow these steps:&r"
		"&7Hold the Table Cloth and right-click an &eStockbroker&r.&r"
		"&7In the interface, select the item and quantity to sell, specify the destination, then click the &a\"Configure\"&r&7 button.&r"
		"&7Place the configured Table Cloth at the desired location to display the merchandise.&r"
		"&7Set the price on the side of the Table Cloth.&r"
		"&7Each Table Cloth can be configured with up to nine items, but only the first four will be displayed at a time.&r"
		"&7Be sure to &clock the logistics network&r&7 in the upper-right corner of the Stockbroker interface to prevent others from directly extracting items.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Purchasing Items&r"
		"&7Point the crosshair at the Table Cloth to view transaction details. Direct trading is possible when stock is available.&r"
		"&7Right-clicking the Table Cloth gives a &ePurchase List&r&7 that records the currently selected items. Holding this list lets you continue buying other items from the same shop; additional selections are automatically added.&r"
		"&7With the Purchase List in hand, right-click the Stockbroker to check out. The system will deduct the corresponding payment items from your inventory. The &eStockbroker&r&7 will then send a request to extract the purchased items.&r"
		"&7Payment from customers is temporarily stored in the Stockbroker. Shop owners can right-click to collect it directly or use &ehoppers&r&7 or other components for automated extraction.&r"
		""
		"&8A small note beside the manuscript: Display, price, trade—all bound by a simple contract.&r"
	]
	quest.02CBB1D9A926F86B.quest_subtitle: "Table Cloth / Countertop"
	quest.02CBB1D9A926F86B.title: "Shop"
	quest.02EBF147125789FB.quest_desc: [
		"&7When equipped:"
		""
		"&7Enhances &#FFCC44Scythe&7 enchantments:"
		""
		"&7&#FFAA33Reap&7: Immediately returns upon hitting an entity, return speed increased to &e2&7×, damage increased to &e1.5&7×."
		""
		"&7&#88DDFFSoar&7:"
		"&7If &66FF66sprinting&7, horizontal speed reduced by &e0.6&7× the line-of-sight vector;"
		"&7Attack range reduced to &e2&7 blocks, offset &e2&7 blocks in the line-of-sight direction, damage increased to &e1.25&7×."
		""
		"&7Disables &#FFCC44Scythe&7 sweeping attacks."
		""
		"&7The &#FFCC44Scythe&7 icon above the player's experience bar indicates charge progress. Full charge takes &e10&7 seconds."
		""
		"&7When fully charged:"
		"&7When attacked by a creature, the &#FFCC44Scythe&7 icon lights up and grants &e5&7 seconds of &#CC6666Malevolent Intent&7. Base effect level is &eII&7; for every &e6&7 damage taken, the level increases by &e1&7, up to &eXI&7."
		""
		"&7While holding &#CC6666Malevolent Intent&7, attacking other creatures with a &#FFCC44Scythe&7 triggers a chain slash:"
		""
		"&7Cancels this attack;"
		"&7Chain slash range is centered on the scythe boomerang or the attacker's position, within &e8×8×8&7 blocks;"
		"&7Damage multiplier = clamp(attack speed, &e0&7, &e2&7) * (effect level * &e2&7 - &e1&7);"
		"&7Duration is &e25&7 game ticks, dealing (original damage / duration * damage multiplier) physical and magic damage every tick to all creatures within range except the attacker, ignoring invincibility frames;"
		"&7&#CC66FFSoul Reaper&7's chance to apply &#CC6666Soul Harvest&7 is reduced to &e40%&7;"
		"&7Resets charge time to &e10&7 seconds."
		""
		"&7While charging, attacking other creatures resets the charge time to &e15&7 seconds."
	]
	quest.02EBF147125789FB.quest_subtitle: "Scythe Authority"
	quest.02F458E4623EBD67.quest_desc: ["&7Right-click to &#FFD700charge&7 forward, performing &#CC99FFspear thrusts&7 along the path. Sneak + Right-click performs &#CC99FFspear thrusts&7 around you."]
	quest.02F458E4623EBD67.quest_subtitle: "Forward, Unstoppable!"
	quest.03639EDED6577831.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Melancholy\",\"color\":\"aqua\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When casting spells:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Each spell cast grants 1 stack of \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Arcane Brand\"\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", up to 5 stacks, lasting 60 seconds\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Each stack provides \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"cast speed, cooldown reduction, and spell power\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When attacking a target with \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Arcane Brand\"\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" (at max 5 stacks):\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Deal \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"bonus spell damage\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Apply \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Arcane Brand\"\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" to the target\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Reset your own Brand stacks\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When an enemy with \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Arcane Brand\"\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" dies:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"All players within 10 blocks \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"restore 15% max health and 200 mana\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
	]
	quest.03639EDED6577831.quest_subtitle: "Melancholy Erosion"
	quest.03639EDED6577831.title: "Melancholy Erosion"
	quest.038444481D165CED.quest_subtitle: "Analysis Paralysis"
	quest.038444481D165CED.title: "Equipment Selection"
	quest.03D7343C57EF0A14.quest_desc: [
		"&7Prolonged exposure to &#66FF99Essence&7 seems to have left my mind somewhat confused. I can even hear strange &#88DDFFcalls&7 echoing in my ears... No, that's not right."
		""
		"&7When holding a &#CC99FFSoul Stone&7, the &#88DDFFcalls&7 grow clearer—it seems to want to lead me somewhere."
		""
		"&7An &#CC66FFEye of Ender&7 points to the End portal. If I infuse a &#CC99FFSoul Stone&7 into it, where will it point?"
	]
	quest.03D7343C57EF0A14.quest_subtitle: "Soul Resonance"
	quest.03D7343C57EF0A14.title: "The Call"
	quest.0401FD00A60774F8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Torreya Forest&r"
		"&7A surface biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Torreya Forests typically generate along the &#5CACEEEther River&r&7."
		"&7The &#8B7355Torreya trees&r&7 are tall and dense, forming winding narrow waterways with the Ether River."
		"&7This also causes Torreya Forests to frequently border multiple different surface biomes."
		""
		"&7The high brightness of &#5CACEEEther fluid&r&7 and &#8B7355Torreya Vines&r&7 significantly reduces monster spawning on the biome's surface."
	]
	quest.0401FD00A60774F8.quest_subtitle: "Crossroads"
	quest.0401FD00A60774F8.title: "Torreya Forest"
	quest.0429A6763D6D23B3.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The Paint Mixer is a crafting device used to create paints. By mixing dyes, materials, or other paints, you can produce paints with \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"custom colors\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" for dyeing tool and equipment parts.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Making Paint\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Place any number of the following items into the Paint Mixer's input slots:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Input Items\",\"color\":\"yellow\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Dye\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\": Provides the dye's color\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Paint\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\": Provides the paint's color\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Material\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\": Provides the material's color\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Slime Ball\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\": Increases output quantity\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.0429A6763D6D23B3.quest_subtitle: "Specialized Equipment for Making Paints"
	quest.0429A6763D6D23B3.title: "Paint Mixer"
	quest.046E980EB69A1209.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mini Totem&r"
		"&7Can be bound to a familiar, and a familiar can only be bound to one totem at a time. When the familiar dies and you have no mana to revive it, the bound totem will be consumed to &aresurrect&r&7 the familiar. The totem is consumed in the process.&r"
	]
	quest.0490EDB36F1CF908.quest_desc: [
		"&7Theoretically, you could also get this from equipment bags in Stage I."
		""
		"&mEquip me and I'll make you fly&r"
	]
	quest.0490EDB36F1CF908.quest_subtitle: "The Sky Is the Limit"
	quest.04DD58980F332FEE.quest_desc: ["&7Similar to a knife, but with lower damage and attack speed. However, it is more &#66DDCCdurable&7 and can be used for cutting board recipes."]
	quest.04DD58980F332FEE.quest_subtitle: "Survival Essential"
	quest.04F1594414B048D0.quest_desc: [
		"&7Increases the stack size per slot in backpacks. Each backpack can hold up to three Stack Upgrades, and their multiplicative effect yields an extremely high stack limit."
		""
		"&7Stack Upgrades also work on tanks, increasing their storage capacity accordingly."
	]
	quest.04F1594414B048D0.quest_subtitle: "Stack a little, stack a little more, stack a whole lot more"
	quest.05499B6A45252488.quest_desc: ["&7Obtained by throwing a pumpkin into the &#CC99FFVoid Well&7. Place it on &#55D5D5Soul Sand&7 and use &#66FF66Bone Meal&7 to grow it, producing &#FF6666Suffering Piles&7."]
	quest.05499B6A45252488.quest_subtitle: "Life Is So Hard"
	quest.056130E2CD71DC75.quest_desc: [
		"&7This modpack includes extensive &#FFD700QOL tweaks&7 and optimizations for &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7, delivering a &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7 experience unlike any other pack! Enjoy!"
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"Click to jump to Silent Gear\", \"underlined\": true, \"color\":\"yellow\",\"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"09E68D57095A5F1D\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.056130E2CD71DC75.quest_subtitle: "The Root of All Evil"
	quest.056130E2CD71DC75.title: "It's Actually a Blueprint"
	quest.058E2E161B35737E.quest_desc: ["A great early-game trait—summons wolves when hit."]
	quest.058E2E161B35737E.quest_subtitle: "Wolf Pack Form"
	quest.0594FF6909227B41.quest_desc: [
		"&6All&r material stats can be viewed in the &6Materials Lexicon&r, and trait effects can be searched in EMI."
		""
		"&7Cod isn't very good at writing quests... please forgive any rough spots..."
		""
		"It's okay, I'll help Cod write them—oh wait, I'm not good at it either. My apologies."
	]
	quest.0594FF6909227B41.quest_subtitle: "To view stat rankings, check the Materials Lexicon"
	quest.0594FF6909227B41.title: "Materials can be searched in EMI: Silent Gear Materials to view all materials"
	quest.059AFBCEE942C1B4.quest_desc: ["Recommended for both mages and warriors alike. Provides damage scaling based on your mana bar."]
	quest.059AFBCEE942C1B4.quest_subtitle: "Damage-Boosting Material"
	quest.059D21A5F949C15C.quest_desc: [
		"&2Players can store enchanted books in this device, converting them into corresponding enchantment experience. This experience can be used to split or merge enchanted books."
		""
		"&cWithdrawing an enchanted book consumes the corresponding enchantment experience, with costs increasing exponentially with level."
		""
		"&2This mechanic reduces the number of equipment modifications needed—a top-tier item may only need 1 modification instead of 4-5, significantly saving experience."
		""
		"&7Can be mined by hand; pickaxes speed up the process. Can be upgraded via infusion into the Library of Alexandria."
		""
		"&eMining and upgrading do not cause loss of stored enchantments."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Usage: The search bar at the top of the GUI allows direct searching for the desired enchanted book. The three slots on the right, from top to bottom, are: Filter Slot (yellow)—place an enchantable item to display supported enchantments; Input Slot (blue)—insert enchanted books to store them in the library; Output Slot (yellow)—used to withdraw selected enchanted books. You can also place an existing enchanted book in the output slot to continue selecting enchantments."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Storage: Enchantments are stored as enchantment points within the device. Enchantment points represent the number of level 1 books of that enchantment. When withdrawing, enchantments consume the corresponding enchantment points based on vanilla anvil cost calculations, but without incurring prior work penalties. Merging enchantments in the library significantly reduces prior work penalties."
	]
	quest.059D21A5F949C15C.quest_subtitle: "Here, May You Find the Book You Seek"
	quest.059D21A5F949C15C.title: "A New Way to Store Magic"
	quest.059FEF132D3FF800.quest_desc: ["&7Right-click to block like a &#FFD700shield&7 (though the animation looks like throwing a sword). For &c2 seconds&7 after a successful block, the next attack deals &a50%&7 more damage."]
	quest.059FEF132D3FF800.quest_subtitle: "My Blade and Shield"
	quest.05A4F69164ABBCCA.quest_desc: ["&7Functions like a vanilla &#66CCFFBow&7."]
	quest.05A4F69164ABBCCA.quest_subtitle: "Classic Ranged Weapon"
	quest.05EA527792F0F44E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Scythe Blade Power&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Scythe Blade Power grants the wearer strength at the cost of &8souls&r&7 taken by the scythe. Over time, each kill makes the held &eweapon&r&7 increasingly &apowerful&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.05EA527792F0F44E.quest_subtitle: "Destroying What Is Broken"
	quest.05F6670AAFE979C5.quest_subtitle: "Time for a break, right?"
	quest.05F6670AAFE979C5.title: "Playtime 4h"
	quest.065CA86479CA3AF9.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FFD700Signal Wave Totem Control&7"
		""
		"&7When multiple rituals are active simultaneously, the order in which they take effect is extremely difficult to keep consistent."
		""
		"&7Normally, a spirit ritual only initiates after collecting enough energy from the world's natural arcane flow."
		"&7For a &#66CCFFSignal Wave Totem Pedestal&7, this energy remains in a state of \"&#FFD700reserve&7\" until it receives a &#FF6666Redstone pulse&7."
		"&7When organizing multiple rituals, a &#FF8844Redstone Repeater&7 can be used to pinpoint the exact tick a spirit ritual can activate."
		""
		"&7Timing the pulse to the &#66CCFFSignal Wave Totem Pedestal&7 may be difficult."
		"&7Note that a continuous signal is not required—the internal circuit only recognizes the pulse at the start of the signal."
	]
	quest.065CA86479CA3AF9.quest_subtitle: "&6Miracles Manifest in the World"
	quest.065CA86479CA3AF9.title: "Totem Magic II"
	quest.06C2F1EFADAD809F.quest_desc: [
		"&7An expensive but powerful material. Mithril is found between Y=-63 and Y=-38, with relatively low spawn rates—mining with a Hammershot makes it easier. Fortune enchantment affects drop rates. Lightning Bottles are obtained by right-clicking a Charged Creeper with a glass bottle, or found in hidden chests within Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks structures."
		""
		"&7Its strength lies in the Arcane Resonance IV trait. Every 10 Mana provides 1% damage bonus, capped at Trait Level × 20. With sufficient mana, a Thunderweave Handle can provide a terrifying 80% damage boost."
		""
		"&eIf multiple pieces of gear have Arcane Resonance, the mana bonus stacks, but the damage bonus does not—only the highest level applies."
	]
	quest.06C2F1EFADAD809F.quest_subtitle: "Excellent Damage-Boosting Material"
	quest.06CCE0753B027D72.quest_subtitle: "Update 1.1"
	quest.070C94F2F2F2D972.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mending Diffuser&r"
		""
		"&7The Mending Diffuser uses fresh blood as a sympathetic anchor for natural regeneration. After completing one &6focused cycle&r&7, a crucible equipped with it has a small chance to repair any &eRune&r&7 by a small amount. However, it cannot save a Rune that has already shattered.&r"
	]
	quest.070C94F2F2F2D972.quest_subtitle: "Dead Scar Tissue"
	quest.073C903793B7F71F.title: "Discover the Sunken City"
	quest.075AC794CF9E3665.quest_desc: [
		"# &eResource Pack Management &r"
		""
		"### &cResource Pack Path &r"
		"&7<Reverie Foundry>"
		"&7\\config\\\\paxi\\\\resourcepacks"
		""
		"### &6Recommendations &r"
		"&f- Delete unwanted resource packs from this path"
		"&f- &cSome resources require additional removal in kubejs &r"
		"&f- For GUI texture packs:"
		"  &7▪ &aStrongly recommend replacing instead of deleting &r"
		"  &7▪ Replacing avoids missing UI elements"
		""
		"### &3Notes &r"
		"&7- Back up original files before making changes"
		"&7- Deleting some resource packs may cause display issues"
		"If display issues occur, also delete resourcepack_load_order.json"
	]
	quest.075AC794CF9E3665.quest_subtitle: "PAXI"
	quest.078C80DB81D1640E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Modpack Command Quick Reference&r"
		"&7The modpack provides many custom commands.&r"
		""
		"&6Wendigo&r"
		"&7&e/rf wendigosystem toggle&r&7 - Toggle Wendigo effect&r"
		"&7&e/rf wendigosystem status&r&7 - Check status&r"
		""
		"&6Ore Stages&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage&r&7 - View current stage status&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage reset&r&7 - &cReset all data (use with caution)&r&7"
		"&7&e/rf orestage reload&r&7 - Reload config file&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage validate&r&7 - Validate config and auto-repair&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage info&r&7 - View detailed progress info&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage kills&r&7 - View kill statistics&r"
		""
		"&6Utility Functions&r"
		"&7&e/rf entityclean&r&7 - Clean up miscellaneous entities nearby. By default only cleans certain dropped items, arrows, etc. (configurable)&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Added Suffering&r"
		""
		"&6Status Management&r"
		"&7&e/rf deathsystem toggle&r&7 - Enable/disable death penalty system&r"
		"&7&e/rf deathsystem status&r&7 - View death statistics and current status&r"
		""
		"&6Data Reset&r"
		"&7&e/rf deathsystem reset&r&7 - &cReset death count and restore max health on next respawn&r"
		""
		"&7&e/rf depression toggle&r&7 - Toggle Depression (Added Suffering)&r"
		"&7&e/rf depression status&r&7 - View Depression status (Added Suffering)&r"
		""
		"&6Item Give Commands&r"
		"&7&e/rf give randomenchanted&r&7 - Receive a random enchanted book&r"
		"&7&e/rf give randomscrollid&r&7 - Receive a random spell scroll&r"
		"&7&e/rf give drunkard&r&7 - Receive the &bDrunkard Set&r&7 (various alcoholic beverages)&r"
		"&7&e/rf give traveler&r&7 - Receive the &bTraveler Set&r&7 (backpack + enchanted books)&r"
		"&7&e/rf give sorcerer&r&7 - Receive the &bSorcerer Set&r&7 (spellcasting equipment)&r"
		"&7&e/rf give warrior&r&7 - Receive the &bWarrior Set&r&7 (combat equipment)&r"
		""
		"&6Admin Functions&r"
		"&7&e/rf give <set_name> <player_name>&r&7 - Give a set to another player&r"
		"&7&e/rf give <set_name> <player_name> clear&r&7 - &cReset a player's claim limit&r"
		""
		"&7&e/wits - Check the current structure you are in"
	]
	quest.078C80DB81D1640E.quest_subtitle: "I Understand"
	quest.078C80DB81D1640E.title: "Useful Commands"
	quest.07C86BA6CAFFD6C8.quest_subtitle: "View the enhancements your current familiar has gained"
	quest.07E7C74E2EA9FB8E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Spiraling Algae Forest&r"
		"&7A marine biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7The Spiraling Algae Forest has a distinctly different vegetation cover compared to the Starlight Sea."
		"&7Its main vegetation consists of &#20B2AASpiraling Algae&r&7, &#98FB98Sea Candle Grass&r&7, and &#DB7093Sea Roses&r&7, rather than the usual &#9ACD32Abyssal Fruit plants&r."
		""
		"&7Non-aquatic creatures can only spawn dozens of blocks below the surface of the Spiraling Algae Forest."
	]
	quest.07E7C74E2EA9FB8E.quest_subtitle: "Eternal Feast"
	quest.07E7C74E2EA9FB8E.title: "Spiraling Algae Forest"
	quest.07E84F32AFD0365F.quest_subtitle: "\"Then, I will naturally show you what power truly means.\""
	quest.07F1B2594FCCAF01.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Agility&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Agility compels the mind to seek movement in times of danger, increasing &amovement speed&r&7. The amount gained increases as the wearer's vitality fades, up to double speed.&r"
	]
	quest.07F1B2594FCCAF01.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Urges Flight"
	quest.082F47A08B859C62.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.082F47A08B859C62.quest_subtitle: "Stage 3"
	quest.085ED7F06792B829.title: "Frozen Man"
	quest.08600655258549DB.quest_desc: ["&7Extremely powerful—eat it instantly, and with high-saturation food, become an immortal demon... as long as you don't get one-shot."]
	quest.08600655258549DB.quest_subtitle: "Someone, feed this gentleman some bread!"
	quest.086482C52023DB55.quest_subtitle: "A utility tool for finding the nearest underground dragon lair"
	quest.086F7ED726FBC65F.quest_desc: ["&7Obtained by killing dragons. Can also be found early via exploration and scavenging. Offers solid stats and remains useful throughout the early-to-mid game."]
	quest.086F7ED726FBC65F.quest_subtitle: "You're a Dragon Too, Huh"
	quest.08A257E690F34298.quest_desc: ["&7Theoretically an extremely durable material—stores energy and provides massive healing. Obtained after defeating the Dead King. A highly reliable sustain option for tough fights."]
	quest.08A257E690F34298.quest_subtitle: "Theoretical Survivor"
	quest.08C5CE1D2BDAE5E9.quest_subtitle: "Kill Kill Kill"
	quest.08DB4D29BBE0A6CD.quest_desc: ["&7Great base stats and exceptional Starlight Affinity. Even just using its trait, it's already top-tier. A worthwhile investment with great versatility."]
	quest.08DB4D29BBE0A6CD.quest_subtitle: "Stellar Core"
	quest.0919F71D241AFD81.quest_desc: [
		"&6Authority of the Gleeful Target&r"
		""
		"&7Your form is frozen in time—an anomaly detached from the world. It does not age, nor can it perceive the outside.&r"
		"&7-All &chealing&r&7 received is reduced to one quarter&r"
		""
		"&7Authority—a pact between your form and the world itself.&r"
		"&7-When struck, the form enters a &6Stasis State&r"
		"&7-While in &6Stasis State&r&7, all &epotion effects&r&7 have their timers paused and do not expire&r"
		"&7-Effects that require time to pass, such as health regeneration and poison, are disabled. Those unaffected by stasis still function&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/authority_of_the_gleeful_target.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0919F71D241AFD81.quest_subtitle: "The Happiest in the World"
	quest.0919F71D241AFD81.title: "Authority of the Gleeful Target"
	quest.092C65BDEC1E30A4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Transmutation Table&r"
		""
		"&7Worried your weapon is too ugly?&r"
		"&7Worried it doesn't have enough swag?&r"
		""
		"&7The Transmutation Table is your first choice! Whether you want to &aturn a sheep into a tiger&r&7 or &aturn a tiger into a sheep&r&7—it's all up to you!&r"
		""
		"&7Place the &eweapon&r&7 you want to transmute in the first slot, and the item you want it to look like in the second slot. Then consume Amethyst energy to transmute your weapon!&r&7&r"
	]
	quest.092C65BDEC1E30A4.quest_subtitle: "Ever-Changing"
	quest.0973A81F39964B58.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.09BD7CB2DEA2CD89.quest_desc: ["Allows customization of arrow velocity and accuracy."]
	quest.09BD7CB2DEA2CD89.quest_subtitle: "Customized Experience"
	quest.0A12067C6B752CAC.quest_desc: ["&7Through the power of the Heart of the Sea, the Ocean Bookshelf has been transformed. Its power is more abundant yet gentle. This bookshelf provides two to three times the &aEterna&7 and &5Arcana&7 of its predecessor. However, the power of the Heart of the Sea is ultimately gentle—it does not raise the &aEterna&7 cap beyond its limit. After all, perfection is rare; achieving this much is already commendable."]
	quest.0A12067C6B752CAC.quest_subtitle: "Mystical Embrace"
	quest.0A12067C6B752CAC.title: "Heart's Blessing"
	quest.0A13EAB37AB4ACEF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Familiar Trinkets&r"
		"&7Familiar trinkets are items that can be equipped in the trinket slot, providing different buffs to the corresponding familiar.&r"
		""
		"&7&eMagic Leaves&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &bDruid&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &bJungle Temples&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eHunter's Chain&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &bHunter&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &cEvoker Fortresses&r&7 or &bHunter Camps&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eLich's Crest Necklace&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &cNecromancer&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &8cemeteries&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eCrown of Oblivion&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &bSummoner&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &cAncient Cities&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eCrown of Brilliance&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &6Archmage&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &6Archmage Labs&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eGolden Bell&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &dIllusionist&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &bWoodland Mansions&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eWizard's Candlestick&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &eScorcher&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &cPyromancer Towers&r&7.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&eBlessed Chalice&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &aCleric&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &aPriest Cottages&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eThunder Crest Necklace&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &6Mage&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &bMountain Towers&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&ePutrid Cheese Necklace&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &cPlague Doctor&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &bIce Spike Shipwrecks&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eLost Melody&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &dBard&r&7 familiar. Can be obtained via &eMystic Orb&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eFrostbloom&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &bFrostling&r&7 familiar. Can be found in &bIce Spider Nests&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eDragon Tear&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of the &6Dragon Warrior&r&7 familiar. Dropped by the &cEnder Dragon&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&ePandora's Box&r&7: Allows &asummoning/dismissing&r&7 up to 10 familiars at once. Crafted via recipe.&r"
	]
	quest.0A13EAB37AB4ACEF.title: "Any Familiar Trinket"
	quest.0A1FF9CCFB4FEA6C.quest_subtitle: "Can't come back empty-handed..."
	quest.0A1FF9CCFB4FEA6C.title: "First Fish Caught"
	quest.0ABD1C741FFFC78C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Burning Frenzy&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Burning Frenzy functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bBurning Frenzy&r&7 effect, slightly increasing &aattack&r&7 and &amining&r&7 speed.&r"
	]
	quest.0ABD1C741FFFC78C.quest_subtitle: "Sharpening Pulse"
	quest.0AC4291DE561460A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ether River&r"
		"&7A relatively rare surface biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Like rivers in the Overworld, it is typically a &8transition biome&r that separates waterways within or between biomes."
		"&7Scattered &#E6E6FAThioquartz Blocks&r&7 can sometimes be found along the banks of the Ether River for players to mine."
		""
		"&7&#5CACEEEther&r&7 is a highly &cdangerous&r&7 high-brightness fluid that prevents any vegetation or creatures from spawning on its surface."
		"&7Creatures can only spawn dozens of blocks below the Ether River."
		""
		"&7The underground area beneath the Ether River is the only place where &#E6E6FAThioquartz Geodes&r&7 can generate."
		""
		"&#5CACEEEther&r&7 can be used as fuel in furnaces."
	]
	quest.0AC4291DE561460A.quest_subtitle: "Painless Death"
	quest.0AC4291DE561460A.title: "Ether River"
	quest.0AD556BD2B2A47D2.quest_desc: [
		"&7Hold a fluid bucket and right-click to pour liquid into the &#FFD700Furnace&7."
		""
		"&7A &#66CCFFDrain&7 must be connected to output liquids from the &#FFD700Furnace&7. You can also use"
		"[ { \"text\": \"Fluid Pipes [Click to Jump]\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"1F38C534465F33BC\" } } ]"
		"&7to import fluids into the &#FFD700Furnace&7 for automation."
		""
		"&7Please note: Do not use the copper hopper from the &#FF6666Extra Delight&7 mod to transport fluids into tanks, as it will cause &#FF6666fluid loss&7."
	]
	quest.0AD556BD2B2A47D2.quest_subtitle: "Exporting Liquid? Importing Liquid?"
	quest.0ADEACC84320DCC0.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Refining system is an &5advanced enhancement mechanic&7 for &6Silent Gear&7 equipment. It improves &aquality&7 through &bcombat wear&7. Each time &cequipment breaks&7, it accumulates &eexperience&7. After enough breaks, the &dRefining Level&7 increases, granting &3random attribute bonuses&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&lCore Mechanics:&r"
		"&7Refining Level caps at &6V&r"
		"&7Each level requires accumulating &especific break counts&r"
		"&7Modifying equipment reduces its Refining Level by &c2 levels&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Each trait is generated independently. Without &6Refining Strength Modifiers&7, bonuses range randomly from &a-25%&7 to &c+25%&7."
		""
		"&7The same attribute can appear at &bdifferent levels&7, and their effects &estack&7."
		"&7Duplicate attributes &cwill not&7 appear within the same level."
		"&7Equipment can have up to &d5 different traits&7."
		""
		"&6Refining Probability Modifier&7"
		"&7Some special materials provide &b\"Refining Modifiers\"&7 that affect the bonus range during refining:"
		"&aHigher positive modifiers&7: Higher chance and cap for positive bonuses"
		"&cHigher negative modifiers&7: Higher chance and cap for negative bonuses"
		"&7Modifier range: &e-50 ~ +50"
		""
		"&6Refining Strength Modifier&7"
		"&7Some special materials provide &b\"Refining Modifiers\"&7 that affect the bonus cap during refining:"
		"&aHigher positive modifiers&7: Higher cap for positive traits"
		"&cHigher negative modifiers&7: Higher cap for negative traits"
		"&7Modifier range: &e-50 ~ +50"
	]
	quest.0ADEACC84320DCC0.quest_subtitle: "Refining Equipment"
	quest.0B0C47F37FDE6435.quest_desc: [
		"&7Soulwoven Silk is a light yet resilient material, filled with &6souls&r&7 and such. Like the form, it innately blocks &darcane energy&r&7. Though other materials can do this, &6Soulwoven Silk&r&7 is easier to work with—at least better than &8stone&r&7."
		""
		"&7Shards of souls can glow, and souls themselves can glow. Why not let the souls within the silk shine?"
		""
		"&7I crafted several &bbanners&r&7 to test the effect, using various &ereagents&r&7 and &6essences&r&7 to design patterns. When infused with energy, they emit a &8dim glow&r&7; adding another essence makes them &ebrilliant&r&7."
	]
	quest.0B0C47F37FDE6435.quest_subtitle: "Weaving the Unreal"
	quest.0B33B7CF2E127A4F.quest_desc: [
		"&7You often need to store a large number of items during your journey. While chests offer considerable capacity, they aren't always convenient in certain situations..."
		""
		"&f\"Come one, come all! You won't regret it, you won't be ripped off. A set of &#66CCFF99% new storage components&f, used by a female gamer. Order now and receive a free &#66DDCC16K Storage Block&f! Don't underestimate this &#66CCFFStorage Component&f—it's small when in your bag, but expands and grows tall when powered. Great for storing ores, junk, and food—very convenient! Act now and grab yours before they're gone!\""
	]
	quest.0B33B7CF2E127A4F.quest_subtitle: "Convenient and Fast"
	quest.0B33B7CF2E127A4F.title: "AAA Kourindou Used Goods Wholesale"
	quest.0BA8FDE1647AA593.quest_subtitle: "Keep Going"
	quest.0BA8FDE1647AA593.title: "First Death"
	quest.0BB5CE1550F46002.quest_desc: [
		""
		"When you have tasks you need to keep track of but worry about forgetting, click the position shown in the image to pin them."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/ftb_kjs2.png width:200 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
		""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Success Example:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/ftb_kjs1.png width:80 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0BB5CE1550F46002.quest_subtitle: "What Was I Supposed to Do Again?"
	quest.0BB5CE1550F46002.title: "Pin"
	quest.0BCF6B18963AB88F.quest_desc: [
		"&7The tomb of the &#FF6666Dead King&7 contains a special cell with a loot barrel that may contain a &#FFD700Summon Dead King&7 scroll. This scroll requires &#FFAA3315000 Mana&7 to cast and generally cannot be cast from a spellbook. However, casting directly from hand ignores the mana cost, though the scroll is &#FF6666consumed&7 in the process."
		""
		"&7Please note that the &#FF6666Enraged Dead King&7 summoned by this scroll is an enhanced boss and is not friendly."
		""
		"&7The dead monster, forcibly revived by some magic, seems to be driven by some unseen will."
		""
		"&8\"A will forcibly stitched into a broken vessel by necromancy. When these fragile threads snap once more, the power it held—a power that should not exist—begins to crumble.\""
	]
	quest.0BCF6B18963AB88F.quest_subtitle: "Power of the Dead"
	quest.0BCF6B18963AB88F.title: "Enraged Dead King"
	quest.0C1EFCAED337180F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Aurora Deer&r&7"
		"&7Neutral creatures that fight back when attacked. They only spawn on the surface of the &#87CEEBStarlight Permafrost Forest&r&7; &r"
		""
		"&7They only perform melee attacks and have low aggression; &r"
		""
		"&7After being hit, they lower their heads to charge up (players near their head take melee damage, which may interrupt the charge); &r"
		""
		"&7Once charged, they &00FFFFcharge&r&7 in a random straight line for several blocks, dealing melee damage to targets in their path; &r"
		""
		"&7All of the above attacks can be blocked by shields. &r"
		""
		"&7&#FFA500Aurora Antlers&r&7 cannot be dropped upon death; &r"
		""
		"&7If an Aurora Deer crashes into any &808080stone block&r&7 during a charge: &r"
		""
		"&7It will drop one full-durability &#FFA500Aurora Antler&r&7, and the deer's model will lose one antler; &r"
		""
		"&7Each Aurora Deer can drop up to two &#FFA500Aurora Antlers&r&7; losing antlers does not affect its attack damage. &r"
	]
	quest.0C1EFCAED337180F.title: "Aurora Deer"
	quest.0C2F2186BE39605E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hunter Camps&r"
		"&7Hunters live in groups, thus they build camps along major hunting routes, primarily in &bforest&r&7 areas rich in prey. These camps can also be found using &eRolled Maps&r&7 obtained from the Origin Island.&r"
	]
	quest.0C2F2186BE39605E.quest_subtitle: "Discover a Hunter Camp"
	quest.0C2F2186BE39605E.title: "&6Hunter Camp&r"
	quest.0C95DCE08BB56AF5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Soul Fortification&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Soul Fortification does not enhance the form's abilities, but instead applies pressure to its arcane existence, increasing the capacity and stability of the &esoul shield&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.0C95DCE08BB56AF5.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Urges Creation"
	quest.0CC6907B16C93F5E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Combines &ccombat&7, &bfelling&7, and &aharvesting&7 in one tool."
		"&7Attack speed is slightly slower. Left-clicking crops performs &aarea harvesting&7, but does not replant."
	]
	quest.0CC6907B16C93F5E.quest_subtitle: "Essence of the Jungle"
	quest.0CCFA64CA88D2D22.quest_desc: [
		"# &3Press R for one-click sorting (default settings) &r"
		""
		"### &bNotes &r"
		"&7- By default, pressing R sorts in Creative mode order&r"
		"&7- Pressing Shift+R sorts by quantity&r"
		"&7- Pressing Ctrl+R sorts alphabetically&r"
		"&7- Pressing Alt+R sorts by ID&r"
	]
	quest.0CCFA64CA88D2D22.quest_subtitle: "Multiple Options!"
	quest.0CCFA64CA88D2D22.title: "R-Key Sorting"
	quest.0CE3D98152F44B6E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Explosions caused by the wearer:"
		""
		"&7Are affected by &66FF66Fortune III&7;"
		""
		"&7Avoid destroying valuable drops (&#CC6666#malum:prospectors_treasure&7): ores, storage/compressed blocks, ingots, nuggets, gems, raw mineral resources, coal, metal nodes, geodes."
		""
		"&7Netherite scraps are not covered by this tag and will be destroyed by explosions."
	]
	quest.0CE3D98152F44B6E.quest_subtitle: "Demolition Miner"
	quest.0CFA26B3944AAF49.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"To enhance material stats, use the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Starlight Charger\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" for empowerment.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Set up a 7×7 area in the open. Place the Charger in the center and a two-block-high pillar at each corner. The blocks placed on top determine the charge level:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/starlight_charger.png width:180 height:100 align:center}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Charged materials gain a stat boost, but the increase is applied to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"specific values\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" (e.g., 12 attack damage → 13). Percentage-based stats see little to no improvement.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Level 1: \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Crimson Steel Block\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", requires \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Gold Dust\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" as catalyst.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Level 2: \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Azure Electrum Block\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", requires \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Azure Silver Dust\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" as catalyst.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Level 3: \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Tyr Steel Block\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\", requires \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Star Glitter Dust\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" as catalyst.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Wait about 15 seconds for the Charger to recognize the setup. It works in \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"open-air areas at night\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" and consumes \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"energy\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" while active.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Higher-tier Chargers can use lower-tier catalysts, but the charge level is determined by the catalyst's tier.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.0CFA26B3944AAF49.quest_subtitle: "&cImportant Item"
	quest.0D0DADF7C531B664.quest_desc: ["&7If you lack experience while enchanting, Ancient Knowledge Potions can solve most problems. Simply add Bottles o' Enchanting to an Awkward Potion to create a potion that significantly increases experience gained. Adding more Bottles o' Enchanting to the finished potion stacks the effect for a massive boost."]
	quest.0D0DADF7C531B664.quest_subtitle: "Tasty Little Drink"
	quest.0D134B44D9F3BA01.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Shield"
		"&7Accelerated externals and fragile nature are inseparable.&r&cSoul shield stability halved"
		"&7Accelerated form of the soul shield, turning danger into safety like a timely rain.&r&aIncreases soul shield capacity&r&aSoul shield recovery rate doubled"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_shield.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0D134B44D9F3BA01.quest_subtitle: "Act with Vigilance"
	quest.0D134B44D9F3BA01.title: "Pact of the Shield"
	quest.0D1AFFB3C244802E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Portal Frame&r"
		"&7A functional block that helps mages create permanent portals.&r"
		"&7When first placed, the Portal Frame is just an empty shell with collision only on its borders.&r"
		""
		"&7By casting the &bEnder Portal&r&7 spell on the frame using tools like the &eWand of Resonance&r&7, it becomes a functional portal. It connects to another Portal Frame that has also been enchanted with the Ender Portal spell. There is no distance limit between these two portals, and the connection is permanent.&r"
		""
		"&7Do not break this block while a portal is active, or the model will disappear while the block persists until you connect it to another portal.&r"
		""
		"&7Players can dye an active portal using any dye, and the linked portal will automatically be dyed the same color.&r"
		""
		"&8It yearns to be given a destined pair. Without its other half, even the void cannot erase it."
	]
	quest.0D1AFFB3C244802E.quest_subtitle: "Fast Travel"
	quest.0D88330EEA17433A.quest_desc: ["&7Fires homing &#66CCFFghost sandstorms&7 at enemies."]
	quest.0D88330EEA17433A.quest_subtitle: "Hacks detected"
	quest.0DA24AFB83B99AA4.quest_desc: ["Boosts soul shield durability and attack speed. Recommended when your weapon has low attack speed."]
	quest.0DA24AFB83B99AA4.quest_subtitle: "Defensive Specialist"
	quest.0DDD36DA6EAB60C4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Dark Swamp&r"
		"&7A surface biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7The Dark Swamp is composed of &#4A331ANight Mud&r&7 and &#7FCC7FMirage Grass&r&7, with a relatively open terrain and numerous shallow pools complementing the ground."
		"&7In addition to the standard Grimstone and Voidstone layers, the Dark Swamp also generates a unique \"&#4A331ANight Mud Layer&r&7\" between the surface and the Grimstone layer."
		""
		"&7The Night Mud Layer consists mainly of &#4A331ANight Mud&r&7 and &#A0A0A0Night Mud Bricks&r&7. Most plants that grow on the Dark Swamp's surface can also grow in the Night Mud Layer (including wild &#FF9900Temperate Fruit&r&7 crops)."
		"&7&#4A331ANight Mud Deep Silver Ore&r&7 or &#A0A0A0Night Mud Brick Deep Silver Ore&r&7 can generate in the Night Mud Layer—these are unique variants of &#C0C0C0Deep Silver Ore&r&7 found only in this biome."
		"&7Similarly, the underground of this biome is the only place where &#9A32CDMalarite Ore&r&7 can naturally generate."
		""
		"&7The main tree of the Dark Swamp is the &#2F4F4FDark Mangrove&r&7 (corresponding to the Overworld's mangrove)."
		"&7Compared to the Overworld's mangrove swamp, trees in this biome are spaced &afurther apart&r&7, giving players &aclearer visibility&r."
		""
		"&7You can also find some unique plants here: &#7FCC7FMirage Grass&r&7, &#FF69B4Swamp Rose&r&7, &#9370DBFan Purple Flower&r&7, &#7FCC7FMirage Fern&r&7, and more."
	]
	quest.0DDD36DA6EAB60C4.quest_subtitle: "Dark and Sticky"
	quest.0DDD36DA6EAB60C4.title: "Dark Swamp"
	quest.0E08AE1987B72D9C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Drops from explosions caused by the wearer spawn directly at the wearer's position."
		""
		"&7If the wearer is holding an item in the offhand, only drops matching the &#66DDCCoffhand item&7 spawn at the wearer's position; other drops remain in their original locations."
	]
	quest.0E08AE1987B72D9C.quest_subtitle: "Demolition Miner"
	quest.0E31F8D2D8BAC8A5.quest_subtitle: "Right-click to summon a random Eternal Gate nearby (only usable in the End)"
	quest.0E49CEBE282BA883.quest_desc: [
		"&eThe most basic fuel. For early-game players who find it difficult to carry lava in bulk, this fuel is found everywhere."
		"&6Slightly higher consumption and speed, but low power output."
		""
		"⚡ Speed: 0.7x | ♨ Temperature: 1000 | ⏳ Consumption: 0.4"
		""
		"&aTip&r&7: &f♨ &r&7Temperature determines the tier of materials that can be processed, ⚡ Speed affects processing time, and ⏳ Consumption represents fuel longevity."
	]
	quest.0E49CEBE282BA883.quest_subtitle: "Found Everywhere"
	quest.0ED82FFAE99D2480.quest_desc: [
		"&eAn inexpensive chemical product."
		"&6A better regular choice than lava."
		""
		"⚡ Speed: 1.0x | ♨ Temperature: 2000 | ⏳ Consumption: 0.3"
		""
		"&aTip&r&7: &f♨ &r&7Temperature determines the tier of materials that can be processed, ⚡ Speed affects processing time, and ⏳ Consumption represents fuel longevity."
	]
	quest.0ED82FFAE99D2480.quest_subtitle: "Better Fuel"
	quest.0EE6ADB913E3CF80.quest_subtitle: "Provides both armor and minor spell stats—very popular"
	quest.0EF088CAC11B1AA7.quest_subtitle: "Kill Kill Kill"
	quest.0EF9389ADF9236E6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Magic Essence&r"
		"&7Consumables used to increase &bspell power&r&7 and &bspell resistance&r&7. Each has 3 tiers with a usage cap. Obtained via:&r"
		"&7Power: Dropped by &emagical creatures&r&7, upgraded via &6rituals&r&7.&r"
		"&7Resistance: Obtained via &eShrinkers&r&7, upgraded via &6rituals&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.0EF9389ADF9236E6.title: "&6Magic Essence: Resistance&r"
	quest.0F430864AB53FB98.quest_desc: [
		"&7Structures generated in the Overworld from emanations of &#66CCFFStarlight Power&7. They are the only way to first enter the &#66CCFFStarlight Dimension&7..."
		""
		"&7You find a... &#FFD700Gatekeeper&7? He doesn't seem keen on talking; perhaps a fight is in order..."
		""
		"&7The &#FFD700Gatekeeper's&7 attack pattern is completely random, but almost all attacks can be blocked by a &#FFD700shield&7."
		""
		"&7The battle with the &#FFD700Gatekeeper&7 is \"friendly\"—he won't actually kill you (usually), and he also cannot be killed by you."
	]
	quest.0F430864AB53FB98.quest_subtitle: "Find the Starlight Portal"
	quest.0F731D1ED5DD01BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Windswept"
		"&7The wind also brushes the face.&r&cGreater momentum results in stronger knockback received"
		"&7Run with the wind.&r&aSprinting accumulates momentum"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_windswept.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0F731D1ED5DD01BC.quest_subtitle: "One with the Wind"
	quest.0F731D1ED5DD01BC.title: "Pact of the Windswept"
	quest.0FE4EF207A6937B7.quest_desc: [
		"&7Opening chests or breaking workstation blocks in villages while being watched will lower your &#FF6666reputation&7. You can try to block villagers' line of sight with blocks, &mor just kill them all&r."
		""
		"&7Each villager has their own &#66CCFFreputation&7 score. High &#66CCFFreputation&7 gives &#66FF66discounts&7 on trades, while low &#66CCFFreputation&7 will cause villagers to &#FF6666refuse to trade&7."
	]
	quest.0FE4EF207A6937B7.quest_subtitle: "— Pillaging —"
	quest.0FE4EF207A6937B7.title: "Arrival at the Village"
	quest.0FF85A086C90BE5A.title: "Discover the Bitter Cold Prison"
	quest.1031E9949D709475.quest_desc: ["The End Bookshelf is an advanced bookshelf crafted with Ender Dragon's Breath-infused magic. While it doesn't provide extremely high stats, it raises the &aEterna&r cap to 90."]
	quest.1031E9949D709475.quest_subtitle: "Approaching the Endgame of Enchanting"
	quest.1031E9949D709475.title: "Introducing End Power"
	quest.1063B9A89D3EE67C.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When you \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-click\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" while holding it, a copy of the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Cursed Eye\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" flies out from your hand towards the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Bitter Cold Prison\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", and the Cursed Eye in your hand goes into a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The locating function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether or End\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", or in worlds without Bitter Cold Prisons.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.1063B9A89D3EE67C.quest_subtitle: "Bitter Cold Prison"
	quest.11047BEDA6023228.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mystic Orb&r"
		"&7Right-click to obtain the &eHarp&r&7 and &eLost Melody&r&7 trinkets. Obtained via the &6Island Ritual&r&7. To use the Mystic Orb, you must complete the taming progress for all &belemental familiars&r&7 (except the Bard).&r"
		"&5Or just craft it directly via ritual to skip the tedious taming process."
	]
	quest.110C8BBFDBFBA375.quest_subtitle: "&cThis will clear your current difficulty settings. All mob health, attack multipliers, armor, and armor toughness will be multiplied by 8."
	quest.110C8BBFDBFBA375.title: "&c\"Unspeakable Brute Force and Ferocity\""
	quest.11113DE0965217BB.quest_subtitle: "A utility tool for finding Starlight Portals"
	quest.1117830BC3A66701.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#66DDCCEssence Catalyst&7 can consume fuel to accelerate the &#CC99FFessence focusing&7 process of the &#66FF99Essence Crucible&7, and can hold &e1&7 upgrade component."
		""
		"&7The &#66DDCCEssence Catalyst&7 has &e1&7 item slot. A &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect how full this slot is."
		""
		"&7The burn time is half the item's burn time. Items are consumed instantly, but burn time is only consumed while essence focusing is active, consuming &#FFDD55fuel consumption rate&7 * &#FFDD55focusing speed&7 burn time per tick."
		""
		"&7The &#66DDCCEssence Catalyst&7 is &e2&7 blocks tall and can only accelerate one nearby &#66FF99Essence Crucible&7 at a time. Each &#66FF99Essence Crucible&7 can be accelerated by at most &e8&7 catalysts. Effective range is &e4&7 blocks from the bottommost block."
		""
		"&7Acceleration and upgrade effects only apply when active (with burn time). Each active &#66DDCCEssence Catalyst&7 provides +&e50%&7 &#FFDD55focusing speed&7 and +&e5%&7 &#FF6666destabilization risk&7."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/spirit_crucible.png width:200 height:110 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1117830BC3A66701.quest_subtitle: "Heating Up"
	quest.1117830BC3A66701.title: "Crucible Acceleration"
	quest.11789A166C0520B4.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.11BB8D522CF607E6.quest_desc: ["Dropped by the Cockatrice or found in loot. Reduces attack speed and durability, but provides decent offensive bonuses."]
	quest.11BB8D522CF607E6.quest_subtitle: "Why you—haha, ouch!"
	quest.11C363982673E669.quest_desc: [
		"&7I tried various materials for the inscription table, and found runic wood to be the most effective (or not)."
		""
		"&7Scrolls can be inscribed into spellbooks. Inscribed scrolls consume mana when cast and can be reused."
	]
	quest.11C363982673E669.quest_subtitle: "Recording Spells"
	quest.11C4380FD58A7FDA.quest_desc: ["&7Grants additional &#66CCFFarmor&7 when held."]
	quest.11C4380FD58A7FDA.quest_subtitle: "Offense and Defense"
	quest.11DCB93F9E3E9564.quest_desc: ["&7Causes mobs spawned by the spawner to have no behavior (no AI)."]
	quest.11DCB93F9E3E9564.quest_subtitle: "Mass Lobotomy"
	quest.11E9AE8529E6FBF2.quest_subtitle: "Hero of the Village"
	quest.11FE874E44E98ADF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each &#66FF99Essence&7 harvested while equipped grants &e30&7 seconds of the &#CC99FFArcane Echo&7 effect."
		""
		"&7If the &#CC99FFArcane Echo&7 effect is already active, instead extends it by &e7.5&7 seconds (up to &e1&7 hour) and increases the current effect level by &e1&7 (up to &e20&7)."
		""
		"&7The duration granted or extended is multiplied by the &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 attribute."
	]
	quest.11FE874E44E98ADF.quest_subtitle: "Special Effect on Essence Harvest"
	quest.12070A3305878F5D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fluid Tank&r"
		""
		"&6Placement&r"
		"&7When Fluid Tanks are placed in a rectangular cuboid shape with a square base (1×1×n, 2×2×n, or 3×3×n), adjacent tanks will automatically merge into a single structure.&r"
		"&7The maximum height n of the tank structure is 32 blocks. Tanks placed above this height will be considered a new independent structure.&r"
		""
		"&6Storing Fluids&r"
		"&7Can store various fluids, with each block having a capacity of 8 B (8000 mB, or 8 buckets). Fluid input and output must be done via a Mechanical Pump.&r"
		"&7In Creative mode, holding a fluid container (like a bucket) and right-clicking the tank injects fluid directly. In Survival mode, a Fluid Drain and other fluid components must be used for input.&r"
		"&7Holding a Wrench and right-clicking the tank opens or closes its observation window for viewing internal fluid status.&r"
		"&7Fluid Tanks can be detected by Comparators, Item Detectors, and Stockpile Switches. The filter slot of an Item Detector can be marked with a bucket or bottle of the fluid.&r"
		""
		"&6As a Boiler&r"
		"&7When a Steam Whistle or Steam Engine is installed on a Fluid Tank surface, the tank structure becomes a boiler. The observation window disappears, and a pressure gauge appears on each side.&r"
		"&7The boiler provides steam to connected Steam Whistles or Steam Engines.&r"
		""
		"&8The edge of this manuscript page has a crude sketch of a stacked tank with simple gauges. A line below reads: Holds plenty, sees clearly, and when needed, it can roar.&r"
	]
	quest.124EF6C94011C149.quest_desc: [
		"&6Strange Mushroom&r"
		"&7Right-click on a tamed familiar to grant it 1 stack of '&cFury&r&7' (when attacked, has a chance to consume 1 stack to gain the '&cCalm Mind&r&7' status for a few seconds). Max 10 stacks per familiar. Dropped by &eMooshrooms&r&7 and sheared &eSwamp Villagers&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.12C9785ECF565304.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.12C9785ECF565304.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.131FF32C0FF28CA8.quest_desc: [
		"&7Must be found in the corresponding structure. Can also be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		""
		"&7Defeat it—the boiling deathly authority coalesces into a scepter, and that dormant heart is the specimen of time's end extracted from beyond... Defeat it, and it will liberate the &#66CCFFmagical ores&7 of the entire world."
		""
		"&7Defeating the &#FF6666Dead King&7 unlocks the following ores:"
		"&7&#67B1E5Gobber&7"
		"&7&#C9C8E1Zenith&7"
		"&7&#757369Rune Shards&7"
	]
	quest.131FF32C0FF28CA8.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0 — Unlocks Stage 1 upon defeat"
	quest.1350642D5141B3BF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Eye of Seeking&r"
		"&7Used to locate &6Boss&r&7 structures within the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Before use: Hold one of the following specific items in your offhand—this determines which structure the Eye will seek."
		""
		"&6Cursed Garden&r&7 (&cLunar Monstrosity&r&7):"
		"&8Vines, Cave Moss, Starlight Berries&r"
		"&8Red Crystal Roots, Blue Crystal Roots&r"
		"&8Ground Red Crystal Moss, Ground Blue Crystal Moss&r"
		""
		"&6Golem Forge&r&7 (&cStarlight Golem&r&7):"
		"&8Redstone Dust, Golem Steel Ingot, Oxidized Golem Steel Ingot&r"
		""
		"&7The Eye of Seeking functions like an Eye of Ender."
		"&7When right-clicked, it flies toward the &6Boss&r&7 structure, hovers in the air, and then drops as an item after some time."
		"&7Similarly, the Eye has a chance to &cbreak&r&7 while hovering (consumed without return)."
	]
	quest.1350642D5141B3BF.quest_subtitle: "Guidance of Starlight"
	quest.13AFD3688361872A.quest_desc: [
		"# &aGame Modifications &r"
		""
		"### &eIce and Fire Adjustments &r"
		"&7- &fPixies no longer steal player items&a—safe to keep around &r"
		""
		"### &#FFBB1AKeep Inventory Adjustments &r"
		"&7- &fIf Keep Inventory is off, respawning no longer restores you to full status—death keeps hotbar items and equipped gear&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"### &#FF9F9AItem Tooltip Adjustments &r"
		"&7- &fIf item tooltips are too long, scroll with the mouse wheel to browse &r"
		""
		"### &#FF91EESign Adjustments &r"
		"&7- &fSigns placed on blocks like chests can be modified while sneaking—clicking normally passes through to the container &r"
		""
		"### &#C9FF74Entity Cleanup System &r"
		"&7- Config path: &9kubejs/server_scripts/entity_clean.js &r"
		"&7- &fThe modpack includes an &6auto-cleanup system (disabled by default)&f—configure in this file: &r"
		"  &7▪ &fCleanup rules &r"
		"  &7▪ &fToggle state &r"
		"&7- &fFor manual cleanup, use command: &b/rf entityclean &r"
	]
	quest.13AFD3688361872A.quest_subtitle: "Gameplay Experience Modifications"
	quest.13AFD3688361872A.title: "Some Changes"
	quest.13C22895EB17EE88.quest_desc: [
		"&6Filler&r"
		""
		"&7A device specifically designed for \"filling\" operations, capable of the following:&r"
		"&7Filling containers (such as buckets and glass bottles) with fluid, effective for most mod fluids; &r"
		"&7Executing special filling recipes from the Create mod (e.g., making Wet Grass Blocks, Blaze Cakes, etc.).&r"
		""
		"&6Requirements&r"
		"&7Fluid must be input into the Filler via fluid components like Fluid Pipes—manual bucket pouring is not supported.&r"
		"&7Can process items on a Belt or Depot below. When a processable item enters its working range, it will play a filling animation and consume the corresponding amount of fluid. Each filling operation takes 21 game ticks (1.05 seconds).&r"
		"&7When the Filler has no fluid or insufficient fluid, it will stop items on the belt that can be processed until more fluid is supplied.&r"
		""
		"&8Only after it's full can it feed what's below.&r"
	]
	quest.13C542FCBB189AEA.quest_subtitle: "Nameless Traveler"
	quest.13CCBB1FAF6834F4.quest_desc: [
		"There are two types of obelisks with different functions."
		"&6Runic Wood Obelisk"
		""
		"&7When placed near a &#CC99FFEssence Altar&7 (within &e4&7 blocks horizontally and &e3&7 blocks vertically), each &#FFAA33Runic Wood Obelisk&7 increases &#CC99FFessence infusion&7 speed by &e25%&7. Multiple altars can be accelerated simultaneously, with up to &e4&7 obelisks per altar."
		""
		"&7This block is &e2&7 blocks tall; only the lower half provides acceleration."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Essence infusion grows increasingly necessary and tedious. Even making a batch of Spirit Ash takes several minutes."
		""
		"&7The acceleration method lies in &6Hallowed Gold&r&7. Place up to four obelisks made from it around the altar to speed up the process by &aa quarter&r&7 each."
		""
		"&7A technique that significantly speeds up essence infusion—true to the philosophy that \"fast is good.\""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Brilliance Obelisk"
		""
		"&7When placed, each &#66DDCCBrilliance Obelisk&7 provides &e5&7 enchanting levels (bookshelves provide &e1&7). Only &e3&7 obelisks are needed around an enchanting table for &e30&7-level enchants."
		"&7This block is &e2&7 blocks tall; only the lower half provides enchanting levels."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Unlike the &#FFAA33Runic Wood Obelisk&7, the &#66DDCCBrilliance Obelisk&7 cannot accelerate &#CC99FFessence infusion&7."
		""
		"&7Though not useful for infusion, the obelisk's structure can be repurposed."
		""
		"&7Replace Hallowed Gold with &eBrilliance&r&7, and the obelisk harmonizes with enchanting intellect, granting immense enchanting power."
		"&7One such obelisk equals &bfive bookshelves&r&7."
	]
	quest.13CCBB1FAF6834F4.quest_subtitle: "Obelisk"
	quest.13CCBB1FAF6834F4.title: "Altar Acceleration"
	quest.13CDF0A883DC5AE7.quest_desc: ["Eternal Gates will naturally generate in the End."]
	quest.13CDF0A883DC5AE7.quest_subtitle: "The End Seems Unstable"
	quest.13CDF0A883DC5AE7.title: "Journey to the End"
	quest.13DF171E70CF449D.quest_desc: [
		"&oBy wind, by water, or by raw muscle power—at any rate, it turned."
		"&r"
		"Attach gears, let them spin and clash, transfer stress, play the symphony—or so the manuscript says."
		""
		"All my questions can be answered by holding &6[W] to Ponder&r. I believe the path ahead is clear."
		""
		"&8But a windmill made of wool can spin even without wind—is that also the engineer's wisdom?&r"
	]
	quest.13DF171E70CF449D.quest_subtitle: "And Then the Gears Started Turning..."
	quest.13DF171E70CF449D.title: "First Note of the Gears"
	quest.13FB94D18517171F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Basin&r"
		""
		"&7It is the most accommodating vessel in the engineer's workshop, patiently holding various items and fluids, waiting for them to transform according to the prescribed recipe.&r"
		""
		"&6Internal Order&r"
		"&7The Basin has 18 item slots: the first 9 are for input materials, and the last 9 are for finished products. Each item type can stack up to 64.&r"
		"&7It also has 4 fluid slots, each capable of holding &c1000 mB&7, with a total fluid capacity of &c4000 mB&7. No single fluid exceeds the 1000 mB limit.&r"
		"&7Items and fluids coexist peacefully without interfering. Even lava and water can coexist within the Basin without interacting.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Rules of Input and Output&r"
		"&7All six sides can accept or output items, but any automated input can only deliver &c1 to 16&7 items at a time. An exception is items that enter as dropped items, which can fill a stack of 64.&r"
		"&7Mechanical Arms and Brass Funnels are also limited to 16 items per input, and Brass Funnels cannot be set to a specific quantity.&r"
		"&7Output is more generous: Andesite Funnels output 1 item at a time, while Brass Funnels and Mechanical Arms can be configured to output 1 to 64 items. Belts and Fluid Drains can also serve as inputs, allowing items to slide in from the edge.&r"
		"&7Fluids must be transferred via Mechanical Pumps or pipes connected to them. Pumping in prioritizes filling the input slots; pumping out prioritizes extracting from the output slots. If the output slot is empty and space is available, it will extract from the input slot—be careful to avoid recipe confusion.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Filtering and Routing&r"
		"&7The Basin has a filter slot on the side. Inserting a single item, a &eFilter&7, or an &eAttribute Filter&7 specifies that it will only produce the marked product (fluids can be marked with bottled samples).&r"
		"&7If the side is unobstructed and there is an open container diagonally below, the Basin will automatically create an &eoutput spout&7 to attempt to deliver the product. This spout has a hidden output slot—if an item is in it, the Basin will stop working, a common cause of production line jams.&r"
		"&7The spout holds only one recipe output at a time. If a recipe produces multiple items, the first will go to the spout slot, and the rest to the Basin's output slots. A &eWrench&7 can be used to adjust or close the spout. The spout will not reappear unless the block below is updated.&r"
		"&7Containers recognized for automatic output include: Basin, Depot, Belt, Funnel, Crushing Wheel, and most Create components, but not vanilla hoppers.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Recipe Processing Order&r"
		"&7When working with &eMechanical Press&7 or &eMechanical Mixer&7, the Basin processes recipes in the following order:&r"
		"&7If there's a processable recipe in the input slots: first process pure item recipes, then item-fluid mixed recipes, and finally pure fluid recipes.&r"
		"&7If there's no recipe in the input slots: prioritize recipes from all item slots, then item-fluid mixed recipes, and finally pure fluid recipes.&r"
		""
		"&7Other details: Identical items will try to stack into existing slots rather than taking new ones. If all 9 output slots are full, all processing stops.&r"
		""
		"&8There's a dark stain on the edge of the page, as if someone pressed a greasy thumb here.&r"
	]
	quest.13FB94D18517171F.quest_subtitle: "A small square container, yet the heart of the entire factory"
	quest.142C80D05D6B1FDC.quest_subtitle: "Clear all difficulty settings you have adjusted"
	quest.143A6CDB76F7A3DC.quest_desc: [
		"Spawns rarely in underground caves."
		""
		"Can also be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.143A6CDB76F7A3DC.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.1444AD82BC8B46CF.quest_desc: [
		"&7When the wearer attacks a creature with health above &e98.75%&7, generates &e2&7 &#88DDFFSoul Voids&7 that fly toward the wearer like &#66FF99Essence&7. Harvesting them triggers essence harvest effects (without generating &#66FF99Essence&7). This can trigger at most once every &e5&7 seconds."
		""
		"&7If the target is a player, &e5&7 &#88DDFFSoul Voids&7 are generated instead."
	]
	quest.1444AD82BC8B46CF.quest_subtitle: "Faster Buff Acquisition"
	quest.1448882981E09E31.quest_desc: ["&7More enemies mean more damage. With high attack stats, clearing efficiency scales with enemy density—a powerful tool for horde situations."]
	quest.1448882981E09E31.quest_subtitle: "Celestial Power"
	quest.147DBFF8D9EC5476.quest_desc: ["&7Can pre-load &#FFD700arrows&7 for later firing."]
	quest.147DBFF8D9EC5476.quest_subtitle: "Illager's Favorite"
	quest.14D4101B90CF5417.quest_subtitle: "Time for a break, right?"
	quest.14D4101B90CF5417.title: "One Hour Played"
	quest.14F646FF9C81DCA0.quest_desc: [
		"&6Venomous Spider Fang&r"
		"&7Used to craft &cToxic Reagent&r&7 and cure the &cPlague Doctor&r&7 familiar. Dropped by &cCave Spiders&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.14F646FF9C81DCA0.quest_subtitle: "Deadly Poison"
	quest.153B8C23F5FF23C5.quest_desc: ["Extends the wireless access point's transmission range to infinite blocks and allows cross-dimensional transmission."]
	quest.153B8C23F5FF23C5.quest_subtitle: "Dimensional Transmission"
	quest.15420045F7ABF5AD.quest_desc: [
		"Through &binfusion&r upgrades, the Nether Bookshelf gains even greater magical power, providing higher &aEterna&r and &4Quanta&r."
		"&l(Recommended Bookshelf)&r"
	]
	quest.15420045F7ABF5AD.quest_subtitle: "Better Quanta and Eterna"
	quest.15420045F7ABF5AD.title: "Magical Chaotic Enhancement"
	quest.159E4C31CF4AB181.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of the Undiscerned Maw&r"
		""
		"&7The consumed essence comes from malice, and thus craves dissolution.&r"
		"&7-Overuse gradually reduces &call healing&r received&r"
		""
		"&7Etched into the malevolent soul-reaper's runes.&r"
		"&7-&6Malevolent Criticals&r&7 &8consume&r&7 the affected creature's &8life essence&r"
		"&7-The consumed essence &aheals&r&7 you based on damage dealt&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_the_undiscerned_maw.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.159E4C31CF4AB181.quest_subtitle: "Devour All Things"
	quest.159E4C31CF4AB181.title: "Oath of the Undiscerned Maw"
	quest.15DC053FF5BA0E9B.quest_subtitle: "Provides both armor and minor spell stats—very popular"
	quest.15DDBCE29F4CEB4B.quest_subtitle: "Crafting material, primarily used for making advanced machinery and smart components."
	quest.1618DB9594EF15C3.quest_subtitle: "So Lonely at the Top"
	quest.161C42E6B708C7DA.quest_subtitle: "Update 1.1 here... misery"
	quest.1633AD29D81FB414.quest_desc: [
		"&aEterna&7 is slightly higher than vanilla bookshelves... Different levels of Eterna blocks placed around an enchanting table stack from lowest to highest. For example, 15 vanilla bookshelves provide 30 Eterna. Adding ten Amethyst blocks then adds +10 Eterna, reaching 40. This applies to other bookshelves as well."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7In the mines, a magical geode catches your eye."
		"&7You discover a thriving crystal cluster. It emanates faint yet potent magical power—better than your current bookshelves. You carefully bring it back and place it near your enchanting table. The table's magical power grows slightly, and its instability decreases a bit. But this small amount is still too little—you wonder if there is a more powerful version."
	]
	quest.1633AD29D81FB414.quest_subtitle: "Mystical Crystal"
	quest.1633AD29D81FB414.title: "Nature's Magic Stabilizer"
	quest.1669DD338D104D3F.quest_desc: ["I can't believe my humble little pack actually attracted an art teacher! They even helped with rendering work—truly amazing..."]
	quest.1669DD338D104D3F.quest_subtitle: "Art + Some Code"
	quest.1675C48578D2D979.quest_desc: ["&7&#FF6666Wither Skeleton Skulls&7 and &#FF6666Skeleton Skulls&7 now have crafting recipes. If you need to fight the &#FF6666Wither&7 but don't have any skulls, you can craft them instead of hunting &#FF6666Wither Skeletons&7 endlessly..."]
	quest.1675C48578D2D979.quest_subtitle: "Doo Doo Da Doo Da"
	quest.1684A811A37D8C86.quest_desc: ["Some materials listed in Tier 2 don't necessarily require killing the Dead King to obtain—they're just rated at T2 value."]
	quest.1684A811A37D8C86.quest_subtitle: "Before Killing the Dead King"
	quest.16FD71D5EBCE3C6A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Train Controls&r"
		""
		"&7This is the \"helm\" of the train structure, allowing the driver—or any other creature—to control the entire mechanical construct's movement.&r"
		""
		"&6Installation&r"
		"&7Each train structure must have at least one set of Train Controls, firmly glued to the structure during assembly.&r"
		"&7To allow a creature to drive, place a &eSeat&7 or &eBlaze Burner&7 directly in front of the controls.&r"
		"&7For bidirectional travel, install Train Controls at both ends of the structure.&r"
		""
		"&6Control Methods&r"
		"&7After assembly, two levers will appear on the controls. Right-click to enter control mode.&r"
		"&7Use movement keys (WASD) to control the train's speed. The speed bar in the interface shows the current speed. It has 18 segments divided into five phases.&r"
		"&7Speed is reduced automatically when turning.&r"
		"&7Coal can be stored on the train to increase speed, consumed over time.&r"
		"&7Scroll the mouse wheel to adjust the speed limit, shown by a brass slider.&r"
		"&7The arrow above the speed bar indicates the train's direction relative to your view.&r"
		"&7If the train has a whistle, pressing the Sprint key (default Ctrl) sounds it.&r"
		""
		"&8The corner of this page is folded, with a crude charcoal sketch of the controls and a scribble: Grip tight, watch the track, and don't forget the coal.&r"
	]
	quest.1739A8FBB4773234.quest_desc: ["Some metals do not have corresponding blocks and thus cannot be cast into blocks."]
	quest.1739A8FBB4773234.quest_subtitle: "Fluid to Block Conversion"
	quest.17695E30CD9EB522.quest_subtitle: "Nobody died over 100 times just to get this quest reward, right?"
	quest.178BC08D4F2D3809.quest_desc: ["&7\"Ponder\" is a strong control effect. Though the material has some downsides, as a means to boost magic damage, it's still cost-effective—control and damage in one."]
	quest.178BC08D4F2D3809.quest_subtitle: "1+1=?"
	quest.17B9D8741CF45918.quest_desc: [
		"&7During my research into enchanting, I discovered some peculiar bookshelves."
		""
		"&7Stone Bookshelves and Melon Bookshelves can suppress unwanted &5Arcana&7 and &cQuanta&7, creating conditions for &einfusion&7."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The Stone Bookshelf was created in the same accident. Unlike the unremarkable Deepslate Bookshelf, this more common stone version exhibits a rejection of enchantment. Perhaps due to Andesite's entanglement with machinery, this bookshelf actually reduces &aEterna&7 and &5Arcana&7—technology's certainty denies magic's mystery, even in a world where magic exists."
		""
		"&7The Melon Bookshelf is a ridiculous accident. While harvesting melons, I temporarily piled them on a bookshelf. When I returned to move them to storage, I noticed the bookshelf's enchanting power had been suppressed. Continuing my research, I eventually had the idea to gild a melon and turn it into a bookshelf. Perhaps due to the heat—or maybe because demons were bribed by watermelon—this bookshelf reduces &aEterna&7 while also suppressing the effects of &cQuanta&7. Whether this absurd reasoning holds true, or the demonic power was partially bribed by melons, remains unclear."
	]
	quest.17B9D8741CF45918.quest_subtitle: "Power Suppression"
	quest.17B9D8741CF45918.title: "The Strangest Bookshelves"
	quest.17CD8FFD1387207D.quest_desc: [
		"&7Aside from finding naturally spawned bosses, you can also use Cataclysm's Soul Altar to summon bosses yourself. Check JEI for specific summoning recipes."
		""
		"&7Simply search for the boss name. If a spawn egg named \"&eSummon: ****&7\" exists with the tooltip \"&eSpawns the associated creature immediately when appearing in the world&7\", it means you can manually summon it. Clicking the spawn egg will show the summoning recipe."
		""
		"&cPlease note: As the tooltip states, this is a summoning ritual that will immediately spawn the boss upon completion. Please summon in an open area."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.17CD8FFD1387207D.quest_subtitle: "At Your Age, At This Stage, How Can You Sleep?"
	quest.17CD8FFD1387207D.title: "Repeated Kills"
	quest.17DE5C30E0CA8765.quest_desc: [
		"# &bPerformance Optimization Recommendations &r"
		""
		"### &e Video Settings Suggestions &r"
		"&b▸ &6Render Distance: &r&l8&r"
		"&b▸ &6Max Shadow Distance: &r&l6&r"
		"&b▸ &6Simulation Distance: &r&l6&r"
		"&b▸ &6Vertical Sync: &r&cOff&r"
		"&b▸ &6Max Framerate: &r&aUnlimited&r"
		"&b▸ &6Entity Render Distance: &r&975%&r"
		""
		"&7Leave other settings at default~"
		""
		"### &3Notes &r"
		"&7- Fine-tune values based on your device's performance"
		"&7- If lag occurs, try lowering render distance"
	]
	quest.17DE5C30E0CA8765.quest_subtitle: "Huh? Optimization isn't as good as expected?"
	quest.182289427E06D427.quest_desc: ["&7Light and compact weapon. Slightly lower damage and reach, but offers high &#FFAA33attack speed&7. Hitting targets &66CCFFreduces their invincibility frames&7."]
	quest.182289427E06D427.quest_subtitle: "Small is also cute"
	quest.188CFA97BB5A32C2.quest_desc: ["&7A base trinket that only provides a small amount of &#FF8844armor&7. A necessary prerequisite for crafting its higher-tier variants."]
	quest.188CFA97BB5A32C2.quest_subtitle: "Trinket Base"
	quest.18AC27B34367E1DD.quest_desc: ["&7Mines in a &#FFAA333×3×1&7 area."]
	quest.18AC27B34367E1DD.quest_subtitle: "Tunnel Digger"
	quest.18B62DD6017843BC.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.18B62DD6017843BC.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.18C5ACA6F816EDCB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mini Shield&r"
		"&7Right-click on a tamed familiar to grant it a low chance to &ablock&r&7 attacks. Limited to 1 per familiar. Obtained via &eShrinker&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.18D4FAD08F8837FD.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pandora's Box&r"
		"&7Allows &asummoning/dismissing&r&7 up to 10 familiars at once (crafted).&r"
	]
	quest.18D4FAD08F8837FD.quest_subtitle: "You Opened Pandora's Box..."
	quest.192F6B22F5E521FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7At least now you have a place to sleep..."
		""
		"&7The modpack has changed &#66CCFFPhantom&7 spawning. Not sleeping for a long time no longer spawns &#66CCFFPhantoms&7. Instead, &#FFD700Phantoms will spawn if you sleep continuously&7 as a &#FF6666penalty&7 for skipping the night."
		"&7&mThen if I keep sleeping, they won't spawn, right?&r"
		""
		"&7This change may make naturally spawned &#66CCFFPhantoms&7 rare. If you need their drops, look for structures that contain &#66CCFFPhantom&7 spawners."
	]
	quest.192F6B22F5E521FF.quest_subtitle: "You Can Also Sleep Under the Stars"
	quest.192F6B22F5E521FF.title: "Establish a Base"
	quest.194FFC9454CBCBA2.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Basic Attributes\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Paint\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" is an item used to color equipment parts.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Color Mixing Logic\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When mixing items of multiple colors, the resulting paint color is the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"blend\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\" of the input colors (following paint mixing principles, similar to real-world color theory).\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Coloring Equipment\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Silent Gear equipment can be colored in three ways:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Craft the equipment with paint or dye\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"→\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\"Colors only the main part\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Craft the equipment with a Part Swapper + paint/dye\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"→\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\"Colors the part specified by the Part Swapper\",\"color\":\"aqua\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Craft the part with paint/dye\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"→\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\"Colors the part—equipment made with it inherits the color\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
	]
	quest.194FFC9454CBCBA2.quest_subtitle: "Color Philosopher"
	quest.1954C7719D379871.quest_desc: [
		"&6Shield Component&r"
		""
		"&7Borrowing the multiphase stacking properties of Soul-Stained Steel, the Shield Component has a chance to completely absorb wear on &eRunes&r&7 while slightly stabilizing the &afocusing process&r&7. It does, however, slow focusing speed.&r"
	]
	quest.1954C7719D379871.quest_subtitle: "Face the Storm"
	quest.1A4259700BD803E8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Andesite Funnel&r"
		""
		"&6Funnel and Dropped Items&r"
		"&7When attached to a container, the Andesite Funnel is in output mode by default, pushing items out from its front as dropped items. In input mode, it rapidly absorbs all dropped items in its block space with no speed limit. Use a Wrench to toggle modes.&r"
		"&7In input mode, right-clicking the funnel's front with an item in hand deposits it directly into the connected container.&r"
		"&7Like many designs, a Redstone signal locks the Andesite Funnel, stopping its operation.&r"
		""
		"&7The funnel can be placed above or below a container. When outputting upward, items are launched with inertia. If not collected, they pile up on top of the funnel, enabling &avertical upward transport&r.&r"
		""
		"&6Vertical Orientation&r"
		"&7When the funnel faces directly up or down, it cannot serve as a vertical transport pipe. For pure vertical transport, use Chutes or vanilla hoppers.&r"
		""
		"&6Funnel and Work Block Integration&r"
		"&7When an Andesite Funnel is attached to the side of a block and a specific work block is directly below, it directly exchanges items with that block. Using a Wrench to toggle mode changes its appearance to '&eAndesite Belt Funnel&r'.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Compatible blocks include: &eDepot&r, &eWeighted Ejector&r, &eBelt&r, &eFluid Drain&r, &eMechanical Saw&r (facing up only), &eTrain Station&r.&r"
		""
		"&7Placing an Andesite Funnel on a belt with its opening aligned with the belt's direction puts it in tunnel mode. Input/output is then determined by the belt's transport direction.&r"
		"&7Tunnel-mode funnels are retracted by default; a Wrench extends them. The extended form covers part of the belt below, serving decorative purposes and changing collision.&r"
		""
		"&8A note in the margin: It's flexible, but don't expect it to break fundamental rules.&r"
	]
	quest.1A58667FA2440598.quest_desc: ["&7Preface: This modpack's main focus is on the &#FFD700side quests&7, not the &#FF85CBmain storyline&7. The main quests only serve to &#FF85CBguide your progression&7."]
	quest.1A58667FA2440598.quest_subtitle: "Pack Your Bags"
	quest.1A58667FA2440598.title: "Wilderness Exploration"
	quest.1A8CEE0746A74FC4.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe and conditions."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1A8CEE0746A74FC4.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.1AA4DC70AD282F2B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Impurity Stabilizer&r"
		""
		"&7&8Malevolent essences&r&7 are drawn to weaknesses and the weak, craving slaughter. The Impurity Stabilizer exploits this property, providing significant &apercentage amplification&r&7 to the crucible's weakest attribute at the cost of increased fuel consumption and destabilization risk. This does impose a minor burden on the standard &etuning process&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.1AA4DC70AD282F2B.quest_subtitle: "Strength from Weakness"
	quest.1AA82BAE61749007.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Slaughter&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Slaughter compels the mind toward destruction, increasing the wearer's &escythe proficiency&r&7 against injured targets. It seems to take effect on creatures at or below half health, increasing scythe damage by approximately two-fifths.&r"
	]
	quest.1AA82BAE61749007.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Urges Destruction"
	quest.1AB5165BCAD5820E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Burning&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Burning compels the mind to share its radiance with everything around it, regardless of consequence; it doubles the &efire damage&r&7 dealt by the wearer.&r"
	]
	quest.1AB5165BCAD5820E.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Urges Burning"
	quest.1ACA39ABEB90A9F5.quest_desc: ["&7Right-click to throw a &#66CCFFboomerang&7 at enemies. Thankfully, it doesn't hit you."]
	quest.1ACA39ABEB90A9F5.quest_subtitle: "Watch Your Eyes!"
	quest.1AF5C4332908323D.quest_desc: ["&7Top-tier traits and stats. Offers solid base values and good damage scaling. Obtained after defeating Skeletron. A key component in any build, and synergizes well with Gobber Ingots."]
	quest.1AF5C4332908323D.quest_subtitle: "May Your Journey Be Filled with Curses and Blessings"
	quest.1B66EC1641E0B30A.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.1B66EC1641E0B30A.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.1B819E833413B729.title: "Mysterious Ghoul"
	quest.1BD8D56B55550058.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Reaper"
		"&7Breaking the bond leads to &cdifficulty&r&7.&r&cWeapons not permitted by the geas deal nine-tenths less damage&r&cWeapons not permitted by the geas rapidly deteriorate when used"
		"&7The soul signs a pact with the scythe, arcane chains binding them closely.&r&aScythe attacks have a chance to trigger chain slashes"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_reaper.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1BD8D56B55550058.quest_subtitle: "Mastery of the Scythe Blade"
	quest.1BD8D56B55550058.title: "Pact of the Reaper"
	quest.1BF4B358E8923423.quest_desc: [
		"&#66DDFFSanity &7is a &#FFAA00core stat&7 for players in the game."
		""
		"&#66DDFFSanity &7is displayed as a UI element in the top-left corner of the screen."
		""
		"&#66DDFFSanity &7has a range of &#FFAA00-45&7 to &#FFAA00+45&7."
		""
		"&7A unit's initial &#66DDFFSanity &7is &f0&7 by default."
		""
		"&#66DDFFSanity &7changes under various conditions. Generally, &#66DD88favorable states&7 increase &#66DDFFSanity&7, while &#FF6644unfavorable states&7 decrease it."
		""
		"&7When a unit with a sanity bar reaches &#FF4444-45&7 &#66DDFFSanity&7, there is a &#FF7733&lhigh chance&7 of entering a &#FF6644Panic state&7, and a &#44DDFFsmall chance&7 of entering a &#CC77FFErosion state&7 (see subsequent quests for details on Erosion)."
	]
	quest.1BF4B358E8923423.quest_subtitle: "&zBasic Understanding"
	quest.1BF4B358E8923423.title: "Sanity"
	quest.1BF526B37EC8A965.quest_desc: ["&7Sacrifices attack speed for a substantial damage boost."]
	quest.1BF526B37EC8A965.quest_subtitle: "Power at a Cost"
	quest.1C22E01E9591DC36.quest_subtitle: "N E V E R  C O M E  B A C K  E M P T Y"
	quest.1C22E01E9591DC36.title: "Caught 10 Fish"
	quest.1CBEB689E8C2B677.quest_desc: [
		"&6Study: Void Slate"
		"&7After passing through the &dWeeping Well&r&7, the &bSoul Stone&r&7 transformed into what I call \"&8Void Slate&r&7.\" Though its physical properties resemble the Soul Stone, it seems to lack a soul... yet its interaction with arcane energy remains identical to that of the Soul Stone."
		"&7"
		"&7Perhaps this is the Soul Stone's state before gaining &dsoul energy&r&7? I cannot determine its interaction pattern with souls, nor can I transfer properties like I did with &6Soul-Stained Steel&r&7. My only theory is that a complete absence of arcane energy—down to the last trace—somehow has its own unique arcane energy. What might this energy be?"
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Re-examining: Void Slate"
		"&7The complete absence of arcane energy also has its use. The nature of Void Slate should now be clear—a Soul Stone attuned to &8Void&r&7 rather than arcane energy."
		"&7"
		"&7It may still be a precursor to the Soul Stone, but the two might be interconnected in other ways... Its outward physical properties match the Soul Stone. The only difference comes from the material's interaction with different entities."
	]
	quest.1CBEB689E8C2B677.quest_subtitle: "Blank Slate, Perhaps a Precursor"
	quest.1CD6A8BB98046D3C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Small upgrades that provide various bonuses to your aircraft. You can use them to compensate for a specific plane's weaknesses or enhance its strengths."
		""
		"&7It's worth noting that the Enhanced Propeller's reduced drag significantly improves acceleration."
	]
	quest.1CDBC70DB8D56271.quest_desc: [
		"&7Once you've made some progress in research, it's time to explore other dimensions. Proper protection can reduce the risk of sudden death. It's recommended to use tools like the &#66DDCCDisassembly Lexicon&7 or &#66DDCCArmor Lexicon&7 to stack protections. Apply &#FFAA33Protection IV&7 or &#FFAA33Protection V&7 to your armor before setting out. &#66CCFFProtection enchantments&7 still follow vanilla calculations, so four pieces of &#FFAA33Protection V&7 will reach the damage reduction cap."
		""
		"&7If you use a full set of &#66DDCCHardened Steel Armor&7, you can also easily reach the armor damage reduction cap. However, it's still recommended to try other materials with special traits for better protection."
	]
	quest.1CDBC70DB8D56271.title: "Rest... Then Set Out Again"
	quest.1CE41ACD131E060B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starfire&r"
		"&7Can upgrade &eThermal Springstone equipment&r&7 into stronger &6Starfire equipment&r&7. The upgrade process requires a &bSmithing Template (Starfire Upgrade)&r."
		""
		"&7Starfire can also be used in a Smithing Table as a &dtrim color&r for armor trimming templates."
		""
		"&7Right-click to &athrow&r&7 Starfire. When it hits a creature or block, it explodes, applying &c10 seconds of Starfire I&r&7 to all creatures within &b3 blocks&r&7."
		"&7Thrown Starfire &cdoes not deal attack damage&r when hitting a creature."
		""
		"&7Throwing Starfire at &8Sand&r&7 or &8Dusk Sand&r&7 converts the hit block into &eCoarse Glass&r."
		"&7Refined &eGlass&r&7 made from Coarse Glass is used to craft another type of &6tier-2 equipment&r&7."
		""
		"&7Right-clicking a &8Torreya Campfire&r&7 with Starfire converts its flame to a brighter red."
		"&7The upgraded campfire continuously applies &c4 seconds of Starfire I&r&7 to non-ally entities within &b10 blocks&r&7."
		"&7The campfire's original &aregeneration effect&r&7 is retained after the upgrade."
		"&7Even if the campfire is extinguished, these enhanced effects &areapply&r&7 when relit."
	]
	quest.1CE41ACD131E060B.quest_subtitle: "Crystal Flame"
	quest.1D08BC5C6C98F4D7.quest_desc: ["&7You'd better not have done it on purpose."]
	quest.1D08BC5C6C98F4D7.quest_subtitle: "Legendary Hero Who Triggered 5 Raids?!?"
	quest.1D30682DE64D68A1.quest_desc: ["&7Used to regulate &#CC99FFMalum's&7 &#FF8844Redstone devices&7."]
	quest.1D30682DE64D68A1.quest_subtitle: "Device Conditions"
	quest.1D7C2FBD7B33CA7A.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1D7C2FBD7B33CA7A.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.1DBA0BF33C43D227.quest_desc: ["Defeat the Ender Dragon to obtain high-tier spell materials."]
	quest.1DBA0BF33C43D227.quest_subtitle: "You're a Dragon Too, Huh"
	quest.1DC249D36D54E164.quest_desc: [
		"&7Passive Abilities"
		""
		"&7Damage Limit:"
		"&7In the broken state, the Starlight Golem cannot take more than &#FFAA332/3&7 of its max health in a single instance of damage."
		""
		"&7Invincibility (Phase 1 only): The Starlight Golem is &#FF6666immune to all damage&7 unless in the broken state."
		""
		"&7Energy (Phase 1 only):"
		"&7The Starlight Golem can hold up to &#FFAA33100&7 energy;"
		"&7Each attack consumes some energy. Even if remaining energy is insufficient, the golem can still use the attack (except at 0 energy);"
		"&7Energy cannot go negative. At 0, the golem immediately enters a charging state;"
		"&7Each time a Cryo Tube is thrown at the golem, its energy decreases by &#FF6666-3&7."
		""
		"&7Energy Block Charging (Charging State)"
		"&7The Starlight Golem always starts in the charging state;"
		"&7It enters the charging state every &#FFAA3390 seconds&7 thereafter;"
		"&7During charging, it cannot attack, and four surrounding energy blocks continuously charge it;"
		"&7During charging, it regenerates &#66FF660.4&7 health per second;"
		"&7After charging, the golem regains &#FFAA33100&7 energy;"
		"&7Players must (right-click / shoot projectiles) &#FF6666extinguish&7 all energy blocks charging the golem; otherwise, it remains invincible;"
		"&7Once all are extinguished: the golem enters the broken state."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Broken State"
		"&7Occurs simultaneously with the charging state. After entering the broken state, the golem is &#FF6666no longer immune&7 to damage until the charging state ends;"
		"&7After taking up to &#FFAA337&7 instances of damage, the golem forcibly ends both charging and broken states, resuming attacks;"
		"&7The broken state lasts at most &#FFAA3360 seconds&7;"
		"&7If the golem enters Phase 2, the current charging and broken states are forcibly ended."
		""
		"&7Phase 2"
		"&7When the golem's remaining health is ≤&#FFAA3320%&7:"
		"&7It loses its invincibility passive and no longer switches between charging and broken states;"
		"&7From this point, players can attack the golem normally;"
		"&7In this phase, the golem's body constantly trembles and sparks, occasionally flashing red (visual only—no self-damage)."
	]
	quest.1DC249D36D54E164.quest_subtitle: "Exquisite Creation"
	quest.1DCC3ACDD6DBDB35.quest_desc: ["Mined from Deepslate in the Overworld. A lava-proof lily pad."]
	quest.1DCC3ACDD6DBDB35.quest_subtitle: "Walking on Lava"
	quest.1DDF2D0C0D0D8DDA.quest_desc: ["&7A flying fortress. Can slowly fly and use mounted weapons to strafe below. Due to its massive size, slow speed, and mediocre weaponry, it's mentioned here for completeness but not recommended for actual use."]
	quest.1DEBD3A3C7F6C452.quest_subtitle: "Increases the extra strength of effects triggered by essence harvesting"
	quest.1DFDD58AC91C2543.quest_desc: [
		"&7Prioritizes consuming &7Shotgun Shells&7 from the pack. Applicable bullet types: &7Shotgun Shells&7, &7High-Explosive Shells&7, &7Wraith Shells&7. Blank rounds will not be applied."
		""
		"&7If there are no bullets in the pack, &7Durability&7 will be consumed based on the charge level instead."
	]
	quest.1DFDD58AC91C2543.quest_subtitle: "I gave you a chance and you wasted it."
	quest.1E1304B2BD351410.quest_desc: ["&7A classic combination that stands the test of time. Tanks paired with an Experience Pump can store experience, ensuring you don't lose it even on death. The amount of experience a tank can store scales with the number of stack upgrades installed. With enough upgrades, you can store massive amounts of experience for a rainy day."]
	quest.1E1304B2BD351410.quest_subtitle: "Liquid Experience"
	quest.1E2790853AD3FE5E.quest_desc: ["&7Allows you to set a void mode to discard unwanted junk items from your inventory. This is very useful for daily mob farming and mining, but be careful not to void items you actually need."]
	quest.1E2790853AD3FE5E.quest_subtitle: "It's Called Void, But It's Really a Trash Can"
	quest.1E5FC0856DAA4E01.quest_subtitle: "Centurion"
	quest.1E5FC0856DAA4E01.title: "Kill Champion Creatures x100"
	quest.1EA661BBFE32AD97.quest_desc: ["&7Faster &#FFAA33attack speed&7 than a sword, slightly lower damage, but &#66CCFFgreater reach&7."]
	quest.1EA661BBFE32AD97.quest_subtitle: "Agile Blade"
	quest.1EBAE1ABF6C57762.quest_desc: [
		"&7Indeed, permanent geases are &8heavy burdens&r&7. While powerful, their &cnegative effects&r&7 are ever-present."
		"&7Geases can be revoked at a &6Brazier&r&7, allowing you to choose the price you pay."
		""
		"&7To revoke a geas, prepare the required materials at the Brazier and light it with &5Profane Flame&r&7."
		"&7This &crevokes&r&7 rather than declares a geas. The process is otherwise identical; revoking a simple soul's geas also requires weakening it before lighting."
	]
	quest.1EBAE1ABF6C57762.quest_subtitle: "The Price Is Too High"
	quest.1EBAE1ABF6C57762.title: "Revoking Geas"
	quest.1EBDC6E060A25C43.quest_desc: [
		"&6Memory Fragments&r"
		"&7Remnants of a familiar's forgotten past. They guide you to places the familiar considers &bhome&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.1EC459CAACF854F3.quest_desc: [
		"&c&lNote:"
		"&eThis list may become outdated without maintenance, but &aCod&f will do his best to keep it up to date!"
		""
		"&6&lTip:"
		"&7- &fThe modpack has adjusted &eJEI &f(though it's &eEMI&f) to let you search for &dtraits&f in &bEMI&f and find all items with that trait."
		""
		"Example:"
		"%+trait_name"
		"&eSearches for all items with that trait&r"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[\"And &+part_name\"]} "
		"&eSearches for all materials usable for that part&r"
		""
		"&7- &fPress &e&lU &f(default) on a material to view its &eJEI &fpage."
		""
		"&7- &fPress &e&lShift + Ctrl &fon a material/weapon to view its &dtraits&f directly."
	]
	quest.1EC459CAACF854F3.quest_subtitle: "View All Recommended Materials, Stats, and Values Here"
	quest.1EC459CAACF854F3.title: "Material Recommendations"
	quest.1F0DFA4EF202BD42.quest_desc: [
		"&7Obtained through crafting."
		"&7&#FFD700Netherite Plating&7 allows players to mass-produce \"knockoffs\" like &#66DDCCNetherite Plated Blocks&7 and their variants for building and decoration."
		"&7When dropped as items, they &#FF6666are not destroyed by fire/lava&7."
	]
	quest.1F0DFA4EF202BD42.quest_subtitle: "Gold Plating? No, Netherite Plating Is the New Trend!"
	quest.1F1102772124A040.quest_desc: ["&7Has a trait that provides bonus damage based on &#FFAA33experience level&7. Though its base stats are slightly lower, the trait more than makes up for it."]
	quest.1F1102772124A040.quest_subtitle: "Never Enough!"
	quest.1F113AE0032F16AA.quest_desc: ["&7Auto-pickup activated. Can sometimes save items from despawning, as it picks them up very quickly. It can also help you find items that may have dropped nearby but are hard to locate."]
	quest.1F113AE0032F16AA.quest_subtitle: "Oops, Forgot to Turn Off Auto-Pickup"
	quest.1F38C534465F33BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fluid Pipe&r"
		""
		"&6Usage&r"
		""
		"&6Transporting Fluids&r"
		"&7A &eMechanical Pump&r&7 provides pressure (power) to transport fluids. By default, a single pump can push fluid &c16 blocks&r&7, requiring another pump beyond that distance.&r"
		"&7Pipes themselves have no speed limit—flow rate depends on the pump's extraction speed.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7If a pipe opening is exposed, it consumes 1000 mB of fluid to generate a fluid block at the opening (if the fluid has a block form; otherwise, it shows a leak effect consuming 1 mB/t). Conversely, it can extract fluid from adjacent sources.&r"
		"&7Extracting from an infinite water source doesn't deplete it—the source block alternates between water and flowing water. If extraction exceeds 200 mB/t (e.g., two pumps at 200 RPM), the source can't keep up, limiting actual extraction speed regardless of pump RPM (observable via Wrench window).&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7For multiple pumps extracting from infinite water, ensure each source block is adjacent to at least two untouched water sources to prevent depletion or speed fluctuations.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Pipes cannot extract water with kelp in it. Breaking the kelp won't restore extraction unless the pipe system is updated (e.g., changing block state, adjusting pump speed, or repositioning fluid at the pipe opening). Water from other waterlogged blocks can be extracted normally.&r"
		"&7Fluid Pipes can extract water and lava from &eCauldrons&r.&r"
		"&7Fluid Pipes can extract &eHoney&r from full &eBee Nests&r or &eBeehives&r, unlocking [Automated Apiary].&r"
		"&7Pipes have no internal buffer. If a pipe with flowing fluid is cut (broken or valve closed), the fluid disappears due to flow reset. Sudden source changes cause the same effect.&r"
		""
		"&6Interaction with Entities&r"
		"&7If the leaking fluid is a potion, it applies its effect to creatures in front; milk removes effects.&r"
		"&7Water particles extinguish fires on entities and blocks; lava particles ignite entities.&r"
		"&7Regardless of the amount sprayed, the entity always receives the full effect—1 mB of potion gives the full duration.&r"
		""
		"&6Opening the Observation Window&r"
		"&7Use a Wrench to open a window on the pipe to observe flowing fluid. A windowed pipe cannot bend. Right-click again to close.&r"
		""
		"&6Encasing&r"
		"&7Right-click with a &eCopper Casing&r to encase the pipe. The casing is not consumed. Encasing locks the pipe's opening directions, preventing automatic connections to newly placed pipes.&r"
		""
		"&6Fluid Reactions Inside Pipes&r"
		"&7When two fluids meet in a pipe, the pipe breaks and may generate a block depending on the fluids (specific reactions omitted).&r"
	]
	quest.1F71B459B51B8E4B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Complex Component&r"
		""
		"&7The Complex Component draws power from its chaotic, fractal-like complexity, as its name suggests. When installed, fuel dependence increases and focusing speed decreases, but the &eCrucible&r&7 may produce double output in a single &6focusing cycle&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.1F71B459B51B8E4B.quest_subtitle: "Abundance and Prosperity"
	quest.1F9846B94E48DEDF.quest_desc: ["&7Using the light of End Rods, I reinforced the End Bookshelf, enhancing its enchanting stats. However, the power of End Rods is not strong enough to reach the pinnacle of enchanting power."]
	quest.1F9846B94E48DEDF.quest_subtitle: "Reinforced End Bookshelf"
	quest.1F9846B94E48DEDF.title: "Ender Power Reborn"
	quest.1FB3D1FAE9A88C39.quest_desc: [
		"&6Engineer's Notebook&r"
		"&7During my travels, I happened upon a notebook—seemingly the legacy of an engineer.&r"
		"&7According to the manuscript, mastering this craft would allow me to become an engineer myself. That means I could build my own production lines, generate endless resources, unlock new crafting methods, and extract materials from ores that a furnace cannot.&r"
		""
		"&7However, this path is not essential to my journey. Becoming an engineer does little to improve my combat abilities. The original owner of this manuscript couldn't even build a malfunctioning robot for battle. The benefits here are more of a luxury than a necessity.&r"
		""
		"&7If you're interested, perhaps it's worth exploring. It all seems to start with a cheap material called &6Andesite Alloy&7.&r"
		""
		"(Side note: In version 0.8 and above, the modpack re-added ScalableLux for optimization. When used with Vanillin, it may cause dynamic structures to cast shadows. If you dislike this, remove either mod.)"
	]
	quest.1FB3D1FAE9A88C39.quest_subtitle: "Not knowing how to use it probably doesn't matter, maybe"
	quest.1FB3D1FAE9A88C39.title: "Prelude to the Gears"
	quest.1FB95C69AF3C83E3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Archmage Settlements&r"
		"&7Archmages travel to the &6End&r&7 dimension to study the secrets of the endless void, requiring a temporary dwelling. They build makeshift homes across the End for research and exploration.&r"
	]
	quest.1FB95C69AF3C83E3.title: "&6Archmage Settlement&r"
	quest.1FBA0FE6A13F8E70.quest_subtitle: "You will receive a starter pack"
	quest.1FBA0FE6A13F8E70.title: "&a\"Honey That Conceals Suffering at the Beginning\""
	quest.1FC7A319D738A388.quest_desc: ["&7Functions like a vanilla &#66CCFFSword&7. Can be crafted by placing a vanilla &#66CCFFSword&7 in a crafting table to convert it into an &#66DDCCSilent Gear Sword&7."]
	quest.1FC7A319D738A388.quest_subtitle: "Classic Weapon"
	quest.1FD98B36E1B61A56.quest_desc: ["As an advanced bookshelf, the Nether Bookshelf provides a higher enchanting cap than vanilla bookshelves. Nether magic grants additional &4&lQuanta&r&r."]
	quest.1FD98B36E1B61A56.quest_subtitle: "The Coming of Quanta"
	quest.1FD98B36E1B61A56.title: "Nether Enchanting Power—Embrace Chaos"
	quest.20026163291DE7A2.quest_desc: ["&7This bookshelf currently appears identical to a regular wooden bookshelf. Its cracks make it seem older and more ordinary. But you can sense a mysterious power surging within—like a heartbeat, like Sculk, waiting to be awakened."]
	quest.20026163291DE7A2.quest_subtitle: "Deep-Sleeping Sculk Power"
	quest.20026163291DE7A2.title: "A Chance Accident?"
	quest.2037EF7CC87E7974.quest_desc: [
		"&7Under normal circumstances, it can be used as a &#FFD700Casting Table&7. When right-clicking the drain, if a &#66DDCCCasting Table&7 and &#66DDCCMold&7 are attached, liquid will flow out."
		""
		"&7It can receive &#FF6666Redstone signals&7, continuously outputting liquid when powered."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Fluids can also be directly exported into &#66CCFFliquid containers&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/productivemetalworks_kjs_1.png width:150 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.2037EF7CC87E7974.quest_subtitle: "Exporting Liquid"
	quest.20736EF41F1FED8E.quest_desc: ["&7Echo Shards effectively increase various drops from mobs, triggering an extra drop roll when a mob dies. This attribute has a maximum of 3 levels."]
	quest.20736EF41F1FED8E.quest_subtitle: "Increased Drops"
	quest.2075CDEF8E217AEA.quest_subtitle: "Who are you?"
	quest.2075CDEF8E217AEA.title: "First Champion Kill"
	quest.20848CB8F54AD783.quest_desc: [
		"&7Provides simple offensive stat bonuses. Downside is that the Acropolis might be far away..."
		""
		"&7Use the Eye of the Storm to locate the Acropolis. Some mobs and bosses there are stage-locked, but the Jellyfish Leah can still be fought and drops Lacrima normally."
		""
		"Recommended part: Weapon Tip Upgrade"
	]
	quest.20848CB8F54AD783.quest_subtitle: "You're in the Same League as the Stat Stick"
	quest.20AB2C2F60CDFE1C.quest_subtitle: "As the title says"
	quest.20B149C81F944E27.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click a &#66FF66Wisp&7 with a glass bottle to capture it in the bottle."
		""
		"&7Right-click a block with a Wisp Bottle to release the &#66FF66Wisp&7, returning the glass bottle."
		""
		"&7Aside from transporting &#66FF66Wisps&7, this item can also be used as a crafting material."
	]
	quest.20B149C81F944E27.quest_subtitle: "Oi, Old Man, I Parked My Wisp Under Your Building"
	quest.20E0FE36906F6A98.quest_desc: ["&7Reduces target &#FF6666max health&7 based on damage dealt (if health is above 50%, no damage—only max health is reduced). Right-click detonates the reduced max health, dealing &#FFAA3320%&7 of the total reduction as damage."]
	quest.20E0FE36906F6A98.quest_subtitle: "You forgot to thaw me"
	quest.20EF8A85CD3EFF3A.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#66FF99Essence Crucible&7 consumes &#FFAA33Rune&7 durability and &#66FF99Essence&7 to perform &#CC99FFessence focusing&7, generating resources."
		""
		"&7The &#66FF99Essence Crucible&7 is &e2&7 blocks tall with &e1&7 item slot, &e4&7 essence slots, &e4&7 upgrade slots, and &e1&7 core upgrade slot. Multiple upgrades of the same type stack. A &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect how full the item and essence slots are."
		""
		"&7Can be accelerated by &#66DDCCEssence Catalysts&7 within &e4&7 blocks (&e3&7 in 1.20.1), up to &e8&7 catalysts."
		""
		"&7Holding a &#66DDCCTuning Fork&7 or &#FF8844Create Wrench&7 displays all stats and allows selecting one attribute to tune."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&b&lFocusing Speed"
		"&7The speed of essence focusing. Base is &e100%&7. Progress increases by &#FFDD55focusing speed&7 per tick until the recipe's required time is reached."
		""
		"&b&lFuel Consumption Rate"
		"&7The rate at which the &#66DDCCEssence Catalyst&7 consumes fuel. Base is &e100%&7. During focusing, consumes &#FFDD55fuel consumption rate&7 * &#FFDD55focusing speed&7 burn time per tick."
		""
		"&b&lDestabilization Risk"
		"&7The probability of double durability consumption. Base is &e20%&7. When this exceeds &e100%&7, consumption becomes round(double durability * &#FF6666destabilization risk&7)."
		""
		"&b&lDamage Absorption Probability"
		"&7The probability that an item consumes no durability."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&b&lRepair Probability"
		"&7After a focus cycle completes and durability is consumed, the chance to repair the item. Each &e100%&7 guarantees &e1&7 repair, with the remainder giving a corresponding chance for &e1&7 repair. Each repair restores &e1%&7 of max durability."
		""
		"&b&lChain Focus Probability"
		"&7When a focus cycle completes, the chance to instantly complete the next focus. On trigger, the next focus takes &#FFDD55focusing speed&7 * &e10&7 ticks (approx. &e10&7 game ticks), all attribute multipliers +&e20%&7, chain focus multiplier -&e20%&7 (stackable). On failure, attribute changes reset to &e0&7."
		""
		"&b&lFortune Probability"
		"&7The chance to increase product output by one. Each &e100%&7 guarantees +&e1&7 product, with the remainder giving a chance for +&e1&7 product."
		""
		"&b&lTuning Burden"
		"&7The debuff multiplier of the tuning fork. Base is &e100%&7. Tuned stat value = current value * (&e1&7 + tuning fork debuff multiplier * &#FF6666tuning burden&7)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&b&lTuning Strength"
		"&7The buff multiplier of the tuning fork. Base is &e100%&7. Tuned stat value = current value * (&e1&7 + tuning fork buff multiplier * &#66FF66tuning strength&7)."
		""
		"&b&lWeakest Attribute Tuning"
		"&7The buff is applied to the lowest attribute among those that can be tuned, calculated after tuning."
		""
		"&b&lDoom Reversal"
		"&7When &#66FF66doom reversal&7 is > &e0&7 and chain focus has not triggered, accumulates item durability loss and reduces buff count by &e1&7. When repaired via repair probability, additionally restores &e1%&7 * &#66FF66doom reversal&7 of max durability, gains &e20%&7 + accumulated durability loss * &e5%&7 all-attribute buff, and resets accumulated durability loss to &e0&7. Buff count is &e3&7."
		""
		"&b&lCaustic Tuning"
		"&7Increases &#66FF66tuning strength&7 by &#FF6666destabilization risk&7 * &#66FF66caustic tuning&7 * &e2&7. Example: destabilization risk &e50%&7, caustic tuning &e100%&7 → tuning strength +&e100%&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&b&lResonance Tuning"
		"&7Calculated after tuning and weakest attribute tuning. Reduces &#FF6666destabilization risk&7 at the cost of &#FFDD55focusing speed&7, with some loss. When &#FFDD55focusing speed&7 ≥ &e2&7 * &#FF6666destabilization risk&7 and &#FF6666destabilization risk&7 ≤ &e1&7, destabilization risk can always be reduced to &e0&7."
		""
		"&7Calculation flow:"
		""
		"&7target value = min(&#FF6666destabilization risk&7 * &#66FF66resonance tuning&7, &#FFDD55focusing speed&7) * &e2&7;"
		"&7conversion value = clamp(&#FFDD55focusing speed&7 / target value, &e0&7, &e1&7);"
		"&7If conversion value > &e0&7:"
		"&#FFDD55focusing speed&7 -= clamp(target value / &#FFDD55focusing speed&7, &e0&7, &e1&7) * &e0.8&7;"
		"&#FF6666destabilization risk&7 -= conversion value."
	]
	quest.20EF8A85CD3EFF3A.quest_subtitle: "Mysterious Duplication"
	quest.20EF8A85CD3EFF3A.title: "Essence Focusing"
	quest.2139D29C06E64C48.quest_subtitle: "Kill Kill Kill"
	quest.214D64602702D242.quest_desc: [
		"&6Suspicious Device&r"
		""
		"&7Arcane and profane magic are indeed opposed, and one can use them to create opposing upgrades. However, the torrent of arcane magic rushing toward the end of profane magic produces only chaos, resulting in explosions that corrode everything and the corruption that follows. This entry is provided as a warning, not a recommendation.&r"
	]
	quest.214D64602702D242.quest_subtitle: "A Cautionary Tale"
	quest.215AB6260ED8DAAD.quest_desc: ["&7Take a gamble?&r"]
	quest.215AB6260ED8DAAD.quest_subtitle: "Random Level + Random Enchantment"
	quest.215AB6260ED8DAAD.title: "Random Enchanted Book Vendor"
	quest.2190DB8F13415C43.quest_desc: [
		"&6Flame Accelerator Throwable&r"
		"&7&cEvolving Fire&r&7 is so intense that it destroys everything in its path as it evolves and spreads. Thus, it was inevitable that a devastating weapon based on it would exist—and indeed, it does."
		"&7"
		"&7Using a pair of &6Lantern Clamps&r&7, I crafted this \"&6Flame Accelerator Throwable&r&7.\" It recalibrates &bLingering Flames&r&7 to \"unlock\" them, transforming their gentle fire into explosive flames and containing them before launch."
		"&7"
		"&7I added a layer of safety, because... I don't want to rebuild my lab again. These flames are extremely explosive. Of course, basic blast-proof measures like obsidian can contain them."
	]
	quest.2190DB8F13415C43.quest_subtitle: "Evolution Transcends All"
	quest.219B219DA2F8C114.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lush Shallows&r"
		"&7A marine biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7The Lush Shallows has a distinctly different vegetation cover compared to the Starlight Sea."
		"&7Its signature &#32CD32Sea Bell Stalk forests&r&7 and unique &#9ACD32yellow-green ambient color&r&7 give the biome a distinct, peaceful atmosphere."
		""
		"&7Non-aquatic creatures can only spawn dozens of blocks below the surface of the Lush Shallows."
	]
	quest.219B219DA2F8C114.quest_subtitle: "Flourishing Forest"
	quest.219B219DA2F8C114.title: "Lush Shallows"
	quest.21A80A164028813C.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.21A80A164028813C.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.21DFA7D5BF06FF3A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mirror of Truth&r"
		"&7Used to reveal disguised &dIllusionist&r&7 familiars. Obtained via &6ritual&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.21FE19A7D8EFA94C.quest_desc: ["Sneak + Right-click to dash forward, dealing damage and stunning targets on impact."]
	quest.21FE19A7D8EFA94C.quest_subtitle: "Shield Hero"
	quest.221645B2BE16D7E1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Prospector"
		""
		"&7Greed burns.&r"
		"&7-When hit while under the '&cGreed&r&7' effect, you are consumed by &cflames&r"
		""
		"&7A blessing from the flames.&r"
		"&7-Collecting &eprecious minerals&r&7 grants the '&6Greed&r&7' status&r"
		"&7-The '&6Greed&r&7' status gradually increases &aluck probability&r"
		"&7-Gaining '&6Greed&r&7' also restores one heart of &alost health&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_combustion.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.221645B2BE16D7E1.quest_subtitle: "Treasures of the Earth"
	quest.221645B2BE16D7E1.title: "Pact of the Prospector"
	quest.2218345B2D47B183.title: "Comet Creeper"
	quest.2227DDA9A63E5685.quest_desc: ["Hmm... do we really need to teach how to summon the Wither?"]
	quest.2227DDA9A63E5685.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.223819B7B37AEFB2.quest_desc: [
		"Back when I barely knew how to do Java tweaks, Cod just mentioned a requirement and they made a whole mod (even though it was later optimized)."
		""
		"But I will never forget it!"
	]
	quest.223819B7B37AEFB2.quest_subtitle: "Contributor"
	quest.223819B7B37AEFB2.title: "The P"
	quest.2239EBD39F850AC6.quest_desc: [
		"&7If traditional spears are limited by reach, why not fire projectiles instead?"
		""
		"&7When fully charged, the &#FFD700Ancient Spear&7 fires a slightly homing &#66CCFFprojectile&7 with left-click. Projectile damage scales with the player's damage (affected by Strength, etc.)."
	]
	quest.2239EBD39F850AC6.quest_subtitle: "Ancient Wisdom"
	quest.2248B07BE012F5B4.quest_desc: ["&7The original airship—stable flight, compact size. The main downside is its relatively slow speed, making it less ideal for exploration."]
	quest.2254C590DE6A8100.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Berserker"
		"&7Harm yourself, harm others.&r&cWrath fades over time&r&cDamage taken is doubled"
		"&7Endless wrath, eternal fury; pain brings wrath, wrath brings power.&r&aDamage taken becomes wrath&r&aDealing damage launches &cevil arcane&r&a blasts at enemies fueled by wrath"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_berserker.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2254C590DE6A8100.quest_subtitle: "An Eye for an Eye"
	quest.2254C590DE6A8100.title: "Pact of the Berserker"
	quest.2258C63A869294AC.quest_desc: ["Faster acceleration of the smelting furnace's processing speed."]
	quest.2258C63A869294AC.quest_subtitle: "Bigger, Better, Stronger"
	quest.226A2B7E35FB2F05.quest_desc: ["Obtained from loot. The Glacial State debuff effectively damages slow enemies."]
	quest.226A2B7E35FB2F05.quest_subtitle: "Provides Spell Power Boost"
	quest.22C08630C5BB8322.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade the Smeltery"
	quest.22C4B375D17DC6C8.quest_desc: [
		"&7[JNE] Jaden's Nether Expansion is a great &#FF6666Nether expansion&7 mod, but in 1.21.1, it hasn't been fully ported yet."
		""
		"So some features may not be implemented. These unimplemented mechanics will be modified in the modpack—for example, by adding new sources to obtain certain items."
	]
	quest.22C4B375D17DC6C8.quest_subtitle: "A Work in Progress"
	quest.22DBDBE68B6E1B4D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Weapon Enchanting&r"
		"&7Spell scrolls can be applied to weapons, allowing the player to cast that spell while holding the weapon. Note: This will override the mod's spell or other mod's right-click weapon skills.&r"
		""
		"&6Robe Enchanting&r"
		"&7Players can also infuse spells into certain robes added by the mod (e.g., &cPlague Surgeon Coat&r&7, &cBlood Cleric Robe&r&7, etc.). While wearing an infused robe, the player can cast the infused spell. However, the &eWandering Mage Robe&r&7 and &eSpooky Pumpkin Robe&r&7 cannot be infused.&r"
	]
	quest.22E5438A416558FF.quest_desc: ["Right-click to clear an ongoing invasion"]
	quest.22E5438A416558FF.quest_subtitle: "Tired of annoying invasions?"
	quest.2331CCFEF5A9EEE5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Lone Druid"
		"&7Unbound means unarmored.&r"
		"&7-When damaged, armor drags you down, growing &cthorns&r&7 that damage your soul&r"
		""
		"&7Whole means unbound.&r"
		"&7-Each empty armor slot grants five &earmor&r&7 points and two &earmor toughness&r"
		"&7-Each empty armor slot increases &ahealing&r&7 received by one quarter&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_lone_druid.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2331CCFEF5A9EEE5.quest_subtitle: "Fleeing the External"
	quest.2331CCFEF5A9EEE5.title: "Pact of the Lone Druid"
	quest.233B0326CCA639C7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Duration Doubling&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Duration Doubling suppresses the form's decay process, extending the duration of &apositive effects&r&7 on the wearer.&r"
	]
	quest.233B0326CCA639C7.quest_subtitle: "Things That Remain in Stasis"
	quest.2358AB144E490565.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.2376D883261AE9AC.quest_desc: ["Dropped by Ignis. Can effectively reduce enemy armor."]
	quest.2376D883261AE9AC.quest_subtitle: "Ignitium Power"
	quest.2377B4B5C5413B34.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.2377B4B5C5413B34.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.23B6D00570354BE3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Boiler&r"
		""
		"&7An advanced power source that generates stress by producing steam from heated water. It outputs vast amounts of stress and is a core power source widely used in the mid-to-late game.&r"
		"&7Stress output: &c2048–294912 su&7"
		"&7RPM range: &c16–64 RPM&r"
		""
		"&6Construction&r"
		"&7Placing a &eSteam Engine&7 or &eSteam Whistle&7 on any &eFluid Tank&7 structure converts it into a boiler.&r"
		""
		"&6Operating Conditions&r"
		"&7The boiler requires a constant water supply and a heat source underneath to function.&r"
		"&7Its efficiency is determined by three factors: **Size**, **Water**, and **Heat**, each with 18 levels. Wear &eEngineer's Goggles&7 to view specific stats.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Attribute        Calculation&r"
		"&7📏Size          Based on boiler volume (m³). Size level = total volume / 4&r"
		"&7💧Water         Based on supply rate. Each Mechanical Pump at 2 RPM provides 1 mB/tick. Water level = supply rate (mB/t) / 10, or Water level = pump RPM / 20&r"
		"&7🔥Heat          Based on total heat from all heat sources below. See below.&r"
		"&7The boiler does not store water; it calculates water levels from the supply rate. Any fluid in the tank before conversion is cleared.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Heat Sources&r"
		"&7Heat sources that can fuel the boiler include:&r"
		"&7Source Type      Source                                Heat Value&r"
		"&7Passive          Blaze Burner (unlit/empty), Campfire, Fire, Magma Block, Lava, Stove (Farmer's Delight), etc.      0&r"
		"&7Level 1          Blaze Burner (normal burn)           1&r"
		"&7Level 2          Blaze Burner (superheated)           2&r"
		"&7Passive sources put the boiler in a &cPassive State&7, outputting a fixed &c2048 su&7. Adding more passive sources does not increase efficiency. Passive sources are ignored if a higher-level source is present.&r"
		"&7Only the heat source directly below the boiler affects it.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Power Output&r"
		"&7The boiler's final level is determined by the **lowest** of the three attributes: Size, Water, and Heat.&r"
		"&7A &eSteam Engine&7 must be attached to the boiler, with a &eShaft&7 placed in the second block in front of the engine to output stress.&r"
		""
		"&6Stress Calculation&r"
		"&7Except in the passive state, the boiler outputs &cBoiler Level × 16384 su&7, distributed evenly among all Steam Engines.&r"
		"&7Each Steam Engine outputs a maximum of &c16384 su&7. If total stress exceeds this, multiple Steam Engines are needed to avoid waste.&r"
		"&7Installing a number equal to the boiler level fully outputs all stress; additional engines do not improve efficiency.&r"
		""
		"&6RPM Output&r"
		"&7The RPM output from Steam Engines ranges from &c16 RPM to 64 RPM&7, determined by the ratio of engines to boiler level.&r"
		""
		"&8This page seems slightly curled from steam.&r"
	]
	quest.24024A47877C3B54.quest_desc: ["Right-click to reset the invasion counter to 0, entering a long safe period"]
	quest.24024A47877C3B54.quest_subtitle: "Tired of annoying invasions?"
	quest.244305D501AB31AA.quest_subtitle: "Higher armor stats than regular armor, at the cost of mana-related stats"
	quest.2443B7C22B13BC1F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Inspired by the Hallowed Gold Obelisk, you crafted an obelisk from what you considered useless Brilliance. The power of experience didn't affect soul infusion rituals but instead enhanced another form of magic—enchanting."
		""
		"&7Though it provides a large amount of &aEterna&7, affected by its original world, its &aEterna&7 cap is no different from a vanilla bookshelf."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7And you might later regret wasting such precious materials on this."
	]
	quest.2443B7C22B13BC1F.quest_subtitle: "High-Level Vanilla Bookshelf (?)"
	quest.2443B7C22B13BC1F.title: "Powerful Yet Feeble"
	quest.2453187E1E29FF73.quest_desc: ["&7Using the light of Prismarine Shards, I amplified and distorted the Ocean Bookshelf's power. Now it provides not only &5Arcana&7 but also some &4Quanta&7. After all, uncertainty is part of the mystery."]
	quest.2453187E1E29FF73.quest_subtitle: "A More Balanced Ocean Bookshelf"
	quest.2453187E1E29FF73.title: "Mystical Extension"
	quest.2482C01B41948195.quest_desc: ["&7A cheap and versatile material. Performs well for both &#CC99FFweapons&7 and &#66CCFFarmor&7. An excellent &#FFD700transition material&7. Its low cost allows mass production for repair kits—with a bit of enchanting, it can handle most early-game enemies."]
	quest.2482C01B41948195.quest_subtitle: "King of Transition"
	quest.24A6B77DD8DEA131.quest_desc: [
		"&7Scrolls are single-use consumables with high material costs, making them economically inefficient."
		""
		""
		"&7Hold a scroll to cast its spell without consuming mana, but the scroll is &4consumed&r in the process."
		"&7Use a &6Spell Inscription Table&r to inscribe the scroll into a spellbook, allowing repeated casting at the cost of mana."
	]
	quest.24C387A38C376961.quest_subtitle: "You didn't farm deaths to get this reward, right? ...Right?"
	quest.24F8461D0711F786.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Unnatural Endurance&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Unnatural Endurance grants the wearer a hysterical speed—they can always sprint, even when &chunger&r&7 is too low to sprint normally.&r"
	]
	quest.24F8461D0711F786.quest_subtitle: "Fleeing the Pursuer"
	quest.257E95B5ED03904D.quest_desc: ["&7An upgraded hoe. Can also function as an &#66DDCCAxe&7 and &#66DDCCShovel&7. Chains small areas of grass, but isn't a full replacement for &#66DDCCAxe&7 or &#66DDCCShovel&7—after all, it's still a hoe."]
	quest.257E95B5ED03904D.quest_subtitle: "Better Than a Hoe"
	quest.25CE20F4B934CF78.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.25CE20F4B934CF78.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.26199250ABE1AA3E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Applies bone meal to crops within a &#FFAA333×3×3&7 range."
		"&7Since it's a &#FFAA333×3×3&7 area centered on the crop you click, all crops within that range will receive a &#66FF66bone meal effect&7."
	]
	quest.26199250ABE1AA3E.quest_subtitle: "The Bell Tolls"
	quest.2650317F3653A86F.quest_desc: ["&7Very hard to obtain. Attacks apply frost buildup—at max stacks, the target is frozen."]
	quest.2650317F3653A86F.quest_subtitle: "Enslaving Dragons Is Truly Disgraceful"
	quest.266954CE47E5BBAA.quest_desc: ["&7Right-click to throw a &#FFD700Thunder Spear&7. On impact with the ground, creates a small area of &#66CCFFlightning pool&7."]
	quest.266954CE47E5BBAA.quest_subtitle: "I Won't Tell You Anything Aaaaaaah!"
	quest.26F574E2557F8ADF.quest_desc: ["Another great snake! They helped with some tweaks early on, though the code was later deprecated... but they still helped Cod!"]
	quest.26F574E2557F8ADF.quest_subtitle: "Some Code + Contributor"
	quest.26FC3272EF9F44E8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crystallized Berries&r"
		"&7Unearthed by &bSniffers&r&7. Can be fed to your familiar to obtain &eMemory Fragments&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.270113919FB0BE75.quest_desc: ["The best percentage-based damage boost in Stage 1."]
	quest.270113919FB0BE75.quest_subtitle: "Feels Tingly When Held"
	quest.27220D017F7E0659.quest_desc: ["&7Each &#66FF99Essence&7 harvested while equipped grants random (&e1.0&7–&e4.0&7) * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 experience points (rounded)."]
	quest.27220D017F7E0659.quest_subtitle: "Special Effect on Essence Harvest"
	quest.2723E285F0AD8412.quest_subtitle: "Higher armor stats than regular armor, at the cost of mana-related stats"
	quest.2723F0F916E98181.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each &#66FF99Essence&7 harvested while equipped:"
		""
		"&7Extends all positive effects by &e3&7 seconds, up to &e150&7 seconds;"
		"&7Reduces all negative effects by &e6&7 seconds."
		""
		"&7The duration extended or reduced is multiplied by &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 and rounded to the nearest tick."
	]
	quest.2723F0F916E98181.quest_subtitle: "Special Effect on Essence Harvest"
	quest.278B31B68AFBBC11.quest_desc: ["&7Using &#66CCFFSilent Gear's&7 alloy system, multiple materials can be fused via the &#FFD700Alloy Machine&7. The first material serves as the base, and traits are overwritten by higher-level versions. This lets you combine the stats of high-tier materials with the &#66FF66useful traits&7 of low-tier ones, customizing your ideal material."]
	quest.278B31B68AFBBC11.quest_subtitle: "Stacking Effects"
	quest.27B6C00949F92CCF.quest_desc: [
		"&7I seem to have discovered something strange: a form of magic not yet recorded. To call myself a mage, I cannot pass up the opportunity to learn it."
		""
		"&7The energy manipulated by this mysterious school seems rooted in &6souls&r&7. More precisely, it is the energy of the soul—the will and pulse that make up each of us."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7So far, I have only described the basics. But I have found a way to separate the soul's pulse and condense it into matter—I call these substances \"&6Essence Crystals&r&7.\" This is the foundation of my research."
		""
		"&7The nature of the condensed soul affects the crystal's properties. Every soul is unique, and the crystals they form vary accordingly. I believe these crystals are the breakthrough my research needs."
	]
	quest.27B6C00949F92CCF.quest_subtitle: "Soul Magic"
	quest.27E19E564DC0F89F.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.27E1C7E671DF7C03.quest_desc: [
		"&7Can point to the nearest unopened &#FFD700Lootr loot container&7 within &#FFAA3364 blocks&7 of you. Right-click to highlight the found container."
		""
		"&7No more worrying about missing hidden treasures in structures."
		"(Only searches when in the hotbar or held, and requires no UI to be open.)"
	]
	quest.27E1C7E671DF7C03.quest_subtitle: "Treasure Gourmet"
	quest.2808547613BD84C8.title: "Vine Wraith"
	quest.28235FFD2D0DE1DD.quest_desc: [
		"&#CC99FFCataclysm&7 focuses on the harvesting and application of &#55D5D5Souls&7. Initial harvesting of &#55D5D5Souls&7 requires a &#FFD700Scythe&7, but most materials made from &#55D5D5Essence&7 also have the ability to harvest souls. By adding a small amount of these materials to &#66CCFFweapons, armor, or even trinkets, you can break free from the constraints of the &#FFD700Scythe&7. Using &#66CCFFspells&7 to attack enemies achieves the same effect."
		""
		"&7Rumors say villagers also studied &#55D5D5Souls&7, but a major &#FF6666accident&7 led them to abandon all related research. Is this a case of village depravity or moral decay..."
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"Click to jump to Cataclysm Side Quest\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"27B6C00949F92CCF\" }  ,\"color\":\"blue\"}]"
	]
	quest.28235FFD2D0DE1DD.quest_subtitle: "Soul Magic"
	quest.28235FFD2D0DE1DD.title: "Uncanny Things"
	quest.283E7DF6FCE579BC.quest_subtitle: "Trait Launcher"
	quest.284BD033E472B251.quest_desc: [
		"Suffering Piles are blocks that do not naturally generate."
		""
		"Players need to use bone meal on a Difficult Gourd placed on Soul Sand."
		""
		"Then, several random blocks of Soul Sand within a few blocks of the gourd will be transformed into Suffering Piles."
	]
	quest.284BD033E472B251.quest_subtitle: "Misery"
	quest.284F3685C1A776D4.quest_desc: [
		"&7Found in the Starlight Dimension's Frozen Enchanted Forest. Can be used as a handle material—good for low-attack-speed weapons."
		""
		"Recommended part: Handle"
	]
	quest.284F3685C1A776D4.quest_subtitle: "Premium Fur"
	quest.287148E99E399EB1.quest_desc: ["Causes the spawner to ignore light levels when spawning mobs."]
	quest.287148E99E399EB1.quest_subtitle: "Eternal Night (on the spawner)"
	quest.287148E99E399EB1.title: "Soul Lantern"
	quest.288F52920CC79FEC.quest_desc: [
		"Initially, the pack was just for playing with friends. Later, the vision grew grander... and so, Reverie Foundry was born."
		""
		"P.S. Roboko is adorable."
	]
	quest.288F52920CC79FEC.quest_subtitle: "Planning + Contributor"
	quest.28A651F6B7D52DF2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Warlock"
		"&7Feel &canger&r&7, and evoke &canger&r&7.&r&cEnemies can detect you from twice as far"
		"&7A pact that specializes in fusing &canger&r&7 with &cpain&r&7.&r&aThe first hit on an enemy triggers a &cevil arcane&r&a blast"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_warlock.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.28A651F6B7D52DF2.quest_subtitle: "Endless Battle"
	quest.28A651F6B7D52DF2.title: "Pact of the Warlock"
	quest.28F42F3025DEB18C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Glowing Moth&r&7"
		"&7Flying neutral creatures that only attack when provoked; &r"
		""
		"&7Group Aggression: When one is attacked, all &A351DAGlowing Moths&r&7 nearby target the attacker; &r"
		""
		"&7Before each attack, the Glowing Moth needs to charge up: &r"
		""
		"&7It flies as far away from the target as possible, circling around them horizontally; &r"
		"&7Then, it continuously fires &F159BBhoming sound waves&r&7 that ignore shields. Each wave can hit the same target up to 10 times (each hit deals damage instantly); &r"
		""
		"&7Though it resembles the Warden's sonic blast, the moth's sound waves deal physical damage (reduced by armor), not magic damage. &r"
		""
		"&7Players can tame Glowing Moths by right-clicking them with any type of meat; &r"
		""
		"&7Tamed Glowing Moths can only follow the player (they cannot sit and stay); &r"
		""
		"&7Tamed Glowing Moths will attack monsters that attack or are attacked by the player; &r"
		""
		"&7Right-click a tamed Glowing Moth with &eLunaris Cactus Cream&r&7: &r"
		""
		"&7The moth consumes it, with a low chance to produce 1 &#F8CD4BShivering Gel&r&7. &r"
	]
	quest.28F42F3025DEB18C.title: "Glowing Moth"
	quest.28FBA3F985201394.quest_subtitle: "Higher armor stats than regular armor, at the cost of mana-related stats"
	quest.2911813B45667FF4.quest_desc: ["Using the symbol of draconic power, I crafted this bookshelf. Perhaps due to returning to simplicity, it provides only a massive amount of &aEterna&r—and most importantly, raises the &aEterna&r cap to its maximum."]
	quest.2911813B45667FF4.quest_subtitle: "Reaching the Pinnacle of Eterna"
	quest.2911813B45667FF4.title: "Dragon's Roar"
	quest.291925E282FCB75C.quest_subtitle: "Most likely a ring"
	quest.292EE3446E29D4BA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Completion"
		"&7Satiety requires health.&r&cArmor and armor toughness halved when near hunger"
		"&7Wholeness means satiety.&r&aArmor and armor toughness increased by one fifth when near full satiety"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_combustion.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.292EE3446E29D4BA.quest_subtitle: "Pursuit of Satisfaction"
	quest.292EE3446E29D4BA.title: "Pact of Completion"
	quest.293A85724AE2C0E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eQuanta Stability: &r&7Alters the minimum final enchantment level affected by Quanta fluctuations—effectively negating Quanta's downside while retaining its upside."
		""
		"&7The Geode-Sealed Stable Bookshelf provides Quanta Stability."
	]
	quest.29833D624EE0F60A.quest_subtitle: "&cDisables natural sanity recovery (does not disable trait effects)"
	quest.29833D624EE0F60A.title: "&c\"Madness oozes from the corners of the eyes\""
	quest.2A0C75F0BB1001BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Precision Mechanism&r"
		""
		"&7An advanced internal component that requires multiple delicate steps to produce. Commonly used in assembling complex machinery like &eMechanical Arms&7.&r"
	]
	quest.2A3657E05759C933.quest_desc: ["&7Excellent stats early on, but only has a &#FFAA332%&7 chance to drop from &#66CCFFDiamond Ore&7."]
	quest.2A3657E05759C933.quest_subtitle: "The Lucky One"
	quest.2A56714310939AFB.quest_desc: ["&7Directly increases luck, affecting loot quality and drops. Stacking luck early on is a high-yield strategy with long-term benefits."]
	quest.2A56714310939AFB.quest_subtitle: "Lucky One"
	quest.2A8629B66F128293.quest_desc: ["&7No need to say more—it sounds great, and I love it."]
	quest.2A8629B66F128293.quest_subtitle: "Comes with Its Own Sound Effect"
	quest.2AE9864AC40241A7.quest_desc: ["Provides percentage-based armor bonus, but reduces healing received and enchantment stats."]
	quest.2AE9864AC40241A7.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Thinking"
	quest.2AF2FF75BEEDF6FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Increases the number of mobs spawned per spawner cycle. Use cautiously—make sure you can handle the output."
		""
		"&7Requires a Ghast Tear for modification; otherwise, the spawn cap limit may bottleneck efficiency."
	]
	quest.2AF2FF75BEEDF6FF.quest_subtitle: "Minimum 2000 Spent Here"
	quest.2B4635BB16624A15.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Essence Altar can perform &#CC99FFessence infusion crafting&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum_kjs1.png width:150 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
		"&7The Essence Altar has &e1&7 item slot, &e8&7 essence slots, and &e8&7 additional slots. A &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect how full the slots are."
		""
		"&b&lEssence Infusion:"
		"&7The main item for the recipe must be placed in the &eitem slot (center of the altar)&7"
		"&#66FF99Essences&7 must be placed in the &eessence slots (center of the altar)&7"
		"&aOther items must be placed in &eextra slots&7 on nearby &#66DDCCItem Stands&7, &#66DDCCItem Pedestals&7, or &#CC99FFRune Workbenches&7"
		"&7(within &e4&7 blocks horizontally and &e3&7 blocks vertically from the Essence Altar)."
		""
		"&7Extra slots can only interact with non-directional item transfer, and all items in extra slots will be &ccleared&7 after each craft."
		""
		"&7The &#66FF99Essence&7 types in the essence slots must exactly match the recipe—no extra &#66FF99Essence&7 types are allowed."
		""
		"&7Each nearby &#FFAA33Runic Wood Obelisk&7 increases essence infusion speed by &e25%&7, up to &e4&7 obelisks."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&#66DDCCEMI&7 can be used to view &#CC99FFessence infusion&7 recipes."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/recipe.png width:125 height:160 align:center}"
		"&7The &#FF6666red box&7 on the left shows the required &#66FF99Essence&7 types"
		"&7The &#66CCFFblue box&7 on the right shows the required &eother items&r"
		"&7The &#FFAA33orange box&7 in the middle shows the required &6main item&r"
		""
		"&7Place them as described on the previous page to begin &#CC99FFessence infusion&7."
	]
	quest.2B4635BB16624A15.quest_subtitle: "Miraculous Creations"
	quest.2B4635BB16624A15.title: "Essence Infusion"
	quest.2B8DFC4AE68FE112.quest_desc: [
		"&7By now, I should know what happens when a living creature enters the well—at least for intelligent life."
		"&7"
		"&7I was careless in my experiment, tripped over a reagent bottle on the floor... and fell straight into the black substance inside the well. The fact that I can still write this clearly shows I &asurvived&r&7... though I probably won't test that again."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7I was spat out by what I now confirm to be a liquid, just like the items I had thrown in. I later tested it on monsters and calves—they &cdid not&r&7 bounce back, simply vanishing into the well. I have no reason to waste more resources testing further. Besides, my attention is now entirely focused on what came back with me."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7It was as if I had shattered a soul—and mine was the only one present at the time. The thought is unsettling, but all my biometrics are still within acceptable ranges. What returned with me was a &8black&r&7 &dessence crystal&r&7, which I also collected. Could this be a precursor to a ninth form of arcane energy? If so, what kind of pulse does it represent? Further research is needed."
	]
	quest.2B8DFC4AE68FE112.quest_subtitle: "Error or Blessing?"
	quest.2B8DFC4AE68FE112.title: "The Pitch-Black Crystal"
	quest.2BA0CB58302C7BD4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Tidal Affinity"
		"&7The ocean's chains bind your heart tightly.&r&cUnable to heal while outside water"
		"&7Bind yourself to the ocean, heeding the tide's chanting call.&r&aUnderwater, gain increased movement speed, attack speed, mining speed, and damage resistance&r&aTide energy enhances these effects and grants constant health regeneration"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_tidal_affinity.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2BA0CB58302C7BD4.quest_subtitle: "One with the Sea"
	quest.2BA0CB58302C7BD4.title: "Pact of Tidal Affinity"
	quest.2C2C118EAFE0B1B7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Soul-Seeking Ember Bell&r"
		"&7Crafted via recipe. Used to summon the Boss &6Echo of Telos - The Primordial Fire-Receiver&r&7.&r"
		"&7Right-click to use. Emits a sound, produces particles, and attempts to summon the Fire-Receiver.&r"
		"&7If a &cBlaze Rune&r&7 is nearby, the bell is consumed and the boss is summoned. If none are found, the bell is not consumed and a message '&cNo response was received&r&7' appears.&r"
		"&7Each use has a 3-second cooldown if the bell is not consumed.&r"
		""
		"&8\"Forged to recall the 'spark' stolen since the world's first flame—a resonance bell that only echoes to the lament of the Blaze Rune.\""
	]
	quest.2C2C118EAFE0B1B7.quest_subtitle: "Ding Dong Ding"
	quest.2C34F57D3538E222.quest_desc: [
		"This bookshelf is crafted by &binfusing&r the Dormant Sculk Bookshelf. It provides decent enchanting stats and raises the Eterna cap to 70."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7What have I done?"
		"&7I seem to have placed the cracked bookshelf into the enchanting table. Under the embrace of Sculk, it began to grow and merge. Eventually, the cracks were filled, becoming a new existence."
		"&7I feel its more powerful presence, and sense no malice from it. Perhaps it's because it's my creation, or maybe it needs something from me. Either way, I now have a more powerful bookshelf."
	]
	quest.2C34F57D3538E222.quest_subtitle: "Embracing Sculk"
	quest.2C34F57D3538E222.title: "Sculk Energy Awakened"
	quest.2C5A0FE2059F81B1.quest_desc: ["&7Tools made for familiars. Shrunken items/armor can become trinkets for familiars, while shrunken food can be fed to heal them. Note that all food special effects and buffs/debuffs do not apply, so choose high-saturation foods."]
	quest.2C5C9488AA4912AD.quest_subtitle: "Used for Casting Wires"
	quest.2C9F35CB08351DC4.quest_subtitle: "Easy to Get, Easy to Improve"
	quest.2CA02120B210EB2D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blaze Burner&r"
		""
		"&6Obtaining&r"
		"&7Right-click a &cBlaze&7 or &cBlaze Spawner&7 with an empty Blaze Burner to obtain it.&r"
		""
		"&6Usage&r"
		""
		"&6Fuel States&r"
		"&7The Blaze Burner requires fuel to operate. Players can feed it by right-clicking with fuel in hand.&r"
		"&7Feeding it normal fuel puts it in a normal burn state, with duration equal to the fuel's burn time in a vanilla &eFurnace&7. After burning, it enters an &cextinguished&7 state.&r"
		"&7Feeding it &6Blaze Cake&7 puts it in a superheated state, with the Blaze inside turning blue. A Blaze Cake lasts for &c160 seconds&r&7. After superheated burning, it enters a 250-second normal burn state, then extinguishes.&r"
		"&7Using a &6Creative Blaze Cake&7 toggles between burn states and maintains the current state permanently.&r"
		"&7Throwing an &eEgg&7 at it puts it in a normal burn state for 4 seconds, with a chewing sound.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The default maximum burn time is &c500 seconds&r.&r"
		"&7However, if a single item has a burn time exceeding 500 seconds and the Blaze Burner is &cextinguished&r, the item's burn time is used instead of the 500-second cap. For example, a Block of Coal provides 800 seconds.&r"
		"&7If the Blaze Burner is already burning, adding more normal fuel will not exceed the 500-second cap. For example, if it has 200 seconds remaining, adding a Block of Coal results in 500 seconds, not 800.&r"
		""
		"&7Blaze Burners can be fed by &eMechanical Arms&r&7 or &eDeployers&r, which automatically recognize the state and stop when fuel is sufficient.&r"
		"&7When using a Mechanical Arm, it will keep feeding if the burner is superheated and Blaze Cakes are available—it won't let it enter normal burn. The arm detects the state and feeds before superheat ends. Rest assured.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Heating Basins&r"
		"&7Blaze Burners can heat Basins to complete '&cMixing&r&7', '&cPressing&r&7', or '&cAutomated Brewing&r&7 recipes that require higher heat.&r"
		"&7Some Basin recipes require normal or superheated heat. Place the Blaze Burner under the Basin and provide fuel to reach the required state. The burn state does not affect recipes needing lower heat.&r"
		""
		"&6Heating Boilers&r"
		"&7Blaze Burners can heat Boilers.&r"
		"&7Normal and superheated states provide &c1 point&r&7 and &c2 points&r&7 of heat, respectively. See the Boiler section.&r"
		""
		"&6As a Fan Heating Medium&r"
		"&7Blaze Burners change the air (wind) state of Fans.&r"
		"&7When air from a Fan passes through a Blaze Burner, it becomes &abulk smoking/smelting&r&7 air depending on the burn state.&r"
		"&7When &cextinguished&r, the air is in bulk smoking mode.&r"
		"&7When burning normally or superheated, the air is in bulk smelting mode.&r"
		""
		"&6Redstone Comparator&r"
		"&7Blaze Burners can be detected by a Redstone Comparator.&r"
		"&7When &cextinguished&r, the signal is 0.&r"
		"&7In normal burn, it outputs up to 2. If burn time is less than 5 seconds, the signal is 1; otherwise, it's 2.&r"
		"&7In superheated state, the signal is 3.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Driving Trains&r"
		"&7Blaze Burners can drive trains.&r"
		"&7To use a Blaze Burner as a driver, attach it to the train structure in front of the Train Controls during assembly. After assembly, right-click the burner with a Train Schedule containing a program. The Blaze will wear a hat and drive automatically according to the schedule.&r"
		""
		"&6As a Stockbroker&r"
		"&7A Blaze Burner can function as a Stockbroker.&r"
		"&7Place a Stockbroker adjacent to a Blaze Burner—it will act as the Stockbroker, and the burner can be right-clicked for interaction.&r"
	]
	quest.2CE15B505BACCDC3.quest_desc: ["It was a huge surprise when a great snake appeared out of nowhere to help with item coding mid-development!"]
	quest.2CE15B505BACCDC3.quest_subtitle: "Code + Contributor"
	quest.2D0DFDD4C050FFA3.quest_desc: [
		"This bookshelf, empowered by Sculk and Ancient City power, provides a new ability—direct access to Treasure Enchantments from the enchanting table."
		"However, opportunity and risk go hand in hand. Cursed enchantments may also appear as Treasure Enchantments. But I recall a device that can prevent curses from applying."
	]
	quest.2D0DFDD4C050FFA3.quest_subtitle: "Ancient City Reborn"
	quest.2D0DFDD4C050FFA3.title: "A Gift from the Deep Dark"
	quest.2D343AAA8E8523D1.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each &#66FF99Essence&7 harvested while equipped grants &e30&7 seconds of &#66BB66Tumorous Growth&7 effect."
		""
		"&7If the &#66BB66Tumorous Growth&7 effect is already active, instead extends it by &e7.5&7 seconds (up to &e1&7 hour) and increases the current effect level by &e1&7 (up to &e20&7)."
		""
		"&7The duration granted or extended is multiplied by the &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 attribute."
	]
	quest.2D343AAA8E8523D1.quest_subtitle: "Special Effect on Essence Harvest"
	quest.2D740B904DAEAB78.quest_desc: [
		"&6Familiar Bed&r"
		"&7A block that familiars can use to &asleep&r&7 and &arecover health&r&7. Familiars will search for nearby beds when they need healing.&r"
	]
	quest.2D740B904DAEAB78.quest_subtitle: "A Warm Home"
	quest.2D7AB1B4FC01C3F8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Empathy Driver&r"
		""
		"&7Evil and holy are opposing forces—why not combine them? When the &eCrucible&r&7 is equipped with an Empathy Driver, &8malevolent essences&r&7 remember the damage taken by &eRunes&r&7. When the &eMending Diffuser&r&7 repairs them, &bholy essences&r&7 \"forgive\" the damage, further repairing the Rune and boosting all stats for the next three &6focusing cycles&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.2D7AB1B4FC01C3F8.quest_subtitle: "Embracing Hatred"
	quest.2DCF4B22632FEAA6.quest_desc: ["&7Not easy to obtain, but the trait is worth the effort. Provides devastating armor break—reducing defense while dealing massive magic damage. Dual physical and magical pressure makes even high-resistance enemies trivial."]
	quest.2DCF4B22632FEAA6.quest_subtitle: "Enslaving Dragons Is Truly Disgraceful"
	quest.2DD51904F4629516.quest_desc: [
		"&7You'll need to start with the &#555555black&7 tier..."
		""
		"&7Once crafted into bricks, they can be &#66CCFFdyed&7. However, please note that &#FF6666dyed bricks cannot be used to craft controllers or other devices&7—you'll need to dye them after crafting the devices."
		""
		"&7In the early game, you can keep the furnace &#FFD700small&7 for easy disassembly and transport."
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"[Click to jump to Silent Gear]\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"09E68D57095A5F1D\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.2DD51904F4629516.quest_subtitle: "The Foundation of the Forge"
	quest.2DE8D48077862833.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Crafted via recipe. Used to summon the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Boss\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Echo of Telos - The Primordial Fire-Receiver\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-clicked\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\", it emits a sound, produces particles, and attempts to summon the Fire-Receiver.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Rune\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" is nearby, the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Soul-Seeking Ember Bell\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" will be consumed and the Fire-Receiver will be summoned. If no Blaze Rune is nearby, it will not be consumed.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.2DE8D48077862833.quest_subtitle: "\"You Should Trust Me and Offer Your Life\""
	quest.2E49C6ACDB5A84E2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Grimstone Golem&r&7"
		"&7Place a &#F5F5DCCarved Lunaris Cactus Fruit&r&7 on top of a &#C0C0C0Grimstone Brick&r&7 to &esummon&r&7 a Grimstone Golem. &r"
		""
		"&7Functions similarly to the &808080Tuff Golem&r&7 mentioned in a past Minecraft mob vote; &r"
		""
		"&7Right-click a Grimstone Golem with any item, and it will &ehold and display&r&7 that item; &r"
		""
		"&7While displaying an item, the Grimstone Golem &cdoes not move&r&7, but can still turn its body; &r"
		""
		"&7Items with &#FF8C00special held models&r&7 will render accordingly in the golem's hand; &r"
		""
		"&7You can retrieve the item by &FF4500killing&r&7 the golem or by &FFD700right-clicking&r&7 it while it's holding the item. &r"
	]
	quest.2E49C6ACDB5A84E2.quest_subtitle: "Item Display Stand"
	quest.2E49C6ACDB5A84E2.title: "Grimstone Golem"
	quest.2E830C01A529257D.quest_subtitle: "Acropolis"
	quest.2EC244BC65F18268.quest_desc: [
		"&7Runic Logs sometimes generate as &#FFAA33Resin-Rich Runic Logs&7, which have unique &#88DDFFmagical properties&7. After stripping with an &#FFCC44Axe&7, right-clicking with a &#66DDCCGlass Bottle&7 collects &#66FF99Runic Resin&7."
		""
		"&7Processing it yields &#66FF99Runic Resin Balls&7, which can partially substitute for &#66DDCCSlime Balls&7."
	]
	quest.2EC244BC65F18268.quest_subtitle: "Delicious Material"
	quest.2F38AC908EC156D9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of Unmaker's Disdain&r"
		""
		"&7The oath coexists with malevolent shelter, and its power is diminished by it.&r"
		"&7-Reduces &cmalevolent shelter&r&7 capacity&r"
		""
		"&7Etched into the malevolent soul-reaper's runes.&r"
		"&7-&6Malevolent criticals&r&7 trigger &econtinuous slashes&r&7 on the target&r"
		"&7-&6Malevolent conversion&r&7 increases the number and strength of the &eslashes&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_unmakers_disdain.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2F38AC908EC156D9.quest_subtitle: "Transcending All Things"
	quest.2F38AC908EC156D9.title: "Oath of Unmaker's Disdain"
	quest.2F6AEED848143A46.quest_subtitle: "Kill Kill Kill"
	quest.2F959196FB453034.quest_desc: [
		"These bookshelves are the highest tier of Sculk bookshelves. In addition to providing large amounts of &aEterna&r, &4Quanta&r, and &5Arcana&r, they also provide additional &3Enchantment Hints&r."
		"&rI recommend making several and permanently placing them near your main enchanting table."
	]
	quest.2F959196FB453034.quest_subtitle: "Listen to the Bookshelf's Heartbeat"
	quest.2F959196FB453034.title: "Warden's Enhancement—Pinnacle of Sculk Power"
	quest.2FE49A9C24350211.quest_desc: ["&7Functions like a vanilla &#66CCFFTrident&7. Customizable for &#FFAA33charge speed&7, &#FFAA33throw damage&7, and &#FFAA33throw velocity&7."]
	quest.2FE49A9C24350211.quest_subtitle: "Big Fork"
	quest.2FE5426155A22ADD.quest_desc: [
		"&7When equipped, consuming rotten food (Rotten Flesh, &#66BB66Putrid Essence&7, &#FFAA33Gluttonous Gel&7):"
		""
		"&7Grants &e30&7 seconds of &#FF8844Gluttony II&7, or increases current &#FF8844Gluttony&7 by &e2&7 levels (up to &eX&7)."
		""
		"&7Consuming &#FFAA33Gluttonous Gel&7 increases &#FF8844Gluttony&7 level by +&e1&7 and duration by +&e40&7 seconds."
	]
	quest.2FE5426155A22ADD.quest_subtitle: "Endless Hunger"
	quest.30039833D92481A3.quest_desc: ["Yes, you can have Creative Items 2.0."]
	quest.30039833D92481A3.quest_subtitle: "Infinite Storage 2.0"
	quest.302F073922CA3873.quest_desc: ["You're a good person. I'll follow you."]
	quest.302F073922CA3873.quest_subtitle: "Without their help, there would be no Reverie Foundry!"
	quest.305EC81E54A58CA7.quest_desc: ["Provides projectile speed and attack damage bonuses. Might work well for arrows."]
	quest.305EC81E54A58CA7.quest_subtitle: "Biu Biu"
	quest.307FD783B49CA47C.title: "Discover the Cursed Pyramid"
	quest.309D32324902DF18.quest_subtitle: "Food Value > 8"
	quest.309D32324902DF18.title: "Meal Recycling x10"
	quest.30E1A8BF53339ACD.quest_desc: ["&7A base trinket that only provides a small amount of &#FF8844armor&7. A necessary prerequisite for crafting its higher-tier variants."]
	quest.30E1A8BF53339ACD.quest_subtitle: "Trinket Base"
	quest.31259F6B81819141.quest_desc: ["&7Functions like a vanilla &#FFD700Mace&7. Damage scales with &#FFAA33fall height&7."]
	quest.31259F6B81819141.quest_subtitle: "A Blow to the Head"
	quest.313E8F6035C2E842.quest_desc: [
		"&7Runic Trees are a curious blend of magic and nature, and are quite common. They are &#FFCC44aesthetic&7, but I value their &#66FF99practicality&7 more. Steeped in &#88DDFFmagic&7, they serve as a foundation for &#CC99FFarcane&7 materials."
		""
		"&7These trees primarily appear on open &#66DD88plains&7, and can also be found in &#66DD88forests&7. Their most distinctive feature is their &#FFCC44leaves&7, which are a bright &#FFAA33orange-yellow&7; &66CCDDvariants&7 also exist in colors like &#88DDFFcyan-blue&7."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/tree.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/tree2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.313E8F6035C2E842.quest_subtitle: "Magical Material"
	quest.314084A1E2474F20.quest_desc: [
		"&6Alchemy Cauldron&r"
		""
		"&7The Alchemy Cauldron has a light level of 3.&r"
		""
		"&6Main Functions&r"
		"&7Boil &bbottled materials&r&7 in liquid form&r"
		"&7Craft &bspecific materials&r&7"
		"&7Brew &evanilla potions&r&7"
		"&7Revert &espell scrolls&r&7 back into ink&r"
		"&7Upgrade &eink quality&r&7"
		"&7Refine mod-specific &6elixirs&r&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Note: Does not have most vanilla cauldron properties (interaction with dripstone, rain filling, washing leather armor, etc.).&r"
		""
		"&6Interaction System&r"
		""
		"&6Storage Slots&r"
		"&7The cauldron has three storage types:&r"
		"&7&eWater Level&r&7: Four levels, corresponding to different liquid heights in the cauldron&r"
		"&7&eMaterial Slots&r&7: Four slots for various materials&r"
		"&7&ePotion Slots&r&7: Four slots for storing liquid products&r"
		""
		"&6Capacity Details&r"
		"&7Each water level stores one bottle of water (250mB), full level stores one bucket (1B)&r"
		"&7Each potion slot can store one &eink&r&7, &epotion&r&7, &6elixir&r&7, or other special liquid&r"
		"&7Each material slot can hold one material, which will float or sink in the cauldron&r"
		""
		"&6Basic Operations&r"
		""
		"&6Inserting Items&r"
		"&7Use a water bucket to fill the cauldron to level 4; each water bottle increases the level by 1&r"
		"&7Using a potion, elixir, or special liquid occupies one potion slot&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Materials include:&r"
		"&7Vanilla &ebrewing materials&r&7"
		"&7&eInk upgrade&r&7 materials (copper ingot, iron ingot, gold ingot, amethyst shard, etc.)&r"
		"&7Mod &6elixir&r&7 materials (dragon's breath, ender pearl, amethyst cluster, confession stone, etc.)&r"
		""
		"&6Collecting Items&r"
		"&7Empty hand right-click: Take one material from the material slots&r"
		"&7Empty bottle right-click: Prioritizes collecting from potion slots; if empty, collects a water bottle&r"
		"&7Automation support: Hopper input, observer state detection, dispenser automatic collection&r"
	]
	quest.31B0A26B1374A322.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starbird&r&7"
		"&7Small birds typically found only in Starlight Forests (excluding the Dense Starlight Forest variant). They are excellent fliers, very friendly, and adorable."
		"&7Come in two color variants: &#FF6B6Bred&r&7 and &#1E90FFblue&r&7. The &#FF6B6Bred variant&r&7 is far more common than the blue one."
		""
		"&7You can find &eStarbird Nests&r&7 generated nearby on Moonlight Trees."
		"&7Starbirds will &aclaim&r&7 a nearby Starbird Nest or &eStarbird House&r&7 for resting and breeding."
		"&7If they don't claim one promptly, place &8seeds&r&7 inside the nest/house, or try using the one they originally claimed."
		"&7Each Starbird Nest/House can hold up to &b2&r&7 adult Starbirds plus several chicks or eggs."
		""
		"&7Players need to hold &8seeds&r&7 and &afeed&r&7 two Starbirds by right-clicking."
		"&7After the breeding animation completes, one bird will fly to its claimed nest/house and lay an &eegg&r."
		"&7If a Starbird hasn't successfully claimed a nest/house, they may &cbe unable to breed&r."
		""
		"&7Eggs take time to hatch into chicks."
		"&7You can hold Shift and right-click the nest/house with an empty hand to take the egg."
		"&7Taken eggs can be placed back by holding Shift and right-clicking with the egg."
		"&7Note: If the nest/house is &cmined and destroyed&r&7, the eggs inside will &cspoil&r."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7Chicks cannot fly and stay in the nest/house until they mature."
		"&7Chicks that haven't left the nest/house &ccannot be interacted with&r&7 (e.g., fed seeds to speed growth)."
		"&7If needed, break the nest/house—the chicks will leave and become interactable."
		""
		"&7Using an axe with &bSilk Touch&r&7 to break the nest/house will &astore&r&7 all adult Starbirds, chicks, eggs, and seeds inside the dropped block."
		"&7When you place it again, everything is restored intact."
		""
		"&7Players can place any &8seeds&r&7 in a Starbird Nest/House (up to &b5&r at a time)."
		"&7When a claimed nest/house has seeds, the Starbird will &aconsume&r&7 them, fly toward you after leaving, and drop &b1–2&r&7 random items."
		""
		"&7The items Starbirds can give are drawn from a loot table."
		"&7Among them, &eStarfire (item)&r&7 is a &6unique drop&r from Starbirds."
		"&7This is a &6very important resource&r&7, serving as a core material for crafting some &6tier-2 equipment&r&7."
	]
	quest.31B0A26B1374A322.quest_subtitle: "Round and Fluffy"
	quest.31B0A26B1374A322.title: "Starbird"
	quest.31B78363809DB5AF.quest_desc: ["&7Functions like other &#CC99FFIron's Spells 'n Spellbooks staves&7. Effects are amplified even when held in the offhand. Amplification strength depends on materials."]
	quest.31B78363809DB5AF.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Amplification"
	quest.321BA6F89B9F2F5E.quest_desc: ["&7A rare but powerful &#66CCFFgem material&7. No attack speed reduction, extremely high durability. Limited quantity prevents mass production, but a single piece can handle most early enemies."]
	quest.321BA6F89B9F2F5E.quest_subtitle: "Heart of Stone"
	quest.32590328D9FB113D.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Trinkets can be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"combined and upgraded\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" like in Terraria. Some simple \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"movement trinkets\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" can speed up early exploration. A few trinkets have been \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"disabled\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" due to being too powerful (Flying Carpet: Why me?).\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Defeating the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Wither\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" has a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"chance\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"drop\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\" a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Demon Heart\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\". Using it increases your \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"accessory slots\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", but there is a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"usage limit\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.3280E06AA7147B28.quest_subtitle: "Can only be worn on the arm"
	quest.32EC8C6D17383BB2.quest_desc: ["&cQuanta (0%–100%): &r&7Fluctuates your final enchantment level, raising the upper limit while lowering the lower limit. Enchanting tables have a default of 15%."]
	quest.330C44884F7FF5A2.quest_desc: [
		"&7Acts as the terminal for the &#FFD700Furnace&7. Items can be input via &#66DDCChoppers&7 or other means for automation."
		""
		"&7Please note: Do not use the &#66CCFFcopper hopper&7 from the &#FF6666Extra Delight&7 mod to transport fluids into tanks, as it will cause &#FF6666fluid loss&7."
		""
		"&7If there are multiple &#66CCFFliquids&7 in the furnace, clicking on a specific &#66CCFFliquid&7 will move it to the bottom. The &#66CCFFdrain&7 will output the liquid at the bottom, so you can adjust the order to drain the desired liquid."
		""
		"&7If there's too much junk in the furnace, you can break the &#FFD700Smeltery Controller&7 to empty it completely."
	]
	quest.330C44884F7FF5A2.quest_subtitle: "Smelting Metals"
	quest.330C44884F7FF5A2.title: "Smeltery Controller"
	quest.332CE7AF2598E3F1.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.332CE7AF2598E3F1.quest_subtitle: "&4Audience"
	quest.3368D9266C268467.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.337B0F8208EA7383.quest_desc: [
		"&6Place Ink&r"
		"&7The quality of ink determines the quality of the scroll.&r"
		""
		"&6Place Paper&r"
		"&7Writing a scroll requires one piece of paper.&r"
		""
		"&6Place School Material&r"
		"&7&eSchool materials&r&7 determine the spell school.&r"
		"&7After placing the &eschool material&r&7, available spells to write will appear. Some spells may show a '?' icon—try using higher-tier ink to write them.&r"
		"&7Completed scrolls appear here. Note that materials are only consumed when you left-click to take the scroll.&r"
		""
		"Materials required for each school:"
		"&7Abyssal: Crystallized Coral / Crystallized Coral Fragment"
		"&6Blaze: Blaze Rod / Charred Bone"
		"&aEldritch: Note Block"
		"&3Frost: Ice / Frozen Bone"
		"&bLightning: Bottled Lightning"
		"&eHoly: Holy Pearl"
		"&5Ender: Ender Pearl"
		"&4Scarlet: Scarlet Essence Bottle"
		"&aEvocation: Emerald"
		"&2Nature: Poisonous Potato"
		"&1Eldritch: Echo Shard"
		"&dDreamscape: Infused Starstone"
	]
	quest.337B2D306A06DD6D.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When you \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-click\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" while holding it, a copy of the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Desert Eye\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" flies out from your hand towards the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Cursed Pyramid\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\", and the Desert Eye in your hand goes into a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The locating function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether or End\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", or in worlds without Cursed Pyramids.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.337C34C06A879409.quest_desc: [
		"This upgraded Sculk bookshelf channels power into Quanta, providing large amounts of &4Quanta&r without providing &5Arcana&r."
		"(Important Bookshelf)"
	]
	quest.337C34C06A879409.quest_subtitle: "Chaotic Power Surge"
	quest.337C34C06A879409.title: "Sculk Growth—Soul Trade"
	quest.339C3EB0CB099097.quest_desc: [
		"&7Every &6charm&r&7 I have made so far has found practical use. Naturally, there are side effects, and I waste a lot of time choosing the right charm. However, these charms can certainly isolate certain effects."
		"&7"
		"&7Thus begins &6Rune Crafting&r&7, using &dbrooches&r&7 and &erunes&r&7. The brooch serves only as a base core, worn close to the heart, symbolizing the inherent cost of pain in runic power."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Rune Crafting starts with inscribing &eRunes&r&7, which must be done on a &bRune Workbench&r&7—you should craft one first. The simplest entry-level brooch is the &dRune Brooch&r&7, which allows you to wear the runes you craft."
	]
	quest.339C3EB0CB099097.quest_subtitle: "The Needle That Strikes True"
	quest.339C3EB0CB099097.title: "Rune Crafting"
	quest.340694D4FDC5A098.quest_desc: ["&7Stably obtainable from a level 10 Enchanting Table. This material significantly boosts &#66CCFFOsmium Ingot's&7 base stats and provides a solid &#FFD700experience bonus&7. Well-rounded and cost-effective—an indispensable practical choice."]
	quest.340694D4FDC5A098.quest_subtitle: "Enchantment Amplifier"
	quest.346013B6D966C7F2.quest_desc: ["A hundred flowers bloom!"]
	quest.346013B6D966C7F2.quest_subtitle: "Typically unlocked after defeating Skeletron"
	quest.34AFC6414A805C2D.quest_desc: ["Restoration method: Eat Golden Apples, Enchanted Golden Apples, or Good Apples"]
	quest.34AFC6414A805C2D.quest_subtitle: "&cEach death reduces your maximum health"
	quest.34AFC6414A805C2D.title: "&c\"Death is the process of shedding one's self\""
	quest.34D446AE0315168C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click to deal damage to a target in front of you, &#FF6666ignoring invincibility frames&7."
		""
		"&7You can also use it as an &#66DDCCAxe&7, though it can't strip bark."
	]
	quest.34D446AE0315168C.quest_subtitle: "Zzzzzap"
	quest.34D5717A03B609A1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Spell Mastery&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Spell Mastery reflects simulated arcane energy, allowing me to charge &estaves&r&7 twice as fast.&r"
	]
	quest.34D5717A03B609A1.quest_subtitle: "Creating Destruction"
	quest.34F5839A32156AF0.title: "Discover the Acropolis"
	quest.350A83A36269F87B.quest_desc: ["&7Finally, I created an experimental substrate called \"&6Alchemical Dust&r&7.\" Its texture is close to solid animal fat under normal conditions, but with minimal force, it reveals powerful &aplasticity&r&7. This will surely be a useful &6material&r&7."]
	quest.350A83A36269F87B.quest_subtitle: "Clay Number Two"
	quest.3530C0A36931A1D6.quest_subtitle: "Demolition Miner"
	quest.3531099CA2E8832A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of the Tidal Catch&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of the Tidal Catch functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bTidal Catch&r&7 effect, equivalent to adding &eone level of Lure&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.3531099CA2E8832A.quest_subtitle: "Blessed Pulse"
	quest.35560F1953AD1C76.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.357A96DA2D1987CE.quest_subtitle: "Eternal Power"
	quest.35957B7E0ACF4060.quest_desc: [
		"&6Super Glue&r"
		""
		"&6Use&r"
		"&7This viscous medium adheres multiple blocks into a single unit, allowing dynamic structure components to recognize and assemble them as a unified &edynamic structure&7.&r"
		""
		"&6Gluing Blocks&r"
		"&7Right-click a block to set the start point, then right-click a second block. All blocks within the rectangular space defined by the two points will be glued, marked by a \"Super Glue\" entity.&r"
		"&7There must be actual block connections between the two selected points; otherwise the outline turns yellow and gluing fails.&r"
		"&7Holding Ctrl while aiming at a block highlights all glued blocks connected to it in blue.&r"
		"&7With Super Glue in the offhand, blocks placed from the main hand will automatically glue to the block clicked.&r"
		"&7When using a Schematicannon to print schematics containing Super Glue, ensure there is sufficient glue in the chest—it will be applied automatically.&r"
		""
		"&6Removing Glue&r"
		"&7Left-click any block within a glued area while holding Super Glue to delete the glue box and remove all associated adhesions.&r"
		""
		"&8A small dried glue stain marks the edge of the page, with a scribble: Easy to stick, easy to separate—just don't get it on your fingers.&r"
	]
	quest.35957B7E0ACF4060.quest_subtitle: "Start Gluing Now"
	quest.359B24E94B66AFA3.quest_desc: ["Spawns naturally upon entering the End. To resurrect the Ender Dragon, place 4 End Crystals around the portal."]
	quest.359B24E94B66AFA3.quest_subtitle: "Stage 3"
	quest.35AEBBC251933E78.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.35AEBBC251933E78.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.35B14862D3D903B2.quest_desc: ["&7One of the best common ores in Stage 1. Requires at least an &#66CCFFDiamond Pickaxe&7 to mine. Advantage is that it's usable immediately without extra processing."]
	quest.35B14862D3D903B2.quest_subtitle: "Excellent Base Material"
	quest.35C26E629284AC1A.quest_desc: [
		"&7You'll need to hunt Hoglins... An excellent handle material with balanced bonuses and a free Bastion trait—but not easy to get."
		""
		"&7The superior Bloody Hogskin has identical stats, with only an added Scarlet Spell Power bonus—not listed separately."
		""
		"Recommended parts: Handle, Plating"
	]
	quest.35C26E629284AC1A.quest_subtitle: "Why Does Pigskin Give Spell Power..."
	quest.35FDA2B4446874E0.quest_desc: ["Increases reach distance. No explanation needed for how strong that is."]
	quest.35FDA2B4446874E0.quest_subtitle: "Short Is Also Cute!"
	quest.35FFD854DFF94776.quest_desc: [
		"&7To overcome the limitation of wireless terminals losing connection over long distances..."
		""
		"Setting up wireless access points to extend signal coverage—creating a structure similar to a cell tower—may be a more viable solution."
	]
	quest.35FFD854DFF94776.quest_subtitle: "WiFi"
	quest.360AE4AB3B482FAC.quest_desc: [
		"&nCrime and Reputation System&r"
		""
		"&eTrading with villagers can slightly increase your reputation, up to a maximum of 25."
		""
		"&6Core Mechanics"
		"&b1. &3Crime Levels&r"
		"Crimes are categorized into three levels, affecting the player's relationship with villagers:"
		""
		"&aLight Crime&r: Slightly reduces reputation."
		""
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Significantly reduces reputation, and &cIron Golems or Guards&r will attack the player."
		""
		"&cHeavy Crime&r: Reputation drops to minimum, and &4Iron Golems will attack immediately&r."
		""
		"&b2. &3Trigger Conditions&r"
		"Crimes must be committed within &9protected structures&r (default: villages only)."
		"Villagers or guards must &6witness&r the crime (detection range affected by invisibility, sneaking, and light levels)."
		"&4Villagers have limited \"intelligence\"—breaking a block you placed yourself will still be considered theft."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Crime List"
		"&b1. &3Breaking Blocks&r"
		"&aLight Crime&r: Breaking crops, hay bales, lanterns, campfires, etc."
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Breaking chests, barrels, workstation blocks (e.g., cartography tables), beds."
		"&cHeavy Crime&r: Breaking bells."
		"&b2. &3Interacting with Blocks&r"
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Opening chests or barrels (considered attempted theft)."
		"&b3. &3Killing Creatures&r"
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Killing passive animals (pigs, cows, chickens, etc.) or villagers' pets (cats, horses, etc.)."
		"&b4. &3Bed-Related&r"
		"&aLight Crime&r: Kicking a villager out of their bed."
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Occupying a bed claimed by a villager."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Witnessing and Detection&r"
		"&bWitness Range&r"
		"Detection range is affected by the following factors:"
		""
		"&7Sneaking&r reduces the chance of being detected."
		"&5Low light levels or Invisibility potions&r can hide crimes."
		"&bWitness Reactions&r"
		"&cIron Golems and Guards&r will attack players who commit &eMedium&r or &cHeavy&r crimes (if witnessed)."
		"&aLight crimes&r only reduce reputation and do not trigger attacks."
		"&bOf course, you can also commit massacres out of sight of other villagers."
	]
	quest.360AE4AB3B482FAC.quest_subtitle: "Reputation"
	quest.3611F55056F7105F.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Gluttony\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When eating:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If health is not full: each point of saturation \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"restores 2 health\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If health is full: gain a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"random positive buff\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" for 30 seconds\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Other players within 5 blocks also \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"restore the same amount of hunger and saturation\",\"color\":\"yellow\"}]}"
	]
	quest.3611F55056F7105F.quest_subtitle: "Gluttony Erosion"
	quest.3611F55056F7105F.title: "Gluttony Erosion"
	quest.363CDDFE0664CBE2.quest_desc: [
		"&7Throw &#66FF66Beetroot Seeds&7 into the &#CC99FFVoid Well&7 to obtain them."
		"&8&mWho the hell came up with this recipe?&r&r"
		""
		"&7Can only be planted by right-clicking on a &#FFD700Skeleton Skull&7."
		""
		"&7After planting, breaking it will return the &#FFD700Skeleton Skull&7 and Brain Heart Cabbage Seeds."
		""
		"&7Brain Heart Cabbage crops grow over time. When fully mature, you can &#66CCFFright-click to harvest&7 directly."
		"&7Harvesting always drops &#FFAA335&7 Brain Heart Cabbage, with a very low chance of dropping &#FFAA331&7 seed."
		""
		"&7Bone Meal can also be used to &#66FF66accelerate growth&7."
		""
		"&7However, if you continue using Bone Meal on a fully mature crop with sufficient space above:"
		"&7it will grow into an &#66DDCCBrain Tree&7."
		""
		"&7Brain Heart Cabbage crops &#FF6666cannot naturally grow&7 into Brain Trees."
		""
		"&7After the Brain Tree grows, you must &#FFD700right-click&7 the crop again (to remove the stem) to allow it to resume normal growth (otherwise it stagnates)."
	]
	quest.363CDDFE0664CBE2.quest_subtitle: "Aaaah!!! Brain... Brain Is Shaking, Shaking, Shaking!!!"
	quest.364547BCDEFB8DDE.quest_desc: [
		"&6Portable Storage Interface&r"
		""
		"&7When a structure begins to rotate or slide, the golden interfaces attached to the &edynamic structure&r seem to awaken. As long as they detect another similar \"face\" looking at them from the right distance, they will pour out all items from their connected container in the agreed direction.&r"
		""
		"&6Making It Work&r"
		"&7This requires careful placement: two interfaces must be &cfacing each other&r&7, &cexactly 1 to 2 blocks apart&r&7. At least one must belong to a &edynamic structure&r—motion gives the transfer meaning.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Minor misalignments during docking don't matter—the transfer contract still holds.&r"
		""
		"&6Finer Control&r"
		"&7With &eItem Detectors&r&7 or &eStockpile Switches&r&7, you can monitor the contents. A simple Redstone signal &alocks&r&7 the interface in block form, making it ignore passing companions—though no visible change occurs.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Finally, remember the rule of elegance: &cexcessive speed or RPM&r&7 makes the handshake hasty and fails. If the receiver is stationary, pair it with &ehoppers&r&7 or &echutes&r—it needs a \"hand\" to catch the flowing gift.&r"
		""
		"&8A rough sketch of two interfaces facing each other is on this page, with a note: They hate jolts but love to dance.&r"
	]
	quest.364547BCDEFB8DDE.quest_subtitle: "An interface for exchanging items, allowing containers on dynamic structures to interact with the outside world."
	quest.3656700FBAEA1A3A.quest_desc: [
		"&7If you drop any item upwards, it will &#66CCFFslowly pass through&7 Insight Glass, effectively allowing for &#FFD700item filtering&7. Creatures &#FF6666cannot pass through&7 Insight Glass."
		""
		"How to use:"
		""
		"&7&#66FF66Whitelist Mode&7:"
		"&7First, place any item inside the Insight Glass."
		"&7Then, any item other than that one &#FF6666cannot pass through&7 the block."
		""
		"&7&#FF6666Blacklist Mode&7:"
		"&7When the Insight Glass receives a &#FFD700Redstone signal&7, it turns red and enters &#FF6666Blacklist Mode&7."
		"&7In Blacklist Mode, any item other than the one placed inside &#66CCFFcan pass through&7 the block."
		""
		"&7You can place a &#FFD700hopper&7 and a container (e.g., chest) below the block."
		"&7In &#66FF66Whitelist Mode&7, this setup will &#66CCFFonly collect&7 the specified item."
		"&7In &#FF6666Blacklist Mode&7, it will &#FF6666filter out&7 the specified item and collect everything else."
		""
		"&7Additionally, simply placing items inside Insight Glass gives a nice &#FFD700display case&7 feel for decorating your base."
	]
	quest.3656700FBAEA1A3A.quest_subtitle: "I Will Always Time You..."
	quest.366BD92ABD4B70A0.quest_desc: ["&7Obtainable via &#66CCFFfishing&7. Higher &#FFD700Luck&7 increases the catch rate. Has Stage 2-level stats."]
	quest.366BD92ABD4B70A0.quest_subtitle: "I Am the Sea King!"
	quest.36713AC6F99D301E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Sometimes, matter becomes charged with &6soul energy&r&7, even though the matter itself has no soul."
		""
		"&7This is the foundation of &6Essence Magic&r&7—animating soulless things with souls. The &6Soul Stone&r&7 is a mineral whose arcane properties surpass its physical ones. After refinement, it has many uses in my magical research. It radiates &dmagical energy&r&7 intensely."
	]
	quest.36713AC6F99D301E.quest_subtitle: "Metamorphosis"
	quest.369E5D74EA1CA624.quest_desc: ["&7Room for everything... maybe. Has massive cargo space for carrying everything you own. But compared to Sophisticated Backpacks, it falls far short—probably not qualified for the job."]
	quest.36DB408ECAE73BC5.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click to fire a &#CC99FFbarrage of spell projectiles&7. Dealing &#FFAA33fire damage&7 restores spell ammo."
		"&7Left-click attacks set enemies on &#FFAA33fire&7."
	]
	quest.36DB408ECAE73BC5.quest_subtitle: "A More Advanced Staff"
	quest.36DC8D2564CAC70C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Deepslate Gold Ore is a strange and useful metal. Its appearance is identical to &6Gold&r&7, but its properties are &ccompletely different&r&7."
		""
		"&7This ore can be found in &8Deepslate layers&r&7 underground, embedded within veins rich in &6Gold Ore&r&7."
	]
	quest.36DC8D2564CAC70C.quest_subtitle: "Infused with Arcane Energy"
	quest.37AB4AF2D44BDEB1.quest_desc: [
		"&5I have found a... structure&r&7. Its significance surpasses almost everything I have found before—it is proof that someone has already walked the path of arcane research."
		""
		"&7I call this well the \"&5Weeping Well&r&7,\" due to the &5aura of sorrow&r&7 it constantly emits. Inside the well is a small pool of... &5substance&r&7."
		""
		"&7I cannot quite determine what it is. Though it does not look like a liquid, its physical properties certainly do not make it a solid."
		""
		"&7Even the Arcane Tome in my pack glowed with a &6strange light&r&7, as if it had gained a will of its own and wanted to throw itself into the well."
	]
	quest.37AB4AF2D44BDEB1.quest_subtitle: "&zA Sudden Urge to Jump In"
	quest.37B8C9432DCC6DAD.quest_desc: ["&7In places like the Nether, combustible materials are a given, and &cBlazing Quartz&r&7 is one such substance. Like &8Coal&r&7, it can even be used to make &etorches&r&7. Though relatively &7commonplace&r&7, it has no shortage of uses."]
	quest.37B8C9432DCC6DAD.quest_subtitle: "Nether Coal"
	quest.37E8E57C588A9106.quest_subtitle: "Quickly add doors/gates"
	quest.37EDF1917F18D163.quest_desc: ["A rare but powerful all-rounder material that boosts every stat—downside is it's hard to obtain."]
	quest.37EDF1917F18D163.quest_subtitle: "All-Around Buff"
	quest.3801B9633700F23D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Wyrd Reconstruction&r"
		""
		"&7The burning star causes your decline.&r"
		"&7-&cWyrd Reconstruction&r&7 has a very long cooldown&r"
		"&7-&cArcane Resonance&r&7 is halved during cooldown&r"
		"&7-Harvesting essence consumes &chunger&r"
		""
		"&7The boundless power granted by Death itself.&r"
		"&7-&6Wyrd Reconstruction&r&7 prevents death&r"
		"&7-&6Wyrd Reconstruction&r&7 grants brief &ainvincibility&r&7 and quickly triggers &bessence harvest&r&7 effects&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_wyrd_reconstruction.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3801B9633700F23D.quest_subtitle: "Deceiving Fate"
	quest.3801B9633700F23D.title: "Pact of Wyrd Reconstruction"
	quest.38092862F38315D2.quest_subtitle: "A utility tool for finding the nearest Ancient City"
	quest.3834AAC7BBB3BDAF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Vitality&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Vitality compels the form to heal itself, increasing &aall healing&r&7 received by approximately one fifth.&r"
	]
	quest.3834AAC7BBB3BDAF.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Urges Mending"
	quest.3847F6BA291E6556.quest_desc: [
		"Through &binfusion&r upgrades, the Ocean Bookshelf gains even greater magical power, providing higher &aEterna&r and &5Arcana&r."
		"&l(Recommended Bookshelf)&r"
	]
	quest.3847F6BA291E6556.quest_subtitle: "Better Arcana and Eterna"
	quest.3847F6BA291E6556.title: "Magical Mystical Enhancement"
	quest.388B4D246EC83BC4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Lifeweaver"
		"&7All creatures deserve &acare&r&7.&r&cThe healing aura is indiscriminate—it heals both allies and enemies"
		"&7Rare is such &agenerosity&r&7: you share your will and flesh with others.&r&aConstantly regenerates health&r&aHealing is shared with nearby creatures"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_lifeweaver.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.388B4D246EC83BC4.quest_subtitle: "Giving to All"
	quest.388B4D246EC83BC4.title: "Pact of the Lifeweaver"
	quest.3890E1D60D9F389F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Defense&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Defense compels the form to hold its ground, increasing the wearer's &aarmor&r&7 by approximately one fifth.&r"
	]
	quest.3890E1D60D9F389F.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Urges Resilience"
	quest.38AC7ED986231005.quest_desc: ["&7Provides good damage bonuses and experience gain early on. A cost-effective choice for the early game."]
	quest.38AC7ED986231005.quest_subtitle: "I Have a FOMO Table"
	quest.38C6EDEB38BC8B99.quest_subtitle: "Enable natural Eternal Gate spawning in the End"
	quest.39138773ED14B1BA.quest_desc: [
		"They solved Cod's biggest problem since starting the pack!"
		""
		"And also... why are there so many bugs?"
	]
	quest.39138773ED14B1BA.quest_subtitle: "Balance Design + Contributor"
	quest.396C3E0A51A61D92.quest_desc: ["&7Right-click to &#FFD700slam&7 the ground, dealing area damage. If the user is below &FF6666half health&7, adds &FFAA33fire damage&7."]
	quest.396C3E0A51A61D92.quest_subtitle: "Bang!"
	quest.3983E32C1CEC4DAA.quest_desc: ["If you use a scythe, Soul Dew's scythe bonuses can effectively boost early-game damage."]
	quest.3983E32C1CEC4DAA.quest_subtitle: "Cheap and Effective"
	quest.39980DF0631D9B6C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Profane Ascetic&r"
		""
		"&7Your devotion to corruption consumes your form.&r"
		"&7-&cSaturation and hunger&r&7 cannot restore health&r"
		"&7-The geas only permits the consumption of &8rotten food&r&7; eating anything else causes &cdamage&r"
		""
		"&7Corruption becomes your closest companion.&r"
		"&7-&6Gluttony&r&7 becomes &6Test of Faith&r"
		"&7-&6Test of Faith&r&7 increases &ahealing&r&7 received and spawns &blocusts&r&7 when healing&r"
		"&7-&6Test of Faith&r&7 lasts significantly longer&r"
		"&7-Consuming &8rotten food&r&7 restores health&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_profane_ascetic.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.39980DF0631D9B6C.quest_subtitle: "Finding Beauty in Dross"
	quest.39980DF0631D9B6C.title: "Pact of the Profane Ascetic"
	quest.39AB32E04D04B64F.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.39AB32E04D04B64F.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.39EB3B61CB5E3E73.quest_subtitle: "Lower defense than other armor, but specializes in spell-related stats"
	quest.39F72CD10646574F.quest_desc: ["&7Searching for specific enchantments among hundreds is like finding a needle in a haystack. Type-restricted enchanted books significantly improve this—these books only have affinity for specific categories of enchantments, making them an excellent way to acquire targeted enchantments."]
	quest.39F72CD10646574F.quest_subtitle: "Practical Enchantments"
	quest.3A08D5D6D65FF6F2.quest_desc: [
		"&7The catacomb contains multiple branching paths and numerous &#66CCFFundead creature&7 spawners. A few rooms contain &#FF6666traps&7—be careful when opening chests."
		""
		"&7The &#FF6666Dead King&7 slumbers on the throne in the central hall, which also contains a spawner that continuously generates &#66CCFFzombies&7. Prepare before the battle, and right-click the sleeping &#FF6666Dead King&7 to awaken him."
		""
		"&mWait, why don't I just sneak attack him?&r"
	]
	quest.3A08D5D6D65FF6F2.quest_subtitle: "Pry It Open (∠・ω< )⌒★"
	quest.3A08D5D6D65FF6F2.title: "Catacombs"
	quest.3A3892760CA0F960.quest_desc: ["Allows any weapon to trigger soul harvesting, freeing you from being locked to scythes. If you want to build around the soul system without being weapon-restricted, this material is tailor-made for you."]
	quest.3A3892760CA0F960.quest_subtitle: "Soul Catalyst"
	quest.3A5D807E30DF3E8C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Whatever your profession or goals, &cRedstone&r&7 is an indispensable aid."
		"&7Building &cpiston doors&r&7 is not exclusive to engineers. Today, I too have contributed to Redstone's advancement."
		""
		"&7By etching the pulse of &eelemental essences&r&7 into &bSpirit-Fire-treated&r&7 &6copper matrices&r&7, four interesting &cRedstone devices&r&7 can be crafted."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Signal Wave Delayer"
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Delayer&7 maintains output strength equal to input strength. When input strength drops, it prolongs the previous output for a set duration."
		""
		"&7Can be placed horizontally; the ◉ side is the input, the opposite side is the output."
		""
		"&7When &#66FF66input strength&7 > &#FF8844output strength&7, creates a planned tick with &e1&7 Redstone-tick delay."
		"&7When &#66FF66input strength&7 < &#FF8844output strength&7, creates a planned tick based on its frequency."
		"&7On that planned tick, &#FF8844output strength&7 changes to the current &#66FF66input strength&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Signal Wave Interrupter"
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Interrupter&7 functions like an adjustable-delay Repeater, maintaining output strength equal to input strength."
		""
		"&7Can be placed horizontally; the ◉ side is the input, the opposite side is the output."
		"&7Total delay = frequency + (&e1&7 Redstone tick). If input strength is still equal to the pending strength after &e1&7 Redstone tick, output is not updated."
		""
		"&7When &#66FF66input strength&7 ≠ &#FF8844output strength&7:"
		"&7&#FF8844output strength&7 = &#88DDFFpending strength&7: creates a planned tick with &e1&7 Redstone-tick delay. On that tick, updates &#88DDFFpending strength&7 to the current &#66FF66input strength&7;"
		""
		"&7Otherwise, creates a planned tick based on its frequency. On that tick, updates &#FF8844output strength&7 to &#88DDFFpending strength&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Signal Wave Continuator"
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Continuator&7 slowly increases or decreases output strength toward input strength."
		""
		"&7Can be placed horizontally; the ◉ side is the input, the opposite side is the output."
		"&7When input strength ≠ output strength, creates a planned tick based on its frequency. On that tick, updates output:"
		""
		"&#66FF66input&7 > &#FF8844output&7: output strength +&e1&7;"
		"&#66FF66input&7 < &#FF8844output&7: output strength -&e1&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Signal Wave Generator"
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Generator&7 functions like a Redstone clock, sending pulses at intervals. During a pulse, it inverts input strength; at other times, it maintains output strength equal to input strength."
		""
		"&7Can be placed horizontally; the ◉ side is the input, the opposite side is the output."
		"&7When placed, creates a planned tick with &e1&7-second delay."
		""
		"&7Cycle = frequency + (&e5&7 game ticks):"
		""
		"&7Normal: creates a planned tick based on its frequency;"
		"&7Inverted: creates a planned tick with &e5&7 game-tick delay."
		""
		"&7On that tick, updates output strength: normal -> &#FF8844output strength&7 = &#66FF66input strength&7; inverted -> &#FF8844output strength&7 = &e15&7 - &#66FF66input strength&7."
	]
	quest.3A5D807E30DF3E8C.quest_subtitle: "Signal Modulation"
	quest.3A5D807E30DF3E8C.title: "Signal Wave Crafting"
	quest.3A5DD56949CF4827.quest_desc: [
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/key_reload.png width:150 height:40 align:center}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Of course, due to some mod reasons, please manually set the <Key Combination> key group to the B key."
	]
	quest.3A5DD56949CF4827.quest_subtitle: "The modpack's default keybinds are already configured—just find the key bindings menu and click (Reset All Keys)"
	quest.3B0E439056FB5B0B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Backpacks can be upgraded with various &#66DDCCupgrades&7. The number of upgrade slots depends on the backpack's &#66CCFFtier&7. A &#66CCFFDiamond Backpack&7 has &#FFAA33five&7 upgrade slots, while a &#CC99FFNetherite Backpack&7 has &#FFAA33seven&7. Upgrading your backpack is essential for adding more upgrades."
		""
		"Common upgrades are listed on the right."
	]
	quest.3B0E439056FB5B0B.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade Your Backpack!"
	quest.3B3B3605F4F0AC43.quest_desc: ["Ultimately, just not enough pull..."]
	quest.3B3B3605F4F0AC43.quest_subtitle: "Some Item Textures Provided"
	quest.3B7226A9387FD816.quest_subtitle: "Cursed Flower"
	quest.3BB2417F411ABDDE.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"An important crafting material\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If you want to craft some \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"BOSS summoning items\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" or some \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"novel materials\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", you will definitely need this.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.3BB2417F411ABDDE.quest_subtitle: "First Steps"
	quest.3BBDB096C8442119.quest_desc: ["&7Hold right-click to charge up, then release to deal &6massive damage&7 to all entities in front of you."]
	quest.3BBDB096C8442119.quest_subtitle: "I Am Fire!"
	quest.3C4F9B874C336EB6.quest_desc: [
		"# &cBUG Feedback Channels &r"
		""
		"### &eFeedback Methods &r"
		"&6➤ &fReport in the official Discord/group chat"
		"&6➤ &fSubmit an Issue on GitHub"
		""
		"&6Cod will handle it as soon as possible!!!"
		""
		"### &9Official Links &r"
		"&6▪ &bGitHub Issues: "
		"&fhttps://github.com/DrowningFish233/Reverie-Foundry/issues"
		"&6▪ &bMC百科 Page: "
		"&fhttps://www.mcmod.cn/modpack/907.html"
		""
		"### &3Notes &r"
		"&7- When reporting, please provide:"
		"  &8• &fDetailed reproduction steps"
		"  &8• &fRelevant screenshots/logs"
		"  &8• &fModpack version info"
	]
	quest.3C4F9B874C336EB6.quest_subtitle: "Oh no!"
	quest.3CCFC8763640AC83.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Arm&r"
		""
		"&6Moving Items&r"
		"&7The Mechanical Arm is the most flexible logistics system in Create, capable of moving items between any two points within its working range.&r"
		"&7It requires gear power—higher RPM means faster operation. Its working range is roughly a &c5&r&7-block radius sphere (3D space).&r"
		"&7The arm can move up to a full stack of items at a time.&r"
		""
		"&6Placement&r"
		"&7To use the Mechanical Arm, set input and output targets. The arm picks up from inputs and deposits to outputs:&r"
		"&7Hold the arm and right-click a location. Right-click once to set as input (blue), twice to set as output (yellow). Multiple inputs or outputs can be set. After setting, place the arm. Targets outside its range are automatically removed. Left-click to cancel selection.&r"
		"&7Note: The arm can only target '&eopen storage spaces&r&7' such as Belts, Depots, Chutes, etc. Vanilla containers like hoppers and chests cannot be targeted.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7All valid targets (red markers are output-only):&r"
		"&7Belt, Chute (Smart Chute), Depot, Weighted Ejector, Basin, Mechanical Crafter, Millstone, Deployer, Powered Mechanical Saw, Jukebox, Train Station, Packager, Repackager, Blaze Burner (empty), Crushing Wheel Controller, Composter, Respawn Anchor, input-mode Create Funnel, Campfire (Soul Campfire).&r"
		"&7Placing the arm on the bottom face of a block inverts it.&r"
		""
		"&6Distribution&r"
		"&7If the arm has multiple outputs, you can set distribution logic via the panel on the side. Right-click and hold to configure.&r"
	]
	quest.3CDB29B0059175A8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Familiar Soul&r"
		"&7The core material for manifesting a familiar into the world. Obtained by capturing &8Lost Souls&r&7 with an empty bottle on the &6Origin Island&r&7. Bottled souls can be released back into the wild.&r"
	]
	quest.3CDB29B0059175A8.quest_subtitle: "Lost Souls"
	quest.3D277D76C151604A.quest_desc: ["&7Comes with the Eternal trait—completely removes durability concerns. Solid base stats make it a reliable and hassle-free choice for long-term use."]
	quest.3D277D76C151604A.quest_subtitle: "Timeless Hold"
	quest.3D485A80778437EF.quest_desc: [
		"&aEterna (0–100): &r&7Determines the maximum enchantment level the enchanting table can provide. Max enchantment level = Eterna level."
		""
		"&7The vanilla Eterna cap is 30, so vanilla bookshelves also have a cap of 30. To achieve higher-level enchantments, you need the power of Apotheosis bookshelves..."
		""
		"&7The higher the Eterna, the better the enchantment results, far exceeding vanilla's enchantment level limits."
	]
	quest.3D65B82D6967E302.quest_desc: [
		"&7Compared to storage blocks, &#66DDCCStorage Disks&7 are a more space-efficient design. A &#66DDCCDisk Drive&7 occupies only one block but can hold up to eight &#66DDCCStorage Disks&7."
		""
		"&7&#66DDCCDisks&7 are crafted from &#66DDCCStorage Components&7 and &#66DDCCDisk Housings&7. &#66DDCCStorage Components&7 start at &#FFAA331k&7 and are upgraded upward. Crafting a &#FFAA3364k&7 storage component requires &#FFAA3327&7 1k components, &#FFAA3336&7 Basic Processors, &#FFAA3312&7 Improved Processors, and &#FFAA334&7 Advanced Processors—a significant amount of &#66CCFFQuartz&7."
		""
		"&7Since the &#FF6666Nether&7 is not recommended for early entry, it's better to mine natural &#66CCFFQuartz Geodes&7 deep in the Overworld with a &#FFD700Fortune&7 enchantment. With &#FFD700Fortune III&7, one geode can supply enough quartz for a &#FFAA3364k&7 disk. Alternatively, you can loot structures with high &#FFD700Luck&7 from &#66CCFFLapis Lazuli&7 components—some structure chests can yield a full stack of &#66CCFFQuartz&7 per chest with high &#FFD700Luck&7."
		""
		"&7Hold a &#66DDCCDisk&7 and Shift + Right-click to extract the &#66DDCCStorage Component&7 from it. The same applies to &#66DDCCStorage Blocks&7."
	]
	quest.3D65B82D6967E302.quest_subtitle: "Plug and Play"
	quest.3D65B82D6967E302.title: "Disk Storage"
	quest.3D71CE179BBC6433.quest_desc: [
		"&6Tower Squid Air Bladder&r&7"
		"&7Dropped by &#1E90FFTower Squid&r&7 upon death; &r"
		""
		"&7Cannot be used as a substitute for &8vanilla ink sacs&r&7 in crafting recipes. &r"
	]
	quest.3DEBEF47CB42C180.quest_desc: [
		"As the fuel's heat value increases, the maximum achievable temperature also rises."
		""
		"&eThe left side shows the types of fuel that can be used.&r"
	]
	quest.3DEBEF47CB42C180.quest_subtitle: "Heating by Consumption"
	quest.3DFF41190EEED602.quest_desc: ["Yes, you can have Creative Items."]
	quest.3DFF41190EEED602.quest_subtitle: "Infinite Storage"
	quest.3E76BD1AEDBFF421.quest_desc: ["&7Good ranged damage boost. The downsides are negligible in weapon crafting. A clean and efficient ranged amplifier."]
	quest.3E76BD1AEDBFF421.quest_subtitle: "Celestial Power"
	quest.3E8F381CC8783800.quest_desc: ["Provides solid attack damage and armor bonuses. One piece might not seem like much, but you can apply multiple layers—and that adds up fast."]
	quest.3E8F381CC8783800.quest_subtitle: "Now You Know Why the Warden Is So Tanky"
	quest.3F1E59D47DB55A82.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.3F1E59D47DB55A82.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.3F36E58182CFD1EA.quest_desc: [
		"&7Increases &#66CCFFLightning Spell Power&7 by &FFAA3310%&7 of &#CC99FFmagic damage&7, capped at base attack × &FFAA331.5&7."
		""
		"&7Right-click to cast &#66CCFFIonic Slash&7. Every &FFAA335&7 attack damage increases spell level by &FFAA331&7 and mana cost by &FFAA3315&7. Cooldown: &FFAA3310/attack speed&7 seconds."
	]
	quest.3F36E58182CFD1EA.quest_subtitle: "Zzzzap"
	quest.3F3E9DDBDE86C19C.quest_desc: [
		"&#55D5D5Sanity &7changes based on &#66CCFFplayer traits&7, &#CC99FFweapon traits&7, damage taken, &#55D5D5player status&7, and many other factors. You can also use certain items to &#66FF66adjust&7 &#55D5D5Sanity&7."
		""
		"&7Without any &#888888miscellaneous traits&7:"
		""
		"&#FF6666Conditions that decrease Sanity:&7"
		"&7When your status worsens, &#55D5D5Sanity &7begins to drain:"
		""
		"&7Health below &#FFAA33&l30%&7: &#55D5D5Sanity &7continuously decreases"
		"&7Health below &#FF6633&l15%&7: &#55D5D5Sanity &7drain rate doubles"
		""
		"&7Taking heavy damage directly reduces &#55D5D5Sanity:"
		""
		"&7Single hit exceeding &#FFAA3350%&7 of max health: &#FF6666Lose 10 Sanity"
		"&7Single hit exceeding &#FFAA3330%&7 of max health: &#FF6666Lose 5 Sanity"
		""
		"&#66FF66Conditions that increase Sanity:"
		"&7When well-fed (&#FFDD44saturation &7≥ &#66FF6616&7) and healthy (above &#66FF8875%&7 health), &#55D5D5Sanity &7slowly recovers."
		""
		"&#66CCFFTrait Effects:"
		"&7Your &#66CCFFplayer traits&7 and &#CC99FFweapon traits&7 can alter the rate of &#55D5D5Sanity&7 drain or recovery, depending on the trait types you have."
		""
		"&#CC99FFItem Adjustments:"
		"&7Some items can directly &#66FF66restore or reduce&7 &#55D5D5Sanity&7, or temporarily change the rate of &#55D5D5Sanity&7 change."
	]
	quest.3F3E9DDBDE86C19C.quest_subtitle: "&zAdvanced Understanding"
	quest.3F3E9DDBDE86C19C.title: "Sanity Effects and Changes"
	quest.3F4F2D1D8EC995BA.quest_desc: [
		"&7A Redstone Comparator allows the spawner to be controlled by Redstone."
		"&7With this modification, the spawner only operates when receiving a Redstone signal. This provides more direct control for automated mob farms."
	]
	quest.3F4F2D1D8EC995BA.quest_subtitle: "Redstone Spawner"
	quest.3F65163CBB21A321.quest_desc: [
		"&7Should I avoid his wrath?"
		""
		"&7From the &#FFD700Gatekeeper&7, I learned that the &#FF6666Dead King&7 is planning something. There's no running from it—a &#FF6666Dead King&7 that drops loot is a good &#FF6666Dead King&7."
		""
		"&7Before challenging the &#FF6666Dead King&7, you can also try defeating other &#FFAA33Stage 1 Bosses&7 to get materials for further gear upgrades. Boss stages can be viewed in the &#66CCFFBoss List&7."
		""
		"&7Although the &#FF6666Dead King&7 primarily uses spells, since &#FFD700Iron's Spells is essentially physical&7, you don't need to prepare specifically for magic resistance—regular armor works fine."
	]
	quest.3F65163CBB21A321.quest_subtitle: "Sprint, Charge!"
	quest.3F65163CBB21A321.title: "Preparation"
	quest.3F95B455EACD5B91.quest_desc: ["Provides all-around bonuses for tools."]
	quest.3F95B455EACD5B91.quest_subtitle: "All-Around Boost"
	quest.3FC49807F1694CE5.quest_desc: ["&7Comes with the Eternal trait—completely removes durability anxiety. Extremely solid stats that offer both convenience and power—an ideal choice for those who want both ease and strength."]
	quest.3FC49807F1694CE5.quest_subtitle: "Eternal Power"
	quest.3FD324391F9D0115.quest_desc: ["This summoning ritual can only be performed in the Golem Forge."]
	quest.3FD324391F9D0115.quest_subtitle: "Starlight Golem"
	quest.3FD324391F9D0115.title: "Summoning Ritual"
	quest.3FD3535AE922834F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Defeating bosses increases the player's (personal) rank level."
		""
		"Consuming a \"&bGood Apple&r\" or defeating the final boss reduces the rank by 1 level."
		""
		"&bRank affects:"
		"&7The rarity of Silent Gear equipment items obtained from equipment bags."
		""
		"&7The Champion spawn rate and the probability of encountering higher-tier Champions."
	]
	quest.3FD3535AE922834F.quest_subtitle: "&zYou believe you're ready to face the challenges ahead, and most importantly, you feel Lady Luck is smiling upon you. It's time to begin your own adventure!"
	quest.3FD839536F2A224B.quest_desc: [
		"&ePure energy condensed from starlight."
		"&6Burns at an astonishing rate, processing your materials extremely quickly."
		""
		"⚡ Speed: 1.5x | ♨ Temperature: 3000 | ⏳ Consumption: 0.4"
		""
		"&aTip&r&7: &f♨ &r&7Temperature determines the tier of materials that can be processed, ⚡ Speed affects processing time, and ⏳ Consumption represents fuel longevity."
	]
	quest.3FD839536F2A224B.quest_subtitle: "Rapid Combustion"
	quest.3FFA3C2B5E1FC24A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Cursed Garden&r"
		"&7A large surface structure guarded by the &cLunar Monstrosity&r&7."
		""
		"&7The entire Cursed Garden is a &8large maze&r built from tall walls."
		"&7Each side of the outer wall has a &8narrow entrance&r&7, while the central endpoint is a flat &aspacious area&r."
		""
		"&7All &6loot chests&r&7 are scattered along the maze corridors. Both the corridors and the endpoint are filled with numerous &#8FBC8FVine Wraiths&r&7 guarding the area."
		"&7You can use the &eEye of Seeking&r&7 to locate this structure."
		""
		"&4The Lunar Monstrosity has high damage reduction until ignited."
	]
	quest.3FFA3C2B5E1FC24A.quest_subtitle: "Once a lush garden, now corrupted by curses."
	quest.3FFA3C2B5E1FC24A.title: "Cursed Garden"
	quest.4015BC05F1AAD9EB.quest_subtitle: "Used for Casting Rods"
	quest.4073FA79B270F976.quest_desc: [
		"&7An excellent survival material. Its armor itself is somewhat weak, but it works well as an alloy component."
		""
		"&7The Soul Catalyst trait provides significant soul shield-related bonuses and increases scythe proficiency."
		""
		"&7The Soul Shield is an independent damage-reduction mechanic. Without bonuses, it heavily reduces magic damage and offers moderate physical damage reduction. Scythe proficiency directly increases scythe attack multipliers."
		""
		"&7The Soul Strike trait allows non-scythe kills to drop essences—great for collecting souls without being locked to a scythe."
		""
		"&7Soul-Stained Steel Plating can also be used as a lining material, but instead of providing a soul shield, it increases the geas limit."
		""
		"Recommended part: Any armor slot"
	]
	quest.4073FA79B270F976.quest_subtitle: "Stack That Armor and Move On"
	quest.40AAE3AB0A6C05DF.quest_desc: [
		"Initially, the pack was just for playing with friends. Later, the vision grew grander... and so, Reverie Foundry was born."
		""
		"P.S. Great Manager!"
	]
	quest.40AAE3AB0A6C05DF.quest_subtitle: "Some Writing + Some Planning + Contributor"
	quest.40C75417213642DC.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Passive Abilities"
		""
		"&7Damage Limit:"
		"&7In the broken state, the Starlight Golem cannot take more than &#FFAA332/3&7 of its max health in a single instance of damage."
		""
		"&7Invincibility (Phase 1 only): The Starlight Golem is &#FF6666immune to all damage&7 unless in the broken state."
		""
		"&7Energy (Phase 1 only):"
		"&7The Starlight Golem can hold up to &#FFAA33100&7 energy;"
		"&7Each attack consumes some energy. Even if remaining energy is insufficient, the golem can still use the attack (except at 0 energy);"
		"&7Energy cannot go negative. At 0, the golem immediately enters a charging state;"
		"&7Each time a Cryo Tube is thrown at the golem, its energy decreases by &#FF6666-3&7."
		""
		"&7Energy Block Charging (Charging State)"
		"&7The Starlight Golem always starts in the charging state;"
		"&7It enters the charging state every &#FFAA3390 seconds&7 thereafter;"
		"&7During charging, it cannot attack, and four surrounding energy blocks continuously charge it;"
		"&7During charging, it regenerates &#66FF660.4&7 health per second;"
		"&7After charging, the golem regains &#FFAA33100&7 energy;"
		"&7Players must (right-click / shoot projectiles) &#FF6666extinguish&7 all energy blocks charging the golem; otherwise, it remains invincible;"
		"&7Once all are extinguished: the golem enters the broken state."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Broken State"
		"&7Occurs simultaneously with the charging state. After entering the broken state, the golem is &#FF6666no longer immune&7 to damage until the charging state ends;"
		"&7After taking up to &#FFAA337&7 instances of damage, the golem forcibly ends both charging and broken states, resuming attacks;"
		"&7The broken state lasts at most &#FFAA3360 seconds&7;"
		"&7If the golem enters Phase 2, the current charging and broken states are forcibly ended."
		""
		"&7Phase 2"
		"&7When the golem's remaining health is ≤&#FFAA3320%&7:"
		"&7It loses its invincibility passive and no longer switches between charging and broken states;"
		"&7From this point, players can attack the golem normally;"
		"&7In this phase, the golem's body constantly trembles and sparks, occasionally flashing red (visual only—no self-damage)."
	]
	quest.40C75417213642DC.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.41555B67D70627EB.quest_subtitle: "Who Can Kill Me!"
	quest.417E7341644D16C8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Rune Exploitation"
		"&7Your soul has its limits.&r&cEach rune equipped reduces healing received, armor, armor toughness, and magic resistance by one twentieth"
		"&7A part of your soul becomes rune slots.&r&aGrants two rune slots"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_rune_exploitation.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.417E7341644D16C8.quest_subtitle: "Honoring the Old Pact"
	quest.417E7341644D16C8.title: "Pact of Rune Exploitation"
	quest.41968B5035595DD8.quest_desc: [
		"&7In Apotheosis, Silk Touch has been enhanced. When mining a spawner with a Silk Touch pickaxe, it consumes 150 durability and drops the spawner. This allows players to collect spawners and place them in more convenient locations."
		""
		"&7Additionally, Apotheosis lets players adjust various spawner attributes using different materials, maximizing a single spawner's potential."
		""
		"Note: The &eCapture&r enchantment has been disabled. You must use the &eMystic Ender Lead&r to change the mob in a spawner. This means empty spawners obtained before defeating the &cPrimordial Fire-Receiver&r are effectively useless—it's better to modify spawners in place and use Waystones for travel."
		""
		"&7Hold Ctrl to view detailed spawner information."
	]
	quest.41968B5035595DD8.quest_subtitle: "Silk Touch Mega Buff"
	quest.41968B5035595DD8.title: "How to Obtain Spawners"
	quest.41A6E2C475A1E6F5.quest_desc: ["&7A Pro version of the biplane—larger than the original, but gains the ability to land on water. This makes takeoff and landing safer when water is plentiful (lakes are everywhere, but runways are not)."]
	quest.41E17B4557322ADD.quest_desc: ["&7Damage scales with the player's current &FFAA33movement speed&7."]
	quest.41E17B4557322ADD.quest_subtitle: "Long, Pointy Stick"
	quest.4213B825EDC1B32D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune Brooch&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune Brooch is the simplest and most unadorned brooch. It symbolizes the power of added cost—or bloodied hands grasping thorny enlightenment. When worn, it removes a slot reserved for &cring&r&7 power from my hands, granting me the &aability&r&7 to inscribe one rune on each palm.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Glass Brooch&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune Brooch works well, but hands are not the only vessels for symbolic power. Through the Glass Brooch, I can channel it into my blood, trading a portion of &cvitality&r&7 for the &aability&r&7 to inscribe two runes on my chest.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Ornate Brooch&r"
		""
		"&7Brooches symbolize sacrifice. But in the eyes of others, such sacrifice may seem abstract or even absurd. A necklace is not much different from a belt. By stripping away notions of fashion and propriety, I can place a belt's &apower&r&7 around my neck.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Gluttony Brooch&r"
		""
		"&7Sacrifice is not limited to the physical—spiritual sacrifice counts too. The Gluttony Brooch deprives me of &csatiety&r&7, leaving me constantly hungry even after a full meal. In exchange, my gaunt abdomen gains the space for an extra &abelt&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.4213B825EDC1B32D.quest_subtitle: "Gaining Rune Slots at a Cost—One Source of Rune Slots"
	quest.4276FE7E4037AC05.quest_desc: [
		"&7A relatively common structure in the Nether."
		"&7At the center of the battlefield is a trial spawner that generates Ancient Knights. The surrounding area has scattered armor pieces that, when mined, have a chance to drop &6Netherite Scraps&7 and spawn Ancient Knights."
		""
		"&7Once you can defeat Ancient Knights, this is a convenient source of Netherite, and the &6Ash Essence&7 dropped here is also an important material."
	]
	quest.4276FE7E4037AC05.quest_subtitle: "Battle, Fun"
	quest.4276FE7E4037AC05.title: "Ancient Battlefield"
	quest.429669316E4CF3A9.quest_subtitle: "Provides both armor and minor spell stats—very popular"
	quest.42A270AF2F03EE3B.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When you \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-click\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" while holding it, a copy of the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Eye\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" flies out from your hand towards the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Ancient Factory\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\", and the Mechanical Eye in your hand goes into a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The locating function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether or End\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", or in worlds without Ancient Factories.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.42EE3883528EA312.quest_desc: ["Speeds up the smelting furnace's processing speed."]
	quest.42EE3883528EA312.quest_subtitle: "One Step Ahead"
	quest.42F6170490C96218.quest_subtitle: "Unrivaled"
	quest.42F6170490C96218.title: "Kill Champion Creatures x1000"
	quest.4342761A11C8B0C0.quest_desc: [
		"&7Has higher &FFAA33critical damage&7 than other weapons."
		""
		"&7When dual-wielded, hold right-click to perform a &FFD700smash&7, damaging nearby entities."
	]
	quest.4342761A11C8B0C0.quest_subtitle: "Critical!"
	quest.43B69EBAF5DCC756.quest_desc: ["&7A tool that works as an &#66DDCCPickaxe&7, &#66DDCCAxe&7, and &#66DDCCShovel&7 all in one."]
	quest.43B69EBAF5DCC756.quest_subtitle: "All-Purpose Tool"
	quest.43DA0D2247FEE7E0.quest_desc: ["Good early-game mana regeneration trait. Worth wearing even just for the attack bonus."]
	quest.43DA0D2247FEE7E0.quest_subtitle: "Garbage In, Garbage Out"
	quest.43DDDB9D9BA35A28.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FF8844Soulbound Brazier&r&7 is used to declare or revoke geases."
		""
		"&7Place the required materials loosely in the &#FF8844Soulbound Brazier&r&7, then light it with &#FFAA33Spirit Fire&r&7 to begin the ritual."
		""
		"&7The ritual lasts &e30&7 seconds, with no limit on participants. Each second, it adds all creatures within &e4&7 blocks holding &#CC6666Weakness&7 to the geas. Players can right-click the brazier to join without needing the &#CC6666Weakness&7 effect."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7When joining a geas, the creature takes &e25%&7 of its max health as damage, type &#CC6666malum:karmic&7, reducible by armor and Protection enchantments, ignoring post-hit invincibility."
		"&7After the ritual ends, all participants gain the geas effect. Each creature can hold at most two geases at once. Geases are soul-bound and persist even after death."
		""
		"&7If already holding &etwo geases&r&7, no new geas is gained, and the creature takes &e50%&7 of its max health as damage, type &#CC6666malum:karmic&7."
		"&7To revoke a geas, light the brazier with &#6666CCProfane Flame&r&7 instead of &#FFAA33Spirit Fire&r&7. The process is otherwise identical. If a creature does not have the corresponding geas, it takes &e50%&7 of its max health as damage."
		""
		"&7Players can view declared geases in the accessory slot—they cannot be removed."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6As shown:"
		"&r{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/malum.png width:115 height:140 align:center}"
		"&7&#66CCFFblue area&7: required &#66FF99essences&7;"
		"&7&#FF6666red area&7: required items;"
		"&7&#FFAA33orange area&7: required main item."
		""
		"&7Place these in the brazier, add &r&zSpirit Fire&r&7, and right-click the brazier to begin the geas declaration ritual."
		"&eDuring the ritual, creatures in a weakened state will also be declared into the geas.&r"
	]
	quest.43DDDB9D9BA35A28.quest_subtitle: "Power at a Cost"
	quest.43DDDB9D9BA35A28.title: "Geases and Other Pacts"
	quest.4432A2327732E7FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Corruption—&cthat which can destroy and damage&r&7. The creations of directionless rituals have many strange properties; I wish to classify them."
		"&7"
		"&7A simple explanation would be that it is just another form of energy that infects the world, but that is clearly incorrect. Corruption is harmless—at least in itself. It is merely a... &7substance&r&7."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Corruption Study: Substance"
		"&7The &bDirectionless Ritual&r&7, as its name suggests, is a random process. It transmutes matter, but the results are fickle. The powder it produces is a random heap of unrelated fragments, and it smells quite foul. Not recommended for consumption or planting, but otherwise harmless."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Corruption Study: Vegetation"
		"&7When testing the interaction between &8Corruption&r&7 and Bone Meal, I observed two types of plants appearing frequently—&aCorrupted Roots&r&7 and &aCorrupted Clusters&r&7. They seem useless, but they grow on Corruption without needing water or light. Interesting."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Corruption Study: Spread"
		"&7Corruption does not spread on its own—it is merely a random substance. But it has a &dessence memory&r&7, a reproducible pattern. When given &earcane energy&r&7 or effective fertilizer, Corruption randomly reproduces this pattern in the surrounding area."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Corruption Study: Resonance"
		"&7This reproduction is precisely why it is so important to the &bRelease Ritual&r&7. The ritual remembers the violence of its creation and &dresonates&r&7 with the memory within Corruption, channeling its energy into whatever is placed above it."
	]
	quest.443DAEA62297C415.quest_desc: [
		"&6Origin Island&r"
		"&7A long-forgotten island in the vast ocean, holding &6secrets&r&7 about the origins of familiars. Its only inhabitants are tiny '&8Lost Souls&r&7'—early forms of familiars that failed to evolve fully. These souls can be captured with empty bottles and used in new rituals. The ritual must be performed on the &epedestal&r&7 at the island's center.&r"
		""
		"&7To locate this island, you first need a &bSniffer&r&7. They sometimes dig up &eCrystallized Berries&r&7. You may also purchase berries from &dFloral Endermen&r&7. Feeding Crystallized Berries to a tamed familiar evokes faint memories of their birth and past, crystallizing into &eMemory Fragments&r&7. Memory Fragments are used similarly to Ender Eyes to guide you to the Origin Island.&r"
	]
	quest.443DAEA62297C415.quest_subtitle: "Discover the Origin Island"
	quest.443DAEA62297C415.title: "Origin Island"
	quest.4440AB0D70D690ED.quest_subtitle: "Some FTB Quest Help + Contributor"
	quest.44568D0ED1546BF5.quest_desc: ["Great stats with a downside that's hardly impactful."]
	quest.44568D0ED1546BF5.quest_subtitle: "Golem's Wisdom"
	quest.446683FEB932319C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Twisted Chaos&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Twisted Chaos does not enhance the mind's abilities but instead randomly twists its actions, causing the wearer's attack damage to vary randomly—sometimes hitting enemy weaknesses, dealing &adouble damage&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.446683FEB932319C.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Urges Corruption"
	quest.447E0F674624A5FA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rose Quartz&r"
		"&7A pale red crystal formed by fusing Redstone and Nether Quartz.&r"
		"&7Hold Rose Quartz in the main hand and Sandpaper in the offhand to polish it. Polishing consumes the Rose Quartz immediately; cancelling mid-animation returns the item. Upon completion, you obtain &ePolished Rose Quartz&7.&r"
	]
	quest.44BFA62BE707B244.quest_desc: ["&7This adjustment affects the initial health of spawned mobs. Lower initial health is beneficial for automated farms or manual farming, reducing kill time and preventing clogging. Each item modifies this stat by 5%, with a minimum value of 20%."]
	quest.44BFA62BE707B244.quest_subtitle: "Born Weak"
	quest.44FF46EF1BE66093.quest_desc: [
		"&6Yeti&r&7"
		"&7Passive creatures that only spawn in the &#87CEEBStarlight Permafrost Forest&r&7; &r"
		""
		"&7Sometimes roll along the ground to move; &r"
		""
		"&7Right-click a Yeti with Shears to shear it (similar to shearing sheep): &r"
		""
		"&7Immediately drops 1–3 &#F5F5DCWhite Yeti Fur&r&7, and the Yeti becomes bald with exposed skin (recovers after 2–3 minutes; cannot be sheared again until recovered). &r"
	]
	quest.44FF46EF1BE66093.title: "Yeti"
	quest.455B8465AECDA168.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When you \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-click\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" while holding it, a copy of the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Eye\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" flies out from your hand towards the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Arena\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", and the Blaze Eye in your hand goes into a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The locating function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld or End\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\", or in worlds without Blaze Arenas.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.455B8465AECDA168.quest_subtitle: "Blaze Arena"
	quest.45983509EA6BD841.quest_desc: ["An upgrade to ATM materials. &7Comes with the Eternal trait—completely removes durability concerns. Extremely solid stats that offer both convenience and power—an ideal choice for those who want both ease and strength."]
	quest.45983509EA6BD841.quest_subtitle: "Eternal Power"
	quest.45A1C2B4E1B4D9BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Profane Glutton"
		"&7Corruption will eventually consume you.&r"
		"&7-Each level of &cUrgent Craving&r&7 adds to &cdamage&r&7 taken&r"
		"&7-&cPoison&r&7 damage is doubled&r"
		"&7-&cHunger&r&7 damage causes &cpoison&r"
		""
		"&7Corruption becomes your strongest weapon.&r"
		"&7-&6Gluttony&r&7 becomes &6Urgent Craving&r"
		"&7-&6Urgent Craving&r&7 increases &escythe proficiency&r&7 and spawns &blocusts&r&7 on scythe damage&r"
		"&7-&6Urgent Craving&r&7 accelerates faster and has a higher cap&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_profane_glutton.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.45A1C2B4E1B4D9BC.quest_subtitle: "Endless Consumption"
	quest.45A1C2B4E1B4D9BC.title: "Pact of the Profane Glutton"
	quest.45A31DEFA09A002A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starlight Permafrost Forest&r"
		"&7A surface biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7The Starlight Permafrost Forest has &ahigher&r&7 surface elevation (similar to Overworld mountains). Year-round snow cover gives its vegetation a &fsilver-white&r appearance distinct from other biomes."
		"&7Its main tree is the &8Northland Tree&r&7 (corresponding to the Overworld's spruce)."
		""
		"&7Below the surface (Y > 0), the main block is &bPermafrost&r&7 instead of Grimstone. This underground area is the only place to find &ePermafrost Stone&r&7."
		"&7You can also find unique plants here: &8Pinecone Flowers, Umbrella Moons, Glowing Umbrella Moons, and more&r."
	]
	quest.45A31DEFA09A002A.quest_subtitle: "Bitter Cold Forest"
	quest.45A31DEFA09A002A.title: "Starlight Permafrost Forest"
	quest.45ED7996360032EC.quest_desc: ["&7Exceptionally well-rounded bonuses covering offense, defense, and more—a rare all-purpose material. Even without alloying, it's already incredibly powerful on its own."]
	quest.45ED7996360032EC.quest_subtitle: "Dragons—the Emblem of Kings"
	quest.4623977971D967E9.quest_desc: [
		"Installing this upgrade in the smeltery prevents smelting from occurring."
		""
		"&8&mThe brain is trembling!&r&r"
	]
	quest.4623977971D967E9.quest_subtitle: "Too Lazy"
	quest.46318C4037942B1E.quest_desc: [
		"Can provide a temperature of 1500°C. Requires an Electric Furnace to function."
		""
		"&eA furnace is not limited to just one of these—multiple can be placed in the same furnace to supply fuel consumption."
	]
	quest.46318C4037942B1E.quest_subtitle: "Low-Temperature Heating"
	quest.463ED67306260BA3.quest_desc: [
		"&7This bookshelf differs from others—it provides a unique attribute: &eQuanta Stability&7."
		"&eQuanta Stability&7 eliminates the negative effects of Quanta. When present, &4Quanta's&7 minimum enchantment level penalty is removed, leaving only its bonus. Additionally, the -15% &4Quanta&7 helps suppress &4Quanta&r and &5Arcana&7 for future &ainfusion&7 operations."
		""
		"The Amethyst Motherlode required for crafting can be obtained by &binfusing&r Amethyst Blocks. (Recommended Bookshelf)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Inspired by the concept of magically enhanced magic, I attempted to &9infuse&r Amethyst."
		"Amethyst Shards are too weak, while Amethyst Clusters are already occupied by ancient power. Only Amethyst Blocks can bear this power, becoming Amethyst Motherlodes. Unfortunately, Amethyst Motherlodes are too fragile, with their power channeled into growing Amethyst Clusters. So I encased them in a Calcite bookshelf—the geode-like environment fully unleashes the Motherlode's power, manifesting as a stronger &4Quanta&r-suppressing force—&eQuanta Stability&7. This property differs from simply reducing &4Quanta&7—it removes only the negative effects of &4Quanta&7 while keeping all the benefits. Can I just weld this bookshelf to my enchanting table ("
	]
	quest.463ED67306260BA3.quest_subtitle: "Nature's Power Awakened"
	quest.463ED67306260BA3.title: "Magical Stability Amplified"
	quest.46B09EB249B0D6E0.title: "Lone Star Skeleton"
	quest.46C1263DC7062475.quest_desc: [
		"&6Distortion Engine&r"
		""
		"&7The Distortion Engine violates natural laws, and its practical applications require extreme caution. It rejects causality, occasionally completing a &6focusing cycle&r&7 instantly, shortly after the previous one ends."
		""
		"&7Additionally, the Distortion Engine's chain activations grant stacking &abonuses&r&7 to all other attributes. But clearly, this significantly increases &cfuel consumption&r&7. Finally, it slightly increases the tuning burden of the standard &etuning process&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.46C1263DC7062475.quest_subtitle: "Beyond Linear Time"
	quest.4761041D4596C446.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.4761041D4596C446.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.47AE747B665C5151.quest_desc: ["Unlike Refined Brilliance, this can be applied to tip upgrades."]
	quest.47AE747B665C5151.quest_subtitle: "Higher Level, Stronger I Am"
	quest.47CF8DC4847AD311.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.47CF8DC4847AD311.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.4846CE562BCEFAD5.quest_desc: ["Extends the wireless access point's transmission range to infinite blocks."]
	quest.4846CE562BCEFAD5.quest_subtitle: "Signal Base Station"
	quest.48A06F2501866438.quest_desc: [
		"&7This bookshelf is an extreme enhancement of the Nether Bookshelf. Using the chaotic and fiery power of Blaze Powder and Fire Charges, it undergoes apotheosis, becoming a far more powerful existence. It provides higher &aEterna&7 caps and &4Quanta&7 than the Nether Bookshelf."
		"&7But this power is so violent that it threatens to consume everything it knows, dragging the world into eternal chaos. This bookshelf even prevents you from previewing enchantment results in the enchanting table. Use with caution."
	]
	quest.48A06F2501866438.quest_subtitle: "Hell Descends"
	quest.48A06F2501866438.title: "Chaos Approaches"
	quest.48BAAB5B16A162FF.quest_desc: ["&7To insert items into a &#66DDCCStorage Pouch&7, drag them over the pouch and right-click, or place the pouch on top of the item and right-click. To remove items, right-click the pouch or hold right-click and drag across the inventory. When the pouch is selected in the hotbar, pressing the use key throws out all its contents. When dragging in the inventory, the last item placed is the first to come out."]
	quest.48BAAB5B16A162FF.quest_subtitle: "Can automatically store essences"
	quest.48BEC55ECB0AC9A3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Portable Fluid Interface&r"
		""
		"&7A connector designed specifically for extracting or inputting fluids between dynamic structures.&r"
		""
		"&6Transferring Fluids&r"
		"&7When one Portable Fluid Interface faces another on a dynamic structure, 1 to 2 blocks apart, they automatically connect and transfer fluids.&r"
		"&7Requires a Mechanical Pump. Flow direction and speed depend on the pump's direction and RPM.&r"
		"&7If the target interface is on a moving dynamic structure, it is briefly stopped until the transfer completes.&r"
		"&7Minor misalignments during connection don't affect transfer.&r"
		"&7High movement speed or RPM significantly reduces connection success rates.&r"
		""
		"&6Redstone Lock&r"
		"&7A Redstone signal locks the interface, preventing it from stopping structures or performing transfers.&r"
		""
		"&8They hate jolts but love to dance together.&r"
	]
	quest.48F1FA137148C82F.title: "Discover the Ancient Factory"
	quest.4923304658C6BF41.quest_desc: [
		"&eThe ultimate fuel. Using it as fuel almost feels like a waste."
		"&6Offers the lowest consumption, fastest speed, and highest temperature—nearly perfect."
		""
		"⚡ Speed: 3.0x | ♨ Temperature: 6000 | ⏳ Consumption: 0.1"
		""
		"&aTip&r&7: &f♨ &r&7Temperature determines the tier of materials that can be processed, ⚡ Speed affects processing time, and ⏳ Consumption represents fuel longevity."
	]
	quest.4923304658C6BF41.quest_subtitle: "Ultimate Fuel"
	quest.4939B8B2FE7A3B5D.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.4939B8B2FE7A3B5D.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.496E4A2F2E407B7E.quest_desc: ["&7Before you have enough arrows, a &#FFD700Slingshot&7 is indeed more practical."]
	quest.496E4A2F2E407B7E.quest_subtitle: "Simple Ranged Attack Option"
	quest.49840E89ACF73DAF.quest_desc: ["&7Functions like a vanilla &#66CCFFShovel&7. Can be crafted by placing a vanilla &#66CCFFShovel&7 in a crafting table to convert it into an &#66DDCCSilent Gear Shovel&7."]
	quest.49840E89ACF73DAF.quest_subtitle: "Little Scoop"
	quest.4996E5CD9E56D25E.quest_subtitle: "Food Value > 8"
	quest.4996E5CD9E56D25E.title: "Meal Recycling x32"
	quest.4A4168EA1BC0644E.quest_desc: ["Blazing Magic increases mana regeneration, and the material also has solid Iron's Spells-related stats."]
	quest.4A4168EA1BC0644E.quest_subtitle: "Mana Surge"
	quest.4A4B782308B84A50.quest_desc: ["&7Not essential, but nice to look through a window and see what's happening inside the furnace."]
	quest.4A4B782308B84A50.quest_subtitle: "Observation Window"
	quest.4A7080BE52CC6335.quest_desc: ["&7Functions like a vanilla &#66CCFFHoe&7. Can be crafted by placing a vanilla &#66CCFFHoe&7 in a crafting table to convert it into an &#66DDCCSilent Gear Hoe&7."]
	quest.4A7080BE52CC6335.quest_subtitle: "Garden Tool"
	quest.4AB1523AE2CA75D7.quest_desc: ["&7A &#FFD700Crossbow&7 that automatically loads arrows from your inventory."]
	quest.4AB1523AE2CA75D7.quest_subtitle: "Transfer to Human"
	quest.4AC2F5D5FF711C0F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Resonance Tuner&r"
		""
		"&7&eVoid&r&7 and &6Earth&r&7 do not normally react with each other, and this non-reaction has its uses. The Resonance Tuner softens the interaction of different forces within the &eCrucible&r&7, significantly reducing or even entirely removing &cdestabilization risk&r&7 at the cost of processing speed.&r"
	]
	quest.4AC2F5D5FF711C0F.quest_subtitle: "Detuning Mitigation"
	quest.4ACF299AC1220CE6.quest_subtitle: "Grand Hall"
	quest.4ACF299AC1220CE6.title: "Discover the Castle"
	quest.4AEAA66A5B802779.quest_desc: [
		"&e\"Fast is good!\""
		"&7The biplane's base speed is far higher than other aircraft. With engine and propeller upgrades, it can rival chunk-loading speeds. However, there's a significant crash risk, and crashes &cexplode&7, which can destroy the dropped plane in fire. Always leave plenty of runway and fly carefully."
	]
	quest.4AF740882E852DBF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Familiar House&r"
		"&7A block that can store up to 10 familiars. Stored familiars are &ainvulnerable&r&7 but typically will not attack other creatures (with some exceptions). The Familiar House has two modes:&r"
		""
		"&7&bStorage Mode&r&7: Allows players to freely &amove&r&7 familiars between their active familiars and those in the house.&r"
		"&7&bRoaming Mode&r&7: Allows stored familiars to &arove&r&7 within a configurable distance. In this mode, you can also enable or disable the familiar's abilities while roaming. The Familiar House block can only be broken by its &cowner&r&7, and only when it is in Storage Mode and contains no familiars.&r"
		""
		"&6Important Note&r&7: Only one Familiar House block can be used within a 16-block radius.&r"
	]
	quest.4AF740882E852DBF.quest_subtitle: "Mansion"
	quest.4AFE778B9A79DA33.quest_subtitle: "Light-Footed"
	quest.4B3F9F49C0FF6B3B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Despite improved preparation processes, Arcane Essence ink—especially higher tiers—remains invaluable."
		""
		"&8Its worth is forever etched in the cost of its creation."
		""
		"&7Ink is used to create magic scrolls at the &6Spell Inscription Table&r&7. Higher-tier ink produces &6higher-level&r&7 scrolls with greater efficiency. Legendary ink is the highest tier, but the scrolls it produces may not always be max level. You can upgrade scrolls at the &6Arcane Anvil&r&7 by placing the scroll in the first slot and ink in the second.&r"
		""
		"&7Lower-tier inks can be combined to create higher-tier inks. Pouring four bottles of the same tier into an &6Alchemy Cauldron&r&7 with the specified material can concentrate them into one bottle of tier+1 ink, though this is quite inefficient. Using &6Create&r&7's mixing mechanism can concentrate four bottles into three bottles of tier+1 ink.&r"
	]
	quest.4B3F9F49C0FF6B3B.quest_subtitle: "Exquisite Craftsmanship"
	quest.4B3F9F49C0FF6B3B.title: "Arcane Ink"
	quest.4B6AD3BEF9352961.quest_desc: [
		"&eA furnace that requires electricity to operate."
		""
		"Compared to traditional fuel-based smelting, electric smelting is more convenient—just supply power to process most materials."
	]
	quest.4B6AD3BEF9352961.quest_subtitle: "Electric Smelting"
	quest.4BA0280CD5AC4EB5.quest_desc: ["&7Same as vanilla &#66CCFFShears&7... why did you bother crafting this?"]
	quest.4BA0280CD5AC4EB5.quest_subtitle: "More Prestigious Shears...?"
	quest.4BCF7827E9797977.quest_desc: [
		"&7Emits light at &e14&7 intensity, has a block entity, can hold water, and is not destroyed by water flow."
		""
		"&7Can be used as a heat source for the &#FFAA33Farmer's Delight&7 mod."
		""
		"&7Similar to &#FF8844Leather Armor&7, &#FFAA33Spirit Fire&7 can be dyed on a crafting table using &#66DDCCDyes&7. Multiple dyes can be used, and it can be dyed multiple times."
		""
		"&7&#FFAA33Spirit Fire&7 has one color; &#CC66FFIridescent Spirit Fire&7 has two colors. When crafting &#CC66FFIridescent Spirit Fire&7, the first color is inherited from the &#FFAA33Spirit Fire&7. Dyeing only changes the last color. Default colors are &#FFAA33#EFC016&7 and &#6666FF#464FA5&7."
		""
		"&7Crafting &#FFAA33Spirit Fire Torches&7 and &#FFAA33Spirit Fire Braziers&7 inherits the color."
		""
		"&bCan be used as a ritual consumable for geas declaration.&r"
	]
	quest.4C4558B339BA59A5.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each attack triggers one of the following effects at random:"
		""
		"&7Deal &630%&7 bonus damage to the target and all enemies within &61.5&7 blocks"
		"&7Apply a &drandom debuff&7 to the target"
		"&7Deal &610%&7 of the target's max health as true damage"
		"&7Restore &a5%&7 of the attacker's max health"
		"&7Apply a &arandom buff&7 to the attacker"
		"&7Reduce the target's max health by &625%&7"
		"&7Deal an additional &610%&7 base damage"
		"&7Deal &63×&7 base damage"
		""
		"&7Can apply &bScythe Proficiency&7"
		"&7Counts as a &6Pickaxe Axe&7"
		"&7Has the &btree-felling&7 function of a Saw"
		"&7Destroys all blocks within &63×3×3&7 around the target when mining (doesn't trigger while sneaking)"
		"&7Gains stats from materials:"
		"&7&bArmor&7, &bArmor Toughness&7, &bKnockback Resistance&7"
		"&7&dSpell Power&7, &dSpell Resistance&7, &dMana Regeneration&7, &dMax Mana&7"
		"&7&bGeas Limit&7, &bHealing Received&7"
	]
	quest.4C4558B339BA59A5.quest_subtitle: "One Thing at a Time"
	quest.4C4D49730F599ADA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crystal Desert&r"
		"&7A surface biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7The Crystal Desert is composed of &8Dusk Sand&r&7, with a sparse layer of &8Dead Moonlight Trees&r&7 on the surface."
		"&7Both the surface and dozens of layers underground contain crystal clusters made of &cRed Starlight Crystals&r&7 and &bBlue Starlight Crystals&r&7—an important source of &ctwo types of crystal shards&r&7."
		""
		"&7Compared to other surface biomes, the Crystal Desert has &alower&r&7 feature density, making it easier to locate &eHot Springs&r&7."
		"&7You can also find unique plants here: &8Lunaris Cactus, Dead Moonlight Shrubs, Purple Desert Grass, Desert Purple Flowers, Star Fly Trees, Dusk Surge Grass, Fly Fruits, and more&r."
	]
	quest.4C4D49730F599ADA.quest_subtitle: "Twinkle Twinkle Little Star"
	quest.4C4D49730F599ADA.title: "Crystal Desert"
	quest.4C7B1F3BC1ACBD92.quest_desc: ["&7Adjusts fuel consumption and engine power output—the latter directly affects flight speed. Fuel isn't particularly precious anyway."]
	quest.4CC2D82F6A669265.quest_desc: [
		"&6Flame Diode&r"
		""
		"&7The Flame Diode harnesses the power of fiery, passionate souls, reducing &cfuel consumption&r&7 for &ecatalysts&r&7 around the &eCrucible&r&7 while slightly accelerating the &afocusing process&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.4CC2D82F6A669265.quest_subtitle: "The Power of Strength"
	quest.4D00769819B3C7B5.quest_desc: [
		"&7An expensive but powerful material. Mithril is found between Y=-63 and Y=-38, with relatively low spawn rates—mining with a Hammershot makes it easier. Fortune enchantment affects drop rates. Lightning Bottles are obtained by right-clicking a Charged Creeper with a glass bottle, or found in hidden chests within Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks structures."
		""
		"&7Its strength lies in the Arcane Resonance IV trait. Every 10 Mana provides 1% damage bonus, capped at Trait Level × 20. With sufficient mana, a Thunderweave Handle can provide a terrifying 80% damage boost."
		""
		"&eIf multiple pieces of gear have Arcane Resonance, the mana bonus stacks, but the damage bonus does not—only the highest level applies."
	]
	quest.4D00769819B3C7B5.quest_subtitle: "Electrified Feels Different"
	quest.4D2714BB06E019FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7After carefully considering the properties I observed in &dessence crystals&r&7, I began to think that structure itself might be important. To test this, I crafted an &8Eidolon&r&7 replica to mimic &cmalevolent arcane energy&r&7; condensed soul memory was the closest substance I could think of. It achieved precision down to a hundred-thousandth of a block."
		""
		"&7I did not expect it to explode in front of me."
		""
		"&7But explosions can be useful—if controlled. So I made another sample, this time designing a framework to contain it—a socket made of &6Soulwood&r&7 and &6Soul-Stained Steel&r&7 to channel the energy outward. When focused through a staff, it acts like a miniature ritual, but with different effects."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7A staff in melee combat... is barely adequate. I would probably choose a scythe first, but staves have their uses. They typically emphasize magic damage over physical damage, which is sometimes useful. Their true specialty is revealed when I &ause&r&7 them."
		""
		"&7The Eidolon Staff condenses liquid malevolent arcane energy into a sphere and fires it, reminiscent of a witch's curse. It takes a while to charge and cannot be fired repeatedly in quick succession, but each shot deals significant damage. The staff draws on my soul for power, so the ammo count is shared across all my staves."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7This method of replicating arcane energy hit a wall with other energies—perhaps due to the material. The resonance between Eidolon and malevolent energy may simply stem from the death required to craft Brilliance."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Ammo Capacity"
		"&7As far as I know, essence crystals hold finite energy... but this only applies to the non-physical matter of arcane energy. The &6Ammo Capacity&r&7 enchantment allows a staff to store more energy in the same physical space, roughly one extra spell shot per level. Staves with this enchantment cannot accept the Quick Charge enchantment."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Quick Charge"
		"&7Staves can channel physically manifested magic. Magic can flow out and in—consciously directing its flow is not impossible. Using a staff with the &6Quick Charge&r&7 enchantment in melee has a chance to replenish the staff's energy reservoir, roughly the equivalent of one spell shot. Staves with this enchantment cannot accept the Ammo Capacity enchantment."
	]
	quest.4D2714BB06E019FF.quest_subtitle: "May Mages Fear My Power"
	quest.4D2714BB06E019FF.title: "Essence Staff"
	quest.4D2D9898C6477E3B.quest_desc: [
		"&7For all aircraft: Press R to dismount—some may require two presses to prevent accidental dismounts. Since R conflicts with shader reload, rebinding is recommended."
		""
		"&7After boarding, open your inventory to access the aircraft's UI. You can install upgrades here, and if the plane requires fuel, add it here as well."
		""
		"&7For biplanes: Hold &eSpace&7 to start the engine—the plane will begin to slide, so prepare a runway. Once started, tap &eS&7 to pitch up for takeoff. After liftoff, press &eD&7 to lower the nose. Hold &eShift&7 to shut down the engine and glide for landing."
		""
		"&cBiplanes are fast but have higher takeoff/landing risks. Crashes cause explosions—the damage is severe, so be cautious."
		""
		"&7For helicopters/gyroplanes: Space to ascend, Shift to descend."
		""
		"&7For human-powered aircraft: Hold W to provide power—once it reaches max, it stays there, and W then controls forward movement. Flight continuously drains hunger."
	]
	quest.4D2D9898C6477E3B.quest_subtitle: "At least you know how to throttle and brake..."
	quest.4D448B1BA52C6548.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.4D448B1BA52C6548.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.4D4B372937B102F6.quest_desc: [
		"&7When a creature has the &#FFAA33Starfire&7 effect, it continuously emits bright orange flame particles."
		""
		"&7Splash Damage Mechanic:"
		"&7When a creature with &#FFAA33Starfire&7 (referred to as the \"carrier\") takes damage, a burst of particles appears at its location."
		"&7All creatures within &#FFAA333 blocks&7 of the carrier (excluding the carrier itself) take splash damage equal to &#FFAA331/3&7 of the damage the carrier took."
		"&7The damage source &#FF6666cannot&7 be Starfire itself—otherwise, splash damage won't trigger."
		"&7Splash damage is &#FFD700physical damage&7, bypassing fire immunity passives but reduced by armor."
		"&7Splash damage &#FF6666does not&7 cause knockback."
		""
		"&7Spread Mechanic:"
		"&7When the carrier dies, all creatures within &#FFAA333 blocks&7 gain &#FFAA33Starfire&7."
		"&7The spread effect has the same level, but its duration is &#FFAA331/2&7 of the carrier's remaining duration at death (minimum &#FFAA331 second&7)."
		"&7Higher Starfire levels &#FF6666do not&7 affect any of the above mechanics or values."
	]
	quest.4D4B372937B102F6.quest_subtitle: "A Single Spark Can Start a Prairie Fire!"
	quest.4D79C56FF94C03AE.quest_desc: ["Want to play an attack-speed proc build?"]
	quest.4D79C56FF94C03AE.quest_subtitle: "Then Tell Me... Why Is Your Head So Pointy?"
	quest.4DBB3CA0C3949A66.quest_desc: [
		"&6Thunder Mage Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &elightning magic&r&7, capable of hitting multiple targets simultaneously.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aMaster of Charge&r&7: Can charge the master for a period, boosting their speed and strength.&r"
		"&7&aCharged Creeper&r&7: Follows and charges creepers whenever it finds one.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Roams in &bmountain&r&7 biomes, seeking good spots to attract lightning.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Archmage Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &ebasic magic&r&7 from various schools.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aTransmutation&r&7: Can convert &espell scrolls&r&7 on a pedestal into other random scrolls of the same rarity, with a small chance for higher rarity.&r"
		"&7&cEnderman's Nightmare&r&7: Endermen fear it and flee upon sight.&r"
		"&7&aShulker Protection&r&7: Can counter shulker missiles.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Found in temporary labs located in the &6End&r&7.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Necromancer Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &cblood magic&r&7, including necromantic abilities to summon the undead.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&cUndead Frenzy&r&7: Can drive nearby undead creatures into a frenzy, causing them to attack anything nearby chaotically.&r"
		"&7&cWitherization&r&7: Can convert nearby skeletons into Wither Skeletons.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Found studying death in &8Soul Sand Valley&r&7 cemeteries.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Summoner Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &8void magic&r&7 and dark arts, capable of summoning shadow-born creations.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aTrue Sight&r&7: Grants the master &anight vision&r&7 and immunity to Blindness and Darkness effects.&r"
		"&7&aDark Ritual&r&7: Can deactivate &cSculk Shriekers&r&7, helping the master avoid Warden detection.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Found studying dark arts in labs at &cAncient Cities&r&7.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Hunter Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in using &ebows&r&7 to attack enemies with swift movement.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aWatcher&r&7: Protects the master from enemies targeting them, even when unaware.&r"
		"&7&aScenting Loot&r&7: The master can right-click any item on it to search for nearby creatures that drop that item, marking them for the master.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Lives in camps across &bforest&r&7 biomes.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Druid Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in using &bnature magic&r&7 to control enemies.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aOvergrowth&r&7: Can use bone meal on nearby crops.&r"
		"&7&aNature's Blessing&r&7: Can breed nearby animals.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Found protecting forests around the world.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Illusionist Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &dillusion magic&r&7, controlling enemies through deception.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aMagic Trick&r&7: When the master is low on health, the Illusionist performs a trick to hide them from enemies.&r"
		"&7&aDecoy&r&7: When low on health, it disappears and leaves behind an explosive decoy to taunt nearby enemies.&r"
		"&7&aPickpocket&r&7: When no one is looking and gold nuggets or emeralds are on the ground, this little trickster will claim them.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Illusionists naturally spawn disguised as other Overworld familiars. Use a &eMirror of Truth&r&7 to reveal them.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Plague Doctor Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &cpoison magic&r&7, slowly killing enemies through poison.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&cToxic Blood&r&7: The master and itself deal extra damage to poisoned entities. When the Plague Doctor is attacked, it throws a poison bottle in retaliation.&r"
		"&7Obtaining: To obtain it, craft a &cToxic Reagent&r&7 and give it to a tamed Druid familiar.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Scorcher Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &efire magic&r&7, burning enemies to death.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&cMolten Heart&r&7: When attacked, it sets the attacker on fire for a period.&r"
		"&7&aHeat Resistance&r&7: Grants the master and itself immunity to fire.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Roams in hot areas of the &cNether&r&7.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Cleric Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &aholy magic&r&7, primarily support but capable of powerful holy spells to purify enemies.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aRedemption&r&7: It attacks undead in sight, but if it sees a zombie villager, it will heal and redeem it using holy power.&r"
		"&7Obtaining: To obtain the Cleric, cast the &aPurification spell&r&7 near an untamed Necromancer familiar.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Bard Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &dmusical magic&r&7, attacking enemies with powerful melodies while supporting allies with buffing tunes.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aMusical Nature&r&7: Plays melodies that make adventures more pleasant.&r"
		"&7Obtaining: To obtain it, cast an &eEldritch spell&r&7 near an untamed familiar to spark its interest in music.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Frostling Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &bfrost magic&r&7, with a balanced mix of offense, defense, and mobility, along with decent crowd control.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aFrosty Footsteps&r&7: It and the master can freeze water surfaces beneath their feet to walk on.&r"
		"&7&aFrozen Heart&r&7: It and the master are immune to freezing effects, including Powder Snow.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Roams in &bicy biomes&r&7.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Dragon Warrior Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &6ender magic&r&7 with a focus on melee combat.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&eDragon Breath&r&7: Can collect dragon's breath with glass bottles.&r"
		"&7&aHeart of the Dragon&r&7: Its dragon heart allows it to naturally regenerate health.&r"
		"&7&aGuardian&r&7: When an allied familiar is attacked in melee range, it swaps places with them and locks onto the attacker.&r"
		"&7Spawn: Found in the &6Outer End Islands&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.4DBB3CA0C3949A66.quest_subtitle: "Adorable"
	quest.4DC5D99569CC3F68.quest_desc: [
		"This upgraded Sculk bookshelf channels power into &5Arcana&r, providing large amounts of &5Arcana&r without providing &4Quanta&r."
		"(Important Bookshelf)"
	]
	quest.4DC5D99569CC3F68.quest_subtitle: "Mystical Power Reborn"
	quest.4DC5D99569CC3F68.title: "Sculk Growth—Gaze into the Deep Dark Again"
	quest.4E154F6CBE09CA32.quest_desc: [
		"&6Tooth of Hunger&r&7"
		"&7Dropped by &#8B0000Hungry Walkers&r&7 upon death; &r"
		""
		"&7Can be used to craft &#FF4500Hunger Daggers&r&7 and various decorative blocks. &r"
		""
		"&7Aside from killing, the Tooth has a special drop method: &r"
		""
		"&7If a Hungry Walker's &#DC143Cbite attack&r&7 is blocked by a &#1E90FFshield&r&7 (or similar equipment), the Hungry Walker has a &#FFA07A16.67%&r&7 chance to drop 0–2 &#8B0000Teeth of Hunger&r&7; &r"
		""
		"&7\"&#FFD700Losing teeth&r&7\" does not affect the Hungry Walker's subsequent behavior or attack damage. &r"
	]
	quest.4E25633D226B8C90.quest_desc: ["Exceptional stats—no wonder dragons are so tough to kill."]
	quest.4E25633D226B8C90.quest_subtitle: "You're a Dragon Too, Huh"
	quest.4E302A6F9E6AAC09.quest_desc: ["&7To insert items into a &#66DDCCStorage Pouch&7, drag them over the pouch and right-click, or place the pouch on top of the item and right-click. To remove items, right-click the pouch or hold right-click and drag across the inventory. When the pouch is selected in the hotbar, pressing the use key throws out all its contents. When dragging in the inventory, the last item placed is the first to come out."]
	quest.4E302A6F9E6AAC09.quest_subtitle: "Can automatically store items placed in the pouch"
	quest.4E7B1EFF01114F88.quest_desc: [
		"&6Steam Engine&r"
		""
		"&7A high-tier power source that works with &eBoilers&r to generate power.&r"
		"&7Stress output: &c0–16384 su&r"
		"&7RPM output: &c16–64 RPM&r"
		""
		"&6Obtaining&r"
		"&7Crafted at a Crafting Table.&r"
		""
		"&6Usage&r"
		""
		"&6Placement&r"
		"&7Steam Engines must be placed on a &eFluid Tank&r, converting it into a &6Boiler&r. To output power, place a &eShaft&r in front of the engine by right-clicking with a Shaft.&r"
		""
		"&6Outputting Stress from Boilers&r"
		"&7Steam Engines extract stress from the boiler. Stress generation is detailed in the &6Boiler&r section.&r"
		"&7Stress is evenly distributed across all Steam Engines on the boiler. Each engine outputs a maximum of &c16384 su&r. If total stress exceeds this, additional engines are needed to avoid waste. The number of engines required equals the boiler's level.&r"
		"&7Adding more engines beyond the required count does not improve efficiency.&r"
	]
	quest.4E826A5530F49919.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.4E826A5530F49919.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.4EB3AF395EE2F05E.quest_desc: ["Increases reach distance. No explanation needed for how strong that is."]
	quest.4EB3AF395EE2F05E.quest_subtitle: "A Little Longer Is A Lot Stronger"
	quest.4EF6614B03841586.quest_desc: [
		"&6Dusk Eye Fish&r&7"
		"&7A common aquatic creature in the Abyss. Cannot survive out of water (loses mobility and slowly takes damage over time); &r"
		""
		"&7Unlike &#ADD8E6Pufferfish&r&7 or &#87CEEBLightfin Piranhas&r&7, this creature cannot be caught in a water bucket; &r"
		""
		"&7Only attacks when provoked (melee only, attacks can be blocked by shields); &r"
		""
		"&7Group Aggression: When one is attacked, all nearby Dusk Eye Fish target the attacker; &r"
		""
		"&7They stop chasing when the target leaves the water. &r"
	]
	quest.4EF6614B03841586.title: "Dusk Eye Fish"
	quest.501A9D4E77A9D0EA.quest_desc: ["&7Can clear large areas of grass, leaves, and other debris. Right-click for &#66FF66area harvesting with auto-replant&7. Crop yields are increased by &FFAA331.5×&7 (rounded up)."]
	quest.501A9D4E77A9D0EA.quest_subtitle: "Farmer's Best Friend"
	quest.501AB9740C6C4447.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Heart Strength&r"
		""
		"&7Unlike similar runes that provide healing, the Rune of Heart Strength forces the form to exceed its limits, granting a small amount of &aextra health&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.501AB9740C6C4447.quest_subtitle: "Healing the Complete"
	quest.502FAEFE4F6CF6B2.title: "Playtime 8h"
	quest.5057DE8E48849E95.quest_desc: [
		"&6Brass&r"
		""
		"&7Molten copper and zinc meet in the furnace, cooling into this warm golden metal. It's soft enough to be shaped by hand, yet serves as the foundation for countless mechanisms.&r"
		""
		"&6Usage&r"
		"&7Holding it and right-clicking a placed &estripped log&r&7 coats it in metal, turning it into a stable &eBrass Casing&r—the starting point for many complex creations.&r"
		"&7At a &eStonecutter&r, it can be shaped into scaffolding and structural components, laying the groundwork for larger builds.&r"
		"&7On a &eCrafting Table&r, it takes more refined forms: as &eBrass Hand Parts&r for nimble joints, as &eBrass Funnels&r to guide materials, or as &eBrass Tunnels&r through which energy and matter flow.&r"
		""
		"&8A note in the margin: It's friendly enough that a beginner with a file and hammer can get started. Of course, don't expect to make a sword out of it.&r"
	]
	quest.5057DE8E48849E95.quest_subtitle: "An important metal, commonly used to craft advanced components"
	quest.50CA5A1721E6B28E.quest_desc: ["As a tip upgrade, provides excellent luck bonuses—perfect for early-game looting and late-game gambling."]
	quest.50CA5A1721E6B28E.quest_subtitle: "I'm So Lucky"
	quest.50E57652755EC341.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The enchanting table seems to have changed. I can sense it's more... \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"unstable\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" than the original version.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Apotheosis enchanting system\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" has been added. Enchantment levels can exceed vanilla limits, with most enchantments having a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"level cap +4\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". Some enchantments may have special adjustments.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If you're unfamiliar with \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\", check the corresponding chapter for details.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[Click to Jump]\",\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"aqua\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"681DDFCA829035FB\"}}]}]}"
	]
	quest.50E57652755EC341.quest_subtitle: "I Have a FOMO Table"
	quest.5125C8D0790C81BB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Roaring Wind&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Roaring Wind functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bRoaring Wind&r&7 effect, increasing &amovement speed&r&7 and &aattack speed&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.5125C8D0790C81BB.quest_subtitle: "Swift Pulse"
	quest.5177469D5E64C1E3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sandpaper Polishing&r"
		""
		"&6Methods&r"
		"&7Polishing can be done in several ways:&r"
		"&7Hold Sandpaper in one hand and the item to polish in the other, then right-click; or&r"
		"&7Hold Sandpaper and right-click a dropped item; or&r"
		"&7Use a Deployer holding Sandpaper—it works the same as manual polishing.&r"
		"&7Each polish consumes 1 durability of Sandpaper.&r"
		""
		"&6Polishing Copper Blocks&r"
		"&7Can treat vanilla copper blocks:&r"
		"&7If waxed, it removes the wax; if oxidized, it reduces the oxidation level by one.&r"
		"&7This matches vanilla axe behavior exactly.&r"
		""
		"&6Polishing Building Blocks&r"
		"&7Can transform certain vanilla building blocks (e.g., Stone Bricks, Andesite) into their \"Polished\" variants.&r"
		""
		"&6Enchanting&r"
		"&7Sandpaper can be enchanted via Enchanting Table or Anvil. Compatible enchantments include Unbreaking, Mending, and Curse of Vanishing.&r"
		"&8A tiny scribble in the margin: Would anyone actually enchant this?&r"
	]
	quest.51BCF840DB0DBE44.quest_desc: ["&7Your old friend from vanilla enchanting—unremarkable, providing only 2 &l&aEterna&7. Yet it still leads you into the halls of enchantment."]
	quest.51BCF840DB0DBE44.quest_subtitle: "It All Begins Here"
	quest.51BCF840DB0DBE44.title: "Magic's Oldest Friend"
	quest.51BE2E9C9209091D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Wave's Grasp&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Wave's Grasp functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bWave's Grasp&r&7 effect, slightly extending &ablock interaction distance&r&7 and &aitem pickup range&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.51BE2E9C9209091D.quest_subtitle: "Extending Pulse"
	quest.523AD23A30544888.quest_desc: ["&7Top-tier traits and stats. Offers solid base values and good damage scaling. Obtained after defeating the Dead King. A key component in any build."]
	quest.523AD23A30544888.quest_subtitle: "May Your Journey Be Filled with Curses and Blessings"
	quest.524A12A30F00E96E.quest_desc: ["&7An upgrade to Flesh Alloy Ingot for spellcasting. Focuses on Scarlet spell stats, and the Feast trait's max stack cap is increased."]
	quest.524A12A30F00E96E.quest_subtitle: "Devouring Hunger"
	quest.527B5583A09AF510.quest_desc: ["Wither Skeleton Skulls have deeper ties to the Nether, thus generating more powerful Quanta."]
	quest.527B5583A09AF510.quest_subtitle: "Stronger Quanta Growth"
	quest.527B5583A09AF510.title: "Sacrificed Skull"
	quest.52FB65193EF182F4.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Wrath\",\"color\":\"red\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When attacked: applies a 10-second \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Wrath Damage\"\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" mark to the attacker and makes them \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"glow\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When attacking:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Attacking a target with the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Wrath Damage\"\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" mark deals \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"10% increased damage\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" (increased to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"20%\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" with the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Mark of Wrath\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" equipped), and consumes the mark.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Each attack grants 1 stack of \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Enhanced Tattoo\"\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\", up to 5 stacks, lasting \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"15 seconds\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". Each stack provides an effect.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If you don't attack for 5 seconds, take \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"10% max health as true damage\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", and again every 4 seconds thereafter.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.52FB65193EF182F4.quest_subtitle: "Wrath Erosion"
	quest.52FB65193EF182F4.title: "Wrath Erosion"
	quest.530E224CB690AC4D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Abyss&r"
		"&7A relatively rare marine biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7The Abyss is characterized by narrow, elongated trenches with &cextremely narrow&r&7 spaces."
		"&7The height difference from the seafloor surface is &agreat&r."
		"&7The deepest parts of the Abyss are often &avery close&r&7 to the bedrock layer (making it nearly impossible for non-aquatic creatures to spawn here)."
		""
		"&7The Abyss is home to many unique &#1E90FFaquatic creatures&r&7 and &#FF4500Abyssal Magma Blocks&r&7 that generate bubble columns."
		"&7Unique plants include &#FF0000Red Moss&r&7 and &#32CD32Sticky Velvet Moss&r&7. Some coral reefs also generate near the upper edges of the Abyss."
		"&7Sticky Velvet Moss Balls can be converted into &#8FBC8FSlime Balls&r&7 in a crafting grid."
		""
		"&7Player visibility is &cextremely limited&r&7 in the Abyss. It is recommended to prepare sufficient &#00FF00Night Vision Potions&r&7 and &#00CED1Water Breathing Potions&r before exploring."
	]
	quest.530E224CB690AC4D.quest_subtitle: "If You Gaze into the Abyss..."
	quest.530E224CB690AC4D.title: "Abyss"
	quest.532E3C393BCE6BA6.quest_desc: ["&7Ghast Tears increase the spawn cap of a spawner. Generally, a spawner stops spawning when N mobs are nearby. Ghast Tears raise the value of N."]
	quest.532E3C393BCE6BA6.quest_subtitle: "Rush Hour Subway"
	quest.533E6E13F1C9E939.quest_desc: [
		"&6Belt&r"
		""
		"&7It is the flowing road in the engineer's hand, moving items between points or transmitting unseen rotational force.&r"
		""
		"&6Laying This Road&r"
		"&7You need at least two Shafts facing the same direction as start and end points. Hold the Belt and right-click the first shaft—red particle trails appear where you aim, asking for the end point. Right-click again when the particles turn green—the road is laid. If the particles remain red, the placement is wrong; if they vanish, the distance exceeds its limit.&r"
		"&7It can extend horizontally, vertically, or at precise 45° slopes, but the total length (including the end shafts) cannot exceed &c20 blocks&7 (&c15 blocks&7 diagonally).&r"
		""
		"&6Trimming and Adjusting&r"
		"&7Right-clicking the end of an existing Belt with a new Belt extends it by one block (the item isn't consumed), moving the end shaft. To shorten it, use a Wrench on the end.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Using a Wrench mid-belt cuts it, usually consuming two Shafts (except in Creative). For two separated Belt segments of valid length and direction, right-clicking the end of one with a Belt connects them, returning one Belt and two Shafts.&r"
		"&7You can also insert a new support Shaft by right-clicking an empty spot mid-belt; using a Wrench removes it.&r"
		""
		"&7It doesn't have to remain a dull metal color. Dyes color it any shade. A bucket of water or a water bottle washes away the dye.&r"
		""
		"&8A winding Belt is sketched in the margin, with the note: The road is laid. Now, make things move.&r"
	]
	quest.5372150CD0958B7B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crushing Wheel&r"
		""
		"&6Processing Items&r"
		"&7Designed to execute \"&ccrushing&r&7\" recipes. Items without a matching recipe are destroyed.&r"
		"&7Most \"&ccrushing&r&7\" recipes match \"&egrinding&r&7\" recipes, so it can replace most &eMillstones&7 in functionality.&r"
		"&7They must be used in pairs, with the rotation directions of the two wheels coordinated for operation.&r"
		""
		"&6Processing Entities&r"
		"&7Active Crushing Wheels deal &cdamage&7 to creatures entering their range (except players in Peaceful mode), dropping crushed products at the output.&r"
		"&7This damage ignores armor, Protection enchantments, and Resistance effects, but can be absorbed by Absorption.&r"
		"&7For horizontally placed wheels, placing a block above prevents entities from being pulled in; for vertical placements, a Chute above the gap prevents suction without affecting operation.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Placement and Mechanics&r"
		"&7When a pair of Crushing Wheels is correctly placed with a one-block gap unobstructed, an invisible block is generated: the &eCrushing Wheel Controller&7.&r"
		"&7This block has collision, cannot be moved by pistons or dynamic structures, acts as an open container, handles item input and output, and controls behavior. It disappears when the wheels are disassembled.&r"
		""
		"&7A functional pair requires:"
		"&7A &c1-block&7 gap between them, unobstructed;"
		"&7Their faces must be &cparallel&7.&r"
		""
		"&8Deep scratches mark this page, as if run over by wheel teeth. Credit goes to the manuscript owner for having a proper emergency stop system...&r"
	]
	quest.5372150CD0958B7B.quest_subtitle: "An operational component that can crush items."
	quest.5378D02C832E3260.quest_subtitle: "Food Value >= 14"
	quest.5378D02C832E3260.title: "Feast Recycling"
	quest.5394037EDC7769D9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Continuing Shot"
		"&7You cannot pretend to be a perfect shot.&r&cMissing an arrow removes all draw speed bonuses and reduces the stat instead"
		"&7Precision is key.&r&aDealing ranged damage increases draw speed for most ranged weapons"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_continuing_shot.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5394037EDC7769D9.quest_subtitle: "Be the Arrow"
	quest.5394037EDC7769D9.title: "Pact of the Continuing Shot"
	quest.53A39052B8DFFE3E.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.53A39052B8DFFE3E.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.53C821423589F530.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
		""
		"Please do not summon during the day—Skeletron enters a berserk state in daylight, with extremely high defense and massively increased damage that can one-shot players."
		""
		"Upon defeat, unlocks:"
		"&#FF3D5CNether Gobber Ore"
		"&r&#7EE344Chlorophyte Ore&r&7"
		"&#770808Dreadstone&r&7"
		"&#DD660ASolar Core&r"
	]
	quest.53C821423589F530.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1 — Unlocks Stage 2 upon defeat"
	quest.54207C49530C50BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6World Difficulty&r"
		"&7You may or may not have noticed, but world difficulty changes aren't just a simple name change&r"
		"&7They affect mob health, damage, and other stats&r"
		""
		"&7&6Classic Mode&r&7: Default values&r"
		""
		"&7&6Expert Mode&r&7:&r"
		"&7Health, Attack Damage, Armor × &c1.2&r"
		""
		"&7&6Master Mode&r&7:&r"
		"&7Health, Attack Damage, Armor, Armor Toughness, Tracking Range × &c1.5&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/difficuity_kjs.png width:180 height:50 align:center fit:true}"
		"&dSo... dear player... if you can't handle it, don't play on high difficulty...&r"
	]
	quest.54207C49530C50BC.quest_subtitle: "Must-Read Info, Yet No One Reads.png"
	quest.54DAB6324FA151F2.quest_desc: [
		"&7The book spat out by the well seems to have changed. It was my research journal, yet it has spawned countless shadows."
		""
		"&7I need to focus to see what the shadows are—they resemble paper, touchable yet intangible, as if made of... essence."
		""
		"&7These shadows connect to my research notes, like annotations, like guidance. The text they hold is both familiar and foreign."
		""
		"&z&mI have seen the truth."
	]
	quest.54DAB6324FA151F2.quest_subtitle: "Falling into Darkness"
	quest.54DCDB42738F0557.quest_desc: [
		"&6Authority of the Inverted Heart&r"
		""
		"&7Your soul is the world's soul. Your heart is the world's heart. Open it wide, for all to see, and for all to hold.&r"
		"&7-&cMagic damage&r&7 taken is quadrupled&r"
		""
		"&7Authority—a pact between your form and the world itself.&r"
		"&7-Your soul opens to the world; when another soul witnesses yours, a &econnection&r&7 is established&r"
		"&7-Damage you take and deal is &bshared&r&7 with them&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/authority_of_the_inverted_heart.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.54DCDB42738F0557.quest_subtitle: "Forging Many Hearts into One"
	quest.54DCDB42738F0557.title: "Authority of the Inverted Heart"
	quest.54F1765FA7F3571B.quest_subtitle: "Rare Treasure"
	quest.551FB78D5B444E41.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#88DDFFRepair Pylon&7 is used for essence repair, capable of restoring shattered &#FFAA33Runes&7 and certain other items."
		""
		"&7The &#88DDFFRepair Pylon&7 is &e3&7 blocks tall, with &e1&7 item slot and &e4&7 essence slots. A &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect how full the slots are."
		"&7Place repair materials and &#66FF99Essence&7 in the pylon, and the item to repair nearby (within &e6&7 blocks horizontally and &e4&7 blocks vertically from the base) on an &#66DDCCItem Stand&7, &#66DDCCItem Pedestal&7, or &#CC99FFRune Workbench&7, and it will be repaired."
		""
		"&aThe interval for detecting repair recipes&7 is &e2&7 seconds. Repair takes &e32&7 seconds, after which the pylon enters a &e60&7-second cooldown."
		"&7When repair begins, the target position is recorded. If the target is lost when the phase ends, it re-enters the recipe detection phase."
		""
		"See next page for diagrams."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7As shown, this is a &#88DDFFrepair&7 recipe:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/repair_pylon2.png width:110 height:150 align:center}"
		"&7&#FF6666Red items&7 must be placed in the &#88DDFFRepair Pylon&7 structure;"
		"&7&#FFAA33Orange items&7 must be placed on nearby &#66DDCCItem Stands&7, &#66DDCCItem Pedestals&7, etc.;"
		"&7&#66CCFFBlue items&7 are the output."
		""
		"&cWhen repairing, ensure the pylon contains exactly the required items and essence amounts!"
		""
		"&rSee next page for practical example."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"An example repairing a Tyrfing weapon."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/repair_pylon.png width:150 height:150 align:center}"
	]
	quest.551FB78D5B444E41.quest_subtitle: "Mysterious Repair"
	quest.551FB78D5B444E41.title: "Arcane Restoration"
	quest.5538FE04FFC149D5.quest_desc: [
		"As an advanced bookshelf, the Ocean Bookshelf provides a higher enchanting cap than vanilla bookshelves. Deep-sea magic grants additional &5&lArcana&r&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&oPS: Check JEI for Pufferfish uses!&r"
	]
	quest.5538FE04FFC149D5.quest_subtitle: "Arcana's Blessing"
	quest.5538FE04FFC149D5.title: "Deep-Sea Enchanting Power—Glimpsing Mystery"
	quest.553B4B865F0C526B.quest_desc: ["Want to remove curses from your weapons? Prismarine Web's properties can strip away curses—though no one knows how it works."]
	quest.553B4B865F0C526B.quest_subtitle: "Curse Removal"
	quest.5543C9B27A71B835.quest_desc: [
		"&7Fire is the foundation, and &#FFAA33metal&7 is the pillar. With &#66CCFFiron&7, I can forge &#CC99FFweapons and armor&7 myself. I could piece together materials and strap them on for protection, or simply press iron sheets into &#CC99FFweapons&7—but that would be a waste of material, only a temporary solution. What I truly need is a &#FFD700roaring blast furnace&7."
		""
		"&7While looking for &#66CCFFiron&7, I found some familiar crystals—precisely the raw material needed for &#66DDCCHardened Steel&7. I think I'll be able to craft my own &#CC99FFgear&7 soon."
	]
	quest.5543C9B27A71B835.quest_subtitle: "Preparing for Smelting"
	quest.5543C9B27A71B835.title: "Metal Smelting"
	quest.55566ED56D9E8281.quest_desc: ["This summoning ritual can only be performed in the Cursed Garden."]
	quest.55566ED56D9E8281.quest_subtitle: "Lunar Monstrosity"
	quest.55566ED56D9E8281.title: "Summoning Ritual"
	quest.555729244B7C2153.quest_desc: [
		"&6Magic Essence&r"
		"&7Consumables used to increase &bspell power&r&7 and &bspell resistance&r&7. Each has 3 tiers with a usage cap. Obtained via:&r"
		"&7Power: Dropped by &emagical creatures&r&7, upgraded via &6rituals&r&7.&r"
		"&7Resistance: Obtained via &eShrinkers&r&7, upgraded via &6rituals&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.555729244B7C2153.title: "&6Magic Essence: Power&r"
	quest.558E23816B266EF8.title: "Glow Leech"
	quest.55A1FBEF21D0FE68.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.55A1FBEF21D0FE68.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.55A79D65F67123C4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Void Tether&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Void Tether functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bVoid Tether&r&7 effect, increasing &ajump height&r&7, slightly reducing &agravity&r&7's effect, and slightly reducing &cfall damage&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.55A79D65F67123C4.quest_subtitle: "Lifting Pulse"
	quest.55BA0F294A5D2F55.quest_desc: ["&7Flowers infused with magic replenish the caster's energy when they select a spell but lack the mana to cast it.&r"]
	quest.55BA0F294A5D2F55.quest_subtitle: "Auto-Restore"
	quest.55FBD2DCCC7E79D2.quest_desc: ["A special drop from the Eternal Starlight dimension—somewhat tedious to obtain, but its powerful trait greatly boosts your strength."]
	quest.55FBD2DCCC7E79D2.quest_subtitle: "E! TER! NAL! STAR! LIGHT!"
	quest.568D517E18953F2F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Scarlet Essence&r"
		""
		"&7When filled with water, the cauldron &cdamages&r&7 creatures inside it. If there is an empty potion slot, it attempts to generate &cblood&r&7. Right-clicking with a glass bottle collects &cScarlet Essence&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&8Plunge the still-pulsing sin into this boiling cauldron of judgment. As scarlet struggles to precipitate from the gap between life and liquid, you may bottle it—a concentrated negation forged from guilt, an extracted and stripped 'anti-life' still warm.&r"
	]
	quest.56AFCEF4D1507B1B.quest_desc: ["&7Fires homing &#66CCFFghost arrows&7 at enemies."]
	quest.56AFCEF4D1507B1B.quest_subtitle: "Hacks detected"
	quest.56B3E6FD85D52F60.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Traveling this world, I often encounter those wielding \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"tomes\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"strange wands\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\", casting \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"spells\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" that give me a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"splitting headache\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Since I can't beat them, I might as well walk the same path.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Click to jump to Iron's Spells Side Quest\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"60C42244ED37BA5F\"},\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"yellow\"}"
	]
	quest.56B3E6FD85D52F60.quest_subtitle: "Endless Enigma"
	quest.56B3E6FD85D52F60.title: "First Encounter with Magic"
	quest.56B761C2894F3C2E.quest_desc: [
		"&7One simple application of &#FFD700Hallowed Gold&7 is the &#FFAA33Essence Jar&7."
		""
		"&7The &#FFAA33Essence Jar&7 can &ainfinitely store&7 a single type of &#66FF99Essence&7. Its operation is similar to &#66DDCCDrawers&7:"
		""
		"&7Left-click: insert &e1 stack&7 of &#66FF99Essence&7"
		"&7Sneak + Left-click: extract &e1 stack&7 of &#66FF99Essence&7"
		""
		"&7Right-click: insert &e1 stack&7 of &#66FF99Essence&7"
		"&7Double right-click: insert all of the same type of &#66FF99Essence&7"
		""
		"&7No automatic input/output is supported, but automation can be achieved via &#FFCC44Mechanical Arms&7, etc."
		""
		"&7These jars have &anearly unlimited capacity&7, but can only store &ca single type of essence&7."
	]
	quest.56B761C2894F3C2E.quest_subtitle: "&7A Simple and Practical &#66FF99Essence&7 Storage Technology"
	quest.56B761C2894F3C2E.title: "Essence Storage"
	quest.56CB359C8D5426A3.quest_desc: [
		"&7Please note that this is where you set the difficulty. &cN1&7 is not the default difficulty. To remove difficulty settings, use &6Clear Difficulty Settings&r below."
		""
		"&7. Base Game Difficulty (World Difficulty)"
		""
		"&6Classic&7: Stat multiplier &a1.0&7x"
		"&6Expert&7: Stat multiplier &a1.2&7x"
		"&6Master&7: Stat multiplier &a1.5&7x + extra &b10&7 block tracking range"
		""
		"&6N1&7: Health/Armor/Toughness &a2&7x, Attack &a1.2&7x"
		""
		"&6N2&7: Health/Armor/Toughness &a3&7x, Attack &a1.4&7x"
		""
		"&6N3&7: Health/Armor/Toughness &a4&7x, Attack &a1.6&7x"
		""
		"&6N4&7: Health/Armor/Toughness &a5&7x, Attack &a1.8&7x"
		""
		"&6N5&7: Health/Armor/Toughness &a6&7x, Attack &a2&7x"
		""
		"&7Final stats = &6Game Difficulty Multiplier &7× &6Player Stage Multiplier&7"
		""
		"&cThis rule only applies to mobs&7"
		""
		"&7Difficulty is detected within &b129&7 blocks of the player"
		""
		"&7Uses the player with the &6highest stage difficulty&7 as the baseline"
	]
	quest.56CB359C8D5426A3.quest_subtitle: "Those who enter this door shall abandon all hope"
	quest.57045442B4763EC9.quest_subtitle: "Strong Swimmer"
	quest.5704D090CFE3D913.quest_desc: ["&7Each &#66FF99Essence&7 harvested while equipped reduces &#88DDFFSoul Shield&7 recovery time by &e2&7 * &#88DDFFSoul Shield recovery rate&7 * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7. Also restores &e10&7 * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 mana."]
	quest.5704D090CFE3D913.quest_subtitle: "Special Effect on Essence Harvest"
	quest.57084B014CE6C718.quest_desc: ["Wither Shells provide a damage bonus and a charge ability."]
	quest.57084B014CE6C718.quest_subtitle: "Ha! Not a Waste of My Bullets After All"
	quest.571979CF7DC3291C.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Pride\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Passive effect per second: gain 1 stack of \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Divinity\"\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\", each stack providing \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"7.5% crit chance\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" (increased to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"15%\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" with the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Crown of Pride\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" equipped), up to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"6\",\"color\":\"white\"},{\"text\":\" stacks (increased to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"10\",\"color\":\"white\"},{\"text\":\" with the Crown of Pride).\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When attacking:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Crit chance is determined by \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Divinity\"\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" stacks.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"On critical hit:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Deal \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"110% damage\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" (increased to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"120%\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" with the Crown of Pride).\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Reset \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Divinity\"\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" stacks.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Gain 1 stack of \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Godhood\"\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\", up to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"6\",\"color\":\"white\"},{\"text\":\" stacks (increased to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"10\",\"color\":\"white\"},{\"text\":\" with the Crown of Pride), each providing \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"5% crit damage\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
	]
	quest.571979CF7DC3291C.quest_subtitle: "Pride Erosion"
	quest.571979CF7DC3291C.title: "Pride Erosion"
	quest.5731A86EC589BF22.quest_desc: [
		"&7Are you tired of placing &bblocks&r&7 one by one?&r"
		"&7Don't worry! The &bBuilding Wand&r&7 lets you place multiple blocks at once!!!&r"
		""
		"&7Whether you're a &bmaster architect&r&7 or just need to build simple structures, it's well worth using!&r"
	]
	quest.5731A86EC589BF22.quest_subtitle: "Artisan Craftsmanship"
	quest.57925645E9E7F4D8.quest_desc: ["&7Getting it is its only downside. Its trait is extremely effective for clearing crowds—efficiency scales with enemy numbers."]
	quest.57925645E9E7F4D8.quest_subtitle: "Enslaving Dragons Is Truly Disgraceful"
	quest.57D76B1B33C57F9F.quest_desc: ["Even though you've swum this far and probably don't need these anymore, I'll give them to you anyway—I don't know what else to give... Have some aquatic specialties."]
	quest.57D76B1B33C57F9F.quest_subtitle: "Then Tell Me, Why Am I Not Taking a Boat?"
	quest.5883458218829D00.quest_desc: [
		"&7The ProMAX version of Soul-Stained Steel. High cost, powerful effect. The Primordial Malice trait provides a massive boost to soul shields and scythe proficiency."
		""
		"Recommended part: All armor slots"
	]
	quest.5883458218829D00.quest_subtitle: "Stack the Thickest Armor"
	quest.589CD98F3C3AA8D3.quest_desc: [
		"&e\"Fast doesn't always win—not stumbling is what counts.\"&7"
		"&7Sticking to the stable-and-steady philosophy, the quadcopter has a perfect zero-crash record. As for the cost..."
		""
		"&7Great for hovering while building—very stable, but also very slow. Since it's considered quiet, it can even be used near Ancient Cities without triggering Wardens."
	]
	quest.58BCF9F1BE8BAA5E.quest_desc: ["&7As it fell, the power sealed within seemed to dissipate... I need to investigate and see what traces it left behind."]
	quest.58BCF9F1BE8BAA5E.quest_subtitle: "Sold!"
	quest.58C802ED3AA66357.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.58C802ED3AA66357.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.58CA43B9AA0530E2.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.58CA43B9AA0530E2.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.58DE58D4F8290C1C.quest_desc: [
		"&7This item was a chance discovery during my travels."
		""
		"&7However, with my current shallow understanding, I cannot comprehend the mysteries it hides."
		""
		"&7Spell scrolls drop from certain special enemies at random levels. Generally, you would use the &6Spell Inscription Table&r&7 to craft scrolls as needed."
		""
		"&7A small number of special scrolls cannot be crafted—they are dropped by specific bosses or can only be cast through designated equipment."
	]
	quest.58DE58D4F8290C1C.quest_subtitle: "Power of the Arcane"
	quest.58DE58D4F8290C1C.title: "Spell Scrolls"
	quest.58FD71F9C065E1AC.quest_desc: ["&7Take a gamble?&r"]
	quest.58FD71F9C065E1AC.quest_subtitle: "Random Spell + Random Level"
	quest.5914AF3C360016D7.quest_desc: ["Maybe strong—who knows."]
	quest.5914AF3C360016D7.quest_subtitle: "Endgame Template"
	quest.591B10BC5FA20823.quest_desc: ["&7An eye used to locate ancient cities. While Deep Dark biomes follow some patterns, their presence doesn't guarantee a city—hence the need for locating tools. The city structure has changed significantly from vanilla, with more open areas and richer loot, but Sculk Shriekers may still be hidden in dark corners. Stay cautious."]
	quest.593ABE7FAC454B34.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Ailment Purge&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Ailment Purge compels the form to catalyze, transform, and alter matter, accelerating the processing and removal of &cnegative effects&r&7, overcoming them at an unnatural speed.&r"
	]
	quest.593ABE7FAC454B34.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Urges Processing"
	quest.59CAC75D442ED208.quest_desc: [
		"&7When equipped:"
		"&7+&e50%&7 &#66FF66Scythe Proficiency&7;"
		""
		"&7Enhances &#FFCC44Scythe&7 enchantments:"
		""
		"&7&#FFAA33Reap&7: Immediately returns upon hitting an entity, return speed increased to &e2&7×, damage increased to &e1.5&7×."
		""
		"&7&#88DDFFSoar&7:"
		"&7If &66FF66sprinting&7, horizontal speed reduced by &e0.6&7× the line-of-sight vector;"
		"&7Attack range reduced to &e2&7 blocks, offset &e2&7 blocks in the line-of-sight direction, damage increased to &e1.25&7×."
		""
		"&7Disables &#FFCC44Scythe&7 sweeping attacks."
	]
	quest.59CAC75D442ED208.quest_subtitle: "Scythe Authority"
	quest.59FF1DA682FCF7E2.quest_desc: ["Since you've opened edit mode, you should also find this content"]
	quest.59FF1DA682FCF7E2.quest_subtitle: "Players interested in coding or other related content can use this tool to quickly create add-on content"
	quest.5A46895D552BC15F.quest_subtitle: "Am I not energetic? I feel great!"
	quest.5A59A7F48EA53168.quest_desc: ["[ { \"text\": \"Click to go to Create Side Quest\", \"underlined\": true, \"color\":\"yellow\",\"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"1FB3D1FAE9A88C39\" } } ]"]
	quest.5A59A7F48EA53168.quest_subtitle: "Mechanical Power"
	quest.5A59A7F48EA53168.title: "Spinning Gears"
	quest.5A8ACB926DFAB615.quest_subtitle: "You will receive a starter pack"
	quest.5A8ACB926DFAB615.title: "&a\"Honey That Conceals Suffering at the Beginning?!\""
	quest.5A8B3E256CCCB82C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Building a &#FFD700Blast Furnace&7 is the foundation for &#FFAA33metal smelting and casting&7. Even though I never imagined needing to build one in the wild, it's not particularly difficult for me."
		""
		"&7Fortunately, I had the habit of taking good notes while studying metallurgy. My notes at least contain the specific components and construction requirements for the &#FFD700Blast Furnace&7, which I call the &#66DDCC\"Complete Metallurgy Manual\"&7."
		""
		"&7The bad news is, why does it only have the furnace-building part and nothing else? Where's the \"complete\" part, damn it?!"
	]
	quest.5A8B3E256CCCB82C.quest_subtitle: "Metal Smelting"
	quest.5A8B3E256CCCB82C.title: "Well, Let's Fire It Up!"
	quest.5A8B7CD00226572C.quest_desc: [
		"Has a low chance to drop when undead creatures are killed by a player."
		"By following the direction this item flies, players can locate the Night Lich. In that structure, players must place four Soul Stars on the altar to summon the Night Lich."
		"Can also be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5A8B7CD00226572C.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.5A9B842FAAFBFD26.quest_desc: ["&7Strong resistance to fire damage, and deals extra damage when attacking burning targets."]
	quest.5A9B842FAAFBFD26.quest_subtitle: "A Miracle It Hasn't Melted"
	quest.5AD7799D9EF0BFBE.quest_subtitle: "Kill Kill Kill"
	quest.5AEF01E9FF0A0727.quest_desc: [
		"&bAn upgraded version of the Lead."
		""
		"&bLeft-click an animal (no other entities) to store it inside. Right-click the ground to release it."
		""
		"&dNo one knows the internal structure of this lead... not even Endermen."
	]
	quest.5AEF01E9FF0A0727.quest_subtitle: "Poké Ball"
	quest.5B0DD1682972CBF0.quest_desc: ["&7Provides high ranged damage multipliers and decent armor. A balanced choice for ranged fighters—keeping offensive pressure while staying alive."]
	quest.5B0DD1682972CBF0.quest_subtitle: "Beeeep"
	quest.5B38A4F8CD3C9B98.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.5B38A4F8CD3C9B98.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.5B941F073DDCD277.quest_subtitle: "Eating twisted-type items increases sanity instead of decreasing it"
	quest.5B941F073DDCD277.title: "&a\"Sweet Dew Blooming from Rot\""
	quest.5BCF3F0899CE62B9.quest_subtitle: "Disable natural Eternal Gate spawning in the End"
	quest.5BDB153064430D05.quest_desc: [
		"&6Study: Lingering Flames"
		"&7After passing through the &dWeeping Well&r&7, &eBlaze Powder&r&7 transformed into what I call \"&6Lingering Flames&r&7.\" A ethereal golden flame, yet solid and tangible. It burns like charcoal, but its flame is unrelated to the burning process."
		""
		"&7Though this bright substance stands out among all materials obtained from the well, it follows a similar pattern. The well strips away certain components of the material—impurities, matter, something more subtle—all possible. In this case, it seems to have stripped away everything except pure flame, producing the embodiment of change."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Re-examining: Lingering Flames"
		"&7Contrary to my earlier assumptions, the well does not strip things away—it &creverses&r&7 them, replacing them with void-like counterparts. Lingering Flames are likely the purest example: everything not belonging to &cevolving essence&r&7 is shrouded in a dark void, producing a material &afar&r&7 more perfect than \"suitable for a purpose.\""
	]
	quest.5BDB153064430D05.quest_subtitle: "Essence of Evolution"
	quest.5C10F3B6A94BA227.quest_desc: [
		"&7Materials for crafting &#66DDCCSoul-Stained Steel&7 tools, weapons, equipment, and trinkets mostly provide the &#88DDFFSoul Shield&7 effect."
		""
		"&7The &#88DDFFSoul Shield&7 reduces damage taken by the player."
		""
		"&7The &#88DDFFSoul Shield&7 is affected by:"
		""
		"&6Soul Shield Capacity&7"
		"&6Soul Shield Stability&7"
		"&6Soul Shield Recovery Rate&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&#88DDFFSoul Shield&7 maximum is &#88DDFFSoul Shield Capacity&7."
		""
		"&7&#88DDFFSoul Shield&7 recovery interval = floor(&#FFDD55base recovery time&7 / &#88DDFFSoul Shield recovery rate&7)."
		"&7Actual time to recover &e1&7 point of &#88DDFFSoul Shield&7 = recovery interval + &e1&7."
		"&7When taking damage > &e0&7, the current recovery time resets to &#FFDD55base recovery time&7 + recovery interval."
		"&7If wearing &#CC6666Witchbane Belt&7 and the damage type is &#CC99FFmagic damage&7, recovery time resets to &e0&7 (recovered on the next player tick)."
		"&7Each &#66FF99Essence&7 harvested while wearing the &#FFAA33Weaver Ring&7 reduces recovery time by &e2&7 * recovery rate * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7."
		""
		"&b&lDamage Mitigation"
		"&7When taking damage > &e0&7 and &#88DDFFSoul Shield&7 > &e0&7, damage is reduced based on damage type."
		"&7If damage type is &#CC99FFmagic damage&7 or wearing the &#CC6666Borderless Belt&7, the &#CC99FFmagic damage multiplier&7 is used; otherwise, the &#FF8844general damage multiplier&7 is used."
		"&7Damage taken = damage * damage multiplier."
		"&7Soul Shield loss = absorbed damage / stability, never dropping below &e0&7."
	]
	quest.5C10F3B6A94BA227.quest_subtitle: "Forging Reality"
	quest.5C65959659507556.quest_desc: [
		"&7This item modifies the spawner's minimum spawn delay. Typically used with clocks. Each item affects 10 ticks. The minimum delay after modification is 20 ticks."
		""
		"&7The minimum and maximum spawn delays combine to determine the spawn interval, which randomly falls between the two values."
	]
	quest.5C65959659507556.quest_subtitle: "I can't wait"
	quest.5C6B5AC7571785F6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Speed Controller&r"
		""
		"&6Usage&r"
		"&7Before use, place a &eLarge Gear&7 on top. Either the gear above or the shaft below can serve as stress input or output.&r"
		""
		"&7Right-click and hold the speed display interface on the controller to precisely adjust the output &aspeed&7 and &adirection&7.&r"
		""
		"&7If stress is input from the bottom shaft, the controller regulates the speed and direction of the top gear. If input from the top gear, it regulates the output of the bottom shaft.&r"
		""
		"&7Think of it as an automatic transmission—but be aware: setting a high output speed requires sufficient &cstress&7 from the power source, or the system may overload.&r"
		""
		"&8This page of the manuscript has been torn.&r"
	]
	quest.5C6B5AC7571785F6.quest_subtitle: "A transmission component that maintains a constant speed."
	quest.5CCD14497FCA00DE.quest_desc: ["&7Each &#66FF99Essence&7 harvested while equipped restores &e5%&7 * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 health."]
	quest.5CCD14497FCA00DE.quest_subtitle: "Special Effect on Essence Harvest"
	quest.5CF40BE797380E84.quest_desc: [
		"&7Killing creatures with a &#FFCC44Scythe&7 easily harvests their &#88DDFFsouls&7, quickly yielding &#66FF99Essences&7 that automatically fly toward the player."
		""
		"&7Using &#CC99FFmagic&7 also harvests the &#88DDFFsouls&7 of creatures."
		""
		"&7Different creatures yield different &#66FF99Essences&7 based on their &#88DDFFsoul nature&7. Try killing various creatures to collect more types."
	]
	quest.5CF40BE797380E84.quest_subtitle: "Harvest"
	quest.5CF40BE797380E84.title: "Any Scythe"
	quest.5D095029A0B8B414.quest_subtitle: "mcmod.cn"
	quest.5D2677DFFEE1AFA1.quest_desc: ["&7Has a massive &65×5×5&7 mining area—enjoy, it's the Gold Rush era!"]
	quest.5D2677DFFEE1AFA1.quest_subtitle: "True Area Mining"
	quest.5DA66C973C8C8C39.quest_subtitle: "Typically unlocked after defeating the Dead King"
	quest.5DAD3734F5DAA6B1.quest_desc: ["&7Significantly boosts regeneration and survivability—provides stable sustain and forgiveness in prolonged fights."]
	quest.5DAD3734F5DAA6B1.quest_subtitle: "For My Sake, Live On!"
	quest.5DEF70A03509B309.quest_desc: [
		"&7In Apotheosis, spawners are highly customizable. You can adjust them according to your needs. Adjustments fall into two categories: spawn target changes and spawner attribute adjustments."
		""
		"&7To change the spawn target, right-click the spawner with a &3Mystic Ender Lead&7 containing a captured mob."
		""
		"&7To adjust spawner attributes, right-click the spawner with the corresponding adjustment item, consuming it to modify the spawner's properties."
	]
	quest.5DEF70A03509B309.quest_subtitle: "Essence Energy Tuning"
	quest.5DFF9CA04548FAB9.quest_desc: ["&7Unlike other staves, this one uses &#55D5D5Soul Energy&7. Right-click to fire &#CC99FFspell projectiles&7; left-click deals &#CC99FFmagic damage&7."]
	quest.5DFF9CA04548FAB9.quest_subtitle: "Basic Staff"
	quest.5E01EC2AC8CE43F0.quest_desc: [
		"&6Cemetery&r"
		"&7This new structure belongs to the &8Soul Sand Valley&r&7, a realm ruled by &cdeath&r&7. &cNecromancers&r&7 are naturally drawn to these places, so you're sure to find them here.&r"
	]
	quest.5E01EC2AC8CE43F0.title: "&6Cemetery&r"
	quest.5E0B8E874FA58643.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.5E0B8E874FA58643.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.5E1CADCE38118460.quest_desc: ["Low cost, but decent stats. Built for Nether exploration."]
	quest.5E313592ACB65BC2.quest_desc: [
		"&7Gobber's unique properties allow it to absorb the abilities of other objects. Crafted into medals and rings, it can absorb other items and activate their corresponding effects for extended periods. Check JEI for specific recipes. Note that even rings don't need to be equipped—once activated, they work even when placed in an Ender Chest."
		""
		"&7Note: The low-tier healing medal slowly restores saturation to the player."
	]
	quest.5E313592ACB65BC2.title: "Gobber Medals / Rings"
	quest.5E3B1B0AB352F0F3.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.5E4E12ACE4F534AD.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When you \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-click\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" while holding it, a copy of the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Abyssal Eye\",\"color\":\"blue\"},{\"text\":\" flies out from your hand towards the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Sunken City\",\"color\":\"blue\"},{\"text\":\", and the Abyssal Eye in your hand goes into a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The locating function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether or End\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", or in worlds without Sunken Cities.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.5E4E12ACE4F534AD.quest_subtitle: "Sunken City"
	quest.5E513FFD985CDDF9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Golem Forge&r"
		"&7A large underground structure guarded by the &cStarlight Golem&r&7."
		""
		"&7The Golem Forge typically generates in the &8Voidstone layer&r&7 below Y<0. It is composed of &8Voidstone&r&7, &#C0C0C0Golem Steel&r&7, and &#8B7355Oxidized Golem Steel&r&7 decorative blocks."
		"&7The interior consists mainly of &8narrow corridors&r&7 connecting rooms filled with &#FF4500lava&r&7 below."
		""
		"&7Some rooms contain &bFrozen Man spawners&r&7 and have a higher chance of containing &6loot barrels&r."
		"&7You can use the &eEye of Seeking&r&7 to locate this structure."
		""
		"&4The Starlight Golem is immune to damage while connected to energy blocks."
	]
	quest.5E513FFD985CDDF9.quest_subtitle: "Once a bastion sheltering countless lives, now only broken walls remain."
	quest.5E513FFD985CDDF9.title: "Golem Forge"
	quest.5E69573B6AA70AFA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Acceleration Lining&r"
		""
		"&7The Acceleration Lining uses highly conductive materials from strange fabrics, significantly increasing the &aFocusing Speed&r&7 of the &eCrucible&r&7 with no negative side effects.&r"
	]
	quest.5E69573B6AA70AFA.quest_subtitle: "Double Down"
	quest.5E69992403F40955.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.5E81AAD675EB0F0F.quest_subtitle: "Summoning Ritual"
	quest.5E89F969FC7A8AF9.quest_desc: ["Early on, nothing beats raw base stat bonuses."]
	quest.5E89F969FC7A8AF9.quest_subtitle: "Excellent Base Damage Bonus"
	quest.5EB5BBBCE2AB1245.quest_subtitle: "A utility tool for finding Weeping Wells"
	quest.5EC974496B2CB2F2.quest_desc: [
		"&7Used as ammunition for bows / crossbows or dispensers. Upon firing, it leaves a trail of &#55D5D5Soul Particles&7."
		"&7Can &#66CCFFignore blocks&7 and pass through terrain."
		""
		"&7This also means that if it misses a creature, the Ghost Arrow won't land—it will fall through the ground and &#FF6666fall into the void&7 (no return)."
		""
		"&7Ghost Arrows are one of the few projectile attacks that can harm &#66FF66Ghosts&7, &#66FF66Wisps&7, or players with the &#66CCFFEthereal Shell&7 enchantment."
		"&7They can also hit Spirit-class mobs in their &#FFD700burrowing state&7."
	]
	quest.5EC974496B2CB2F2.quest_subtitle: "Headshot!"
	quest.5F1C1AA992472C3D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Heresy&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Heresy dismantles magic, &csilencing&r&7 enemies similarly to an Erosion Scepter. This effect weakens their &eEssence Magic&r&7 and can stack to completely suppress a target's &cmagical abilities&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.5F1C1AA992472C3D.quest_subtitle: "Destroying Creation"
	quest.5F253340FE9F4FCF.quest_desc: [
		"&7With many new materials unlocked, it's time to upgrade your gear. Try more alloy combinations and select materials based on your needs."
		""
		"&7Many Stage 1 recommended materials from the Silent Gear chapter are still usable. Under the powerful alloy system, weighing traits against stats is essential. You need to balance armor values and damage while incorporating as many useful traits as possible."
	]
	quest.5F253340FE9F4FCF.quest_subtitle: "A Fresh Start"
	quest.5FC4F86EF4128003.quest_desc: [
		"&7Theoretically, you could also craft this in Stage I."
		""
		"&7On attack, &cdeals additional damage&7 equal to &62 × &7 the number of &bEssence&7 the target drops on death."
		"&7If the target is a player, damage is 4 × max(1, (1 + target armor / 12) × (1 + (1 - 1 / target armor)) / 12)."
		"&fThis value remains 4 for armor values up to 60 points (×30)."
		""
		"&7Example: A Creeper drops 4 &bEssence&7, so the &cbonus damage&7 is 4 × 2 = &68 points&7."
	]
	quest.5FC4F86EF4128003.quest_subtitle: "Kill!"
	quest.5FFB29607E15D805.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Defiance"
		"&7Magic has transformed your perception of death: damage becomes increasingly &cpainful&r&7.&r&cMaximum health reduced by one fifth"
		"&7An unnatural regenerative ability is infused into your form: an eternal &adesire&r&7 to &agrow&r&7.&r&aSaturation-based healing is doubled, and tripled near death&r&aHealing received increased by two fifths"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_defiance.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5FFB29607E15D805.quest_subtitle: "Defying Limits"
	quest.5FFB29607E15D805.title: "Pact of Defiance"
	quest.601016E861B6036F.quest_subtitle: "Peak Arcane"
	quest.6038063D7681AFB5.quest_subtitle: "Food Value >= 14"
	quest.6038063D7681AFB5.title: "Feast Recycling x32"
	quest.609276A8CA8ACF91.quest_desc: [
		"&7When equipped, consuming rotten food (Rotten Flesh, &#66BB66Putrid Essence&7, &#FFAA33Gluttonous Gel&7):"
		""
		"&7Eating time halved;"
		"&7Extends &#FF8844Gluttony&7 by &e15&7 seconds, up to &e150&7 seconds (only extends existing effects);"
		"&7Reduces Hunger effect by &e7.5&7 seconds;"
		"&7Additional &e1&7 hunger and &e1&7 saturation restored."
		""
		"&7When consuming &#FFAA33Gluttonous Gel&7, each equipped &#66DDCCGreed Ring&7 increases &#FF8844Gluttony&7 level by +&e1&7 and duration by +&e10&7 seconds."
	]
	quest.609276A8CA8ACF91.quest_subtitle: "Endless Hunger"
	quest.609ED89F7E454DCA.quest_desc: [
		"&eThe energy within is exceptionally volatile."
		"&6Double the speed, surging high temperatures—a leap in performance."
		""
		"⚡ Speed: 2.0x | ♨ Temperature: 4000 | ⏳ Consumption: 0.2"
		""
		"&aTip&r&7: &f♨ &r&7Temperature determines the tier of materials that can be processed, ⚡ Speed affects processing time, and ⏳ Consumption represents fuel longevity."
	]
	quest.609ED89F7E454DCA.quest_subtitle: "Overlimit Combustion"
	quest.60BAD1C5ADE6C33A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Study: Malevolent Lead"
		"&7After passing through the &dWeeping Well&r&7, &eDeepslate Gold&r&7 transforms into &cMalevolent Lead&r&7. Most of the arcane energy bound to the gold shifts to &cmalevolent arcane energy&r&7, causing the metal to fall from the alchemist's pedestal to the lowest tier of materials."
		""
		"&7The arcane energy in the metal is roughly halved. Was it stripped away by the well, or has it transformed into something I have yet to identify? Both are possible. This might be related to the arcane interaction capability shown by &8Void Slate&r&7..."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Re-examining: Malevolent Lead"
		"&7Currently, I only have &cMalevolent Lead&r&7 as a way to examine the physical form of &8Shadow Crystals&r&7—having lost exactly half its arcane mass, what else could it be?"
		""
		"&7Separating the microcrystals in &eDeepslate Gold&r&7 from the malevolent crystals in &cMalevolent Lead&r&7 has yet to yield results. But until I can obtain more materials, this is the best way to study the structure of &8Shadow Arcane Energy&r&7."
	]
	quest.60BAD1C5ADE6C33A.quest_subtitle: "Turning Wonder into Decay"
	quest.60BBE14FB14FB583.quest_desc: [
		"&7This bookshelf is different from others. You can place books in it like a Chiseled Bookshelf, but it exhibits precise and powerful magic-blocking capabilities. &eWhile enchanting, it completely blocks the enchantments it contains (if a book has multiple enchantments, only the first is blocked)&7, preventing the enchanting table from offering them."
		""
		"&7What is this? I feel a motherly presence here. Like an overprotective mother, it removes everything you don't want."
	]
	quest.60BBE14FB14FB583.quest_subtitle: "Like a Child in a Mother's Arms"
	quest.60BBE14FB14FB583.title: "Ocean's Embrace"
	quest.60C42244ED37BA5F.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I rummaged through my pack and found a few \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"ancient scrolls\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\"—turns out they've been in my hands all along, just never looked at closely.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[\"\"]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The so-called \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"magic\"\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" of this world might be hidden within them, waiting for a key.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.60C42244ED37BA5F.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Creations"
	quest.60CCCAA11DDEA68F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Functions like the Rending Anchor Blade—can be thrown. It actively tracks &FFAA33all nearby creatures&7, quickly &#66CCFFdashes between targets&7, and applies &#FF6666Hatred&7 stacks. Higher stacks increase bonus damage."
		""
		"&7When thrown, the Rending Anchor Blade in your inventory temporarily becomes an &#66CCFFAnchor Soul&7, reverting upon return."
	]
	quest.60CCCAA11DDEA68F.quest_subtitle: "Though expensive, you can definitely craft this by now"
	quest.6130B6740A8460CE.quest_desc: ["&7Hold left-click to launch a &#66CCFFYo-Yo&7 to attack enemies."]
	quest.6130B6740A8460CE.quest_subtitle: "Swing and Sway"
	quest.613D2E97D95993FF.quest_subtitle: "Mother's Tenderness"
	quest.613D3C5BA25706B6.quest_subtitle: "This Is... a Workbench?"
	quest.613D3C5BA25706B6.title: "The Beginning of Everything"
	quest.61CD195A772A6255.quest_desc: [
		"&7When &#6Sanity&7 drops to &e-45&7, you have a chance to enter the &#88DDFFErosion state&7."
		""
		"&7If you are wearing a &#FFD700Seven Deadly Sins trinket&7, you will be eroded by the corresponding sin."
		""
		"&7Without a trinket, there is a &e25%&7 chance of being eroded by a random sin, and a &e75%&7 chance of falling into a &#FF6666Panic state&7."
	]
	quest.61CD195A772A6255.quest_subtitle: "Erosion State"
	quest.62214066B0F19784.quest_desc: ["&7Tired of noisy slaughterhouse sounds? Sick of mobs' grunts and squeals? This modification makes spawner-spawned mobs silent, reducing noise pollution."]
	quest.62214066B0F19784.quest_subtitle: "SHUT UP!"
	quest.623ECC7C41919422.quest_desc: [
		"&7Attacks have a chance to become &FFAA33critical hits&7."
		"&7The next attack after a kill is &FFAA33guaranteed to crit&7."
	]
	quest.623ECC7C41919422.quest_subtitle: "Crits for Days"
	quest.62B6DB17872E27D4.quest_desc: ["&7Great base stats and exceptional Starlight Affinity. Even just using its trait, it's already top-tier. A worthwhile investment with great versatility."]
	quest.62B6DB17872E27D4.quest_subtitle: "Stellar Core"
	quest.62F882E969E15846.quest_subtitle: "Used for Casting Nuggets"
	quest.630EEC8565D962D6.quest_desc: ["&7Excellent ranged stats. When enough stacks are accumulated, consumes a small amount of health to trigger extra damage—trading blood for damage."]
	quest.630EEC8565D962D6.quest_subtitle: "Erase Me! Erase You Too!"
	quest.6324F101E1CFA4CA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Glimmering River&r"
		"&7A surface biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Like rivers in the Overworld, it is typically a &8transition biome&r that separates waterways within or between biomes."
		"&7The Glimmering River is narrow and long, but eventually flows into the vast &#87CEEBStarlight Sea&r."
		""
		"&7The Glimmering River also has some &#9ACD32Abyssal Fruit plants&r&7 and &#20B2AAaquatic vegetation&r similar to lily pads."
		"&7Non-aquatic creatures can only spawn dozens of blocks below the river—they're not really river dwellers anyway."
	]
	quest.6324F101E1CFA4CA.quest_subtitle: "Glimmer in the Lake"
	quest.6324F101E1CFA4CA.title: "Glimmering River"
	quest.633471475BE20F2E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Dropped by &#ADD8E6Pufferfish&r&7 upon death; &r"
		""
		"Can be used to make ink."
		""
		"&8Who knows how it turns into two glass bottles?"
	]
	quest.633B88042B030B5E.quest_subtitle: "Long night... the hardest to endure~"
	quest.63423F9C2A3931E5.quest_desc: ["&7Mining speed may be slower than an axe, but it can &#66DDCCfell an entire tree&7 at once."]
	quest.63423F9C2A3931E5.quest_subtitle: "One Tree, One Hit"
	quest.634CBFD54B22E624.quest_desc: [
		"&6Brass Funnel&r"
		""
		"&6Usage&r"
		"&7Its basic use is almost identical to the Andesite Funnel, but with finer control: it supports &eitem filtering&7 and &esetting the number of items transferred per operation&7.&r"
		"&7In output mode, looking at its filter slot and scrolling the mouse wheel adjusts the single-output quantity, up to &c64&7.&r"
		""
		"&6Additional Notes&r"
		"&7The Brass Funnel can output up to a full stack of items at once.&r"
		"&7In downward output mode, it only outputs if the block below is empty of dropped items—it pauses if items are already there.&r"
		""
		"&8It's smart enough to know when to stop.&r"
	]
	quest.6386F7A674C56D65.quest_subtitle: "Steel Rod Plus"
	quest.639AC8246CA81675.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.639AC8246CA81675.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.63A0E5D82118EC71.quest_desc: ["&7A highly versatile material with great stats, fitting almost any build. The Promotion effect increases most trait levels—pushing your existing setup even higher. An essential choice for endgame optimization."]
	quest.63A0E5D82118EC71.quest_subtitle: "Iridescence"
	quest.63D0E7814E6F4017.quest_desc: ["Similar to Bone, but summons wisps every 5 seconds to attack nearby enemies. Useful for early exploration. Drops from the Banshee."]
	quest.63D0E7814E6F4017.quest_subtitle: "Spirits and Phantoms"
	quest.6449D872847D4B67.quest_desc: ["I can't believe my humble little pack actually attracted an art teacher!"]
	quest.6449D872847D4B67.quest_subtitle: "Art"
	quest.6456C4ED798E5EBD.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crimson Forest&r"
		"&7A surface biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Unlike most biomes, the Crimson Forest's primary color is a low-saturation, low-brightness &#DC143Cred&r&7 instead of purple."
		"&7Its main tree is the &#DC143CCrimson Tree&r."
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Glow Mushrooms&r&7 (features) generate more frequently in the Crimson Forest."
		"&7Most plant species on the surface are the same as the Starlight Forest, but there are also a few unique species."
	]
	quest.6456C4ED798E5EBD.quest_subtitle: "A contaminated forest, slowly purifying itself."
	quest.6456C4ED798E5EBD.title: "Crimson Forest"
	quest.647E80D4B00C0C82.quest_desc: ["&7The &#FFAA33Reap&7 enchantment creates wind vortexes, but &FFAA33Reap&7's cooldown is extended."]
	quest.647E80D4B00C0C82.quest_subtitle: "Scythe Authority"
	quest.648E4AF815BE0547.quest_desc: [
		"&7Scythe attack damage is boosted by &bScythe Proficiency&7."
		""
		"&7Attacking a creature with a scythe or spell exposes its &bSoul&7 for &610 seconds&7. Refreshing the duration resets the timer."
		""
		"&7If the creature dies during this period, its &bSoul&7 shatters, triggering &bEssence Harvest&7 and &dCovert Harvesting&7."
	]
	quest.648E4AF815BE0547.quest_subtitle: "Soul Rip"
	quest.6495C96750D3BA0C.quest_desc: ["&7Some aircraft can mount weapons, but air combat is rarely necessary. The Bomb Bay has decent damage output but high resource consumption."]
	quest.64AC4146C392E8A6.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Envy\",\"color\":\"yellow\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When attacking:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Apply a 10-second \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Enmity\"\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" mark to the target.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Against targets without the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Enmity\"\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" mark, \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"deal 30% less damage\",\"color\":\"red\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When attacking a target with the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Enmity\"\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" mark:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Steal 1 positive effect from the target\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" (max once every 0.5 seconds).\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Reduce the target's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"max health by 5%\",\"color\":\"red\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The stealer gains \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"temporary health\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Passive: When attacked by someone with \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Envy\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" and you do not have the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Enmity\"\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" mark, \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"you take 30% less damage\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
	]
	quest.64AC4146C392E8A6.quest_subtitle: "Envy Erosion"
	quest.64AC4146C392E8A6.title: "Envy Erosion"
	quest.64E40E59C864874C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Meteor Shower&r"
		"&7A special weather event that can only occur in the &bStarlight Dimension&r&7, with a low chance of happening."
		""
		"&7During a Meteor Shower:"
		"&7Several meteors with &dpurple trails&r&7 fall in straight lines, crashing into the ground and dealing &cdamage&r to creatures within 1 block."
		"&7Meteors containing &eore resources&r&7 may also fall. Upon impact, they &cexplode&r&7 (without damaging terrain) and emit particles."
		""
		"&7Some meteor impacts may only yield &b8&r&6Coarse Aethersent Ore&r."
		"&7Others may generate resource blocks composed of &eNebula Stone&r&7 and &6Coarse Aethersent Blocks&r&7."
		"&7Some impacts may spawn a &cComet Creeper&r on the spot."
		""
		"&7Survival players can craft and launch &bStar Guide Rockets&r&7 to actively trigger a Meteor Shower."
		"&7&8Small Comet Creepers&r&7 begin naturally spawning in low-light areas of the Starlight Dimension during Meteor Showers."
		"&7You can build &aAethersent Golems&r&7 to intercept falling meteors."
	]
	quest.64E40E59C864874C.quest_subtitle: "Sometimes, meteor showers occur here. Countless stars streak across the night sky, creating a beautiful spectacle..."
	quest.64E40E59C864874C.title: "Meteor Shower"
	quest.651B146F0F9BEA1D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Press&r"
		""
		"&6Pressing&r"
		"&7Processes items via recipes by pressing dropped items or items on &eBelts/Depots&r&7.&r"
		"&7Primarily used to press metal ingots into &eMetal Sheets&7.&r"
		""
		"&6Packing&r"
		"&7Processes items inside a &eBasin&r&7 via pressing.&r"
		"&7Used to combine multiple materials into finished products.&r"
		""
		"&6Compacting&r"
		"&7Also processes items inside a &eBasin&r&7 via pressing.&r"
		"&7Executes &c4×4&r&7 or &c9×9&r&7 single-material crafting recipes.&r"
	]
	quest.65477F1881F13EBB.quest_desc: ["Obtained via blood extraction or from loot. Provides quick stat boosts early on."]
	quest.65477F1881F13EBB.quest_subtitle: "Provides Spell Power Boost"
	quest.65823964A5871AED.quest_desc: ["&dCompared to the previous generation, this version is far more stable—even capable of holding creatures that would resist... at your mercy.&r"]
	quest.65823964A5871AED.quest_subtitle: "Master Ball"
	quest.65B3DDCC5C5B7361.quest_desc: [
		"&6Deployer&r"
		""
		"&6Usage&r"
		"&7The Deployer has two modes: Use and Attack. Use a Wrench to switch between them.&r"
		""
		"&6Use Mode&r"
		"&7Default mode, simulating a player's right-click.&r"
		"&7It can place blocks, operate doors, shear sheep, and essentially perform any survival-mode right-click action.&r"
		"&7Given tools or items have enchantments applied and consume durability; feeding food heals creatures.&r"
		""
		"&6Attack/Destroy Mode&r"
		"&7Simulates a player's left-click, including attacking creatures and breaking blocks. Given weapons or tools have enchantments applied and consume durability.&r"
		"&7Creatures killed by a Deployer count as player kills, dropping loot and experience normally.&r"
		"&7The Deployer's attacks are always fully charged, regardless of its working speed.&r"
		""
		"&6Mechanics&r"
		"&7When powered, the Deployer's arm extends and retracts rhythmically, performing an action at its farthest point.&r"
		"&7A full cycle: extend → use/attack → retract → wait.&r"
		"&7Speed is determined by RPM, with an effective range of &c4 RPM&7 to &c256 RPM&7. Beyond this range, speed changes no longer affect efficiency.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The Deployer always targets the block or entity in the second block ahead, unaffected by intervening blocks.&r"
		"&6It stops working in the following situations:&r"
		"&7Item overflow;"
		"&7No power supplied;"
		"&7Held item matches the block's item form;"
		"&7Held item is the bucket form of a target fluid;"
		"&7Receiving a Redstone signal (if activated mid-cycle, it finishes the current cycle before stopping).&r"
		""
		"&6Item Access&r"
		"&7The Deployer has a single item slot. Items can be input or output via logistics components.&r"
		"&7Its filter slot can mark items or filters to prevent them from being output.&r"
		"&7When shearing, breaking blocks, killing creatures, or performing other actions that produce drops, the drops go directly into its internal storage. If it already holds an item, it enters overflow.&r"
		""
		"&6Overflow&r"
		"&7The Deployer enters overflow in two cases:&r"
		"&7More than one type of item is stored;"
		"&7The internal item does not match the filter.&r"
		"&7In overflow, it stops working until the excess is removed via logistics.&r"
		"&7Placing a tool in the filter slot prevents it from being output.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Feeding/Breeding&r"
		"&7In Use mode, the Deployer can feed creatures or players by consuming a held food item. Fed creatures enter a breeding state; players restore hunger and saturation and gain food effects.&r"
		""
		"&6Processing Items&r"
		"&7Place the Deployer above a Depot or Belt to process items on them. See relevant guides for specifics.&r"
		""
		"&6Dynamic Structures&r"
		"&7Deployers on dynamic structures work while moving, though held items are not visible.&r"
		"&7Right-click a Deployer on a dynamic structure to give it items, or use a Wrench to switch modes.&r"
		"&7They can automatically pull items from the structure's storage and return overflow items to it.&r"
		"&7If a deployed Schematic is placed in the filter slot, the Deployer will use it to place blocks from storage, enabling '&e3D printer&7' systems.&r"
		""
		"&8It does what you do—just more stubborn and tireless.&r"
	]
	quest.65B599AA9888FBF2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Celestial Mechanism&r"
		""
		"&7Harnessing harmonic crystals forged deep within star cores, the Celestial Mechanism unconditionally stabilizes the &etuning process&r&7, permanently enhancing its strength.&r"
	]
	quest.65B599AA9888FBF2.quest_subtitle: "Stellar Blessing"
	quest.660EAD8BBC2734CA.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Sloth\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When taking damage:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Deal \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"magic damage\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\" to all enemies within 2 blocks based on your armor value (1-second cooldown).\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Also triggers \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"35% damage reduction\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.660EAD8BBC2734CA.quest_subtitle: "Sloth Erosion"
	quest.660EAD8BBC2734CA.title: "Sloth Erosion"
	quest.66417960000F082A.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.66417960000F082A.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.66481C79877E0ED7.quest_subtitle: "Food Value >= 14"
	quest.66481C79877E0ED7.title: "Feast Recycling x10"
	quest.664DF00DAF0D957A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Flame Consolation&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Flame Consolation toughens the wearer's skin when on fire, granting &aresistance&r&7 to various damage types. However, it does nothing to the &cflames&r&7 themselves.&r"
	]
	quest.664DF00DAF0D957A.quest_subtitle: "Things That Fuel Burning"
	quest.664E9A6E52944333.quest_desc: [
		"&7Hold a &#FFCC44Lantern Clamp&7 in one hand and an &#66FF99Essence&7 in the other, then right-click to consume the &#66FF99Essence&7 and place the corresponding type of &#66FF99Essence Cluster&7, for decorative use."
		""
		"&7&#888888Shadow Essence&7 and &#66DDCCVoid Essence&7 cannot be used to place &#66FF99Essence Clusters&7."
		""
		"&7These clusters are pure condensates of arcane energy, with a thin protective layer to prevent overflow. They are nearly useless in magic but make for beautiful lamps."
	]
	quest.66B362ABCF6C2B8D.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#888888Tainted Stone&7 is a decorative block, and blocks crafted from it are immune to &#FFD700Totem&7 rituals. It is used to craft &#FFAA33Runes&7 on the &#CC99FFRune Workbench&7."
		""
		"&7Stone resists change, but the energy of the &#88DDFFreleased soul&7 is unstoppable."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7By forcing change with &#FF8844raw arcane energy&7, stone with practical magical properties can be produced. When using &#88DDFFholy arcane energy&7 as a catalyst, it forms &#9966CCTainted Stone&7, a stone that can neutralize surrounding magic."
	]
	quest.66B362ABCF6C2B8D.quest_subtitle: "Infused with Arcane Power"
	quest.66B362ABCF6C2B8D.title: "Essence Stone"
	quest.66D8D31B50D06630.quest_subtitle: "Hero of the Village...?"
	quest.66EA89C1E75509EB.quest_desc: ["&eOptional, not a mandatory quest. Does not affect most game content. Don't activate it unless necessary."]
	quest.66EA89C1E75509EB.quest_subtitle: "&6\"Once you take this step, there is no turning back\""
	quest.66EA89C1E75509EB.title: "&cAdded Suffering"
	quest.66F8BBB3BC24A7FF.quest_desc: [
		"&dThis lead, wrapped in an ominous aura, can capture the souls of most creatures..."
		""
		"&eUsed with a spawner, it can change the mob spawned, enabling efficient farming of desired drops—though the cost is high..."
	]
	quest.66F8BBB3BC24A7FF.quest_subtitle: "Origin Ball"
	quest.67A539CCFEDE8EBC.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.67A539CCFEDE8EBC.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.67D8839DF18183B2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pufferfish&r&7"
		"&7A common aquatic creature in the Abyss. Cannot survive out of water (flops around and slowly takes damage over time); &r"
		""
		"&7Right-click a Pufferfish with a water bucket to store it as an item (&#ADD8E6Pufferfish Bucket&r&7); &r"
		""
		"&7Only attacks when provoked, with a unique attack method; &r"
		""
		"&7When a Pufferfish takes damage, if the attacker is within 3 blocks: &r"
		""
		"&7The Pufferfish briefly swells (0.5-second wind-up), then deals damage and applies &aPoison I&r&7 for 3 seconds to the attacker; &r"
		""
		"&7If the damage is enough to kill the Pufferfish instantly, it cannot retaliate. &r"
	]
	quest.67D8839DF18183B2.title: "Pufferfish"
	quest.67F1B7217A46DF7E.quest_desc: [
		"&eFaint screams seem to echo from within."
		"&6Low consumption provides lasting power."
		""
		"⚡ Speed: 1.0x | ♨ Temperature: 3000 | ⏳ Consumption: 0.1"
		""
		"&aTip&r&7: &f♨ &r&7Temperature determines the tier of materials that can be processed, ⚡ Speed affects processing time, and ⏳ Consumption represents fuel longevity."
	]
	quest.67F1B7217A46DF7E.quest_subtitle: "Soul Incineration"
	quest.680583B3F5EF1CC2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Caustic Catalyst&r"
		""
		"&7&cInfernal Fire&r&7 and &bAzure Water&r&7 combine violently, often driving change and destruction. The Caustic Catalyst increases &atuning strength&r&7 as the &eCrucible&r&7's destabilization risk rises—in other words, using impending violent reactions for greater power.&r"
	]
	quest.680583B3F5EF1CC2.quest_subtitle: "Destabilizing Flames"
	quest.681DDFCA829035FB.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" is a large-scale general adventure mod that enhances vanilla Minecraft elements such as \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"potions, enchanting, spawners, and equipment\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", providing more adventuring depth and higher end-game ceilings.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Here, \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" is divided into several modules (not six). This modpack uses Apotheosis's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Enchanting Module\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Spawner Module\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.681DDFCA829035FB.quest_subtitle: "Crowning You with a False Divinity"
	quest.68780331B0515EB6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of the Overeager Fist"
		"&7The impulse within your soul makes you act without thinking.&r"
		"&7-&cSpell shots&r&7 fire immediately upon full charge&r"
		""
		"&7An impulse infused into form and soul.&r"
		"&7-&aSpell&r&7 charge time halved&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_the_overeager_fist.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.68780331B0515EB6.quest_subtitle: "Never Hesitate"
	quest.68780331B0515EB6.title: "Oath of the Overeager Fist"
	quest.688BD76E40216736.quest_desc: [
		"This modification causes the spawner to produce baby versions of mobs (if a baby variant exists). Otherwise, it has no effect."
		"The most direct use for this upgrade seems to be obtaining Turtle Shells."
	]
	quest.688BD76E40216736.quest_subtitle: "Don't Want to Grow Up"
	quest.688BD76E40216736.title: "Turtle Egg"
	quest.68954EBEC12D958D.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.68954EBEC12D958D.quest_subtitle: "Stage 3"
	quest.68EF2FB94A761FFD.quest_desc: [
		"&aI often hear the term \"experience\"—what others call knowledge gained over time."
		""
		"&7Its connection to the soul is not strong, &6but it is a part of the soul, and can be collected and repurposed for enchanting and repair."
		""
		"&eWhat most don't know is that it can also be condensed into physical form."
		""
		"&7I've heard rumors that it drops from ores, but &6the most reliable source is small ore clusters where souls dissipate&f&7—the experience left by souls is etched into the rock."
	]
	quest.68EF2FB94A761FFD.quest_subtitle: "Experiential Matter"
	quest.69049202784168C9.quest_desc: ["&7Right-click to swing a &#FFD700Whip&7 at enemies. Materials can increase your &#CC99FFFlying Sword damage&7."]
	quest.69049202784168C9.quest_subtitle: "Brave Wood"
	quest.6930993364FD1814.quest_subtitle: "Lower defense than other armor, but specializes in spell-related stats"
	quest.6A03DEB0CCE71AF2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Armor Plating&r"
		"&7Consumables used to increase the familiar's &aarmor value&r&7. Has 3 tiers, each with a usage cap.&r"
	]
	quest.6A8313927B15ECEE.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hungry Walker&r&7"
		"&7A creature that resembles an &#8A2BE2Enderman&r&7, but lacks the Enderman's &#ADFF2Fteleportation&r&7 ability and &#1E90FFwater weakness&r&7; &r"
		""
		"&7The Hungry Walker is a &8conditionally hostile&r&7 creature that only performs melee attacks. Successful hits also apply &FF8C00Hunger I&r&7 for 6 seconds; &r"
		""
		"&7It has a special &#FFD700aggression logic&r&7: &r"
		""
		"&7Regardless of whether the player attacks it first, an unprovoked Hungry Walker will &00CED1actively follow&r&7 the player and attempt one melee attack; &r"
		""
		"&7This attack has a unique animation (referred to as the &#DC143Cbite attack&r&7); &r"
		""
		"&7If the bite hits or is blocked by a shield: the Hungry Walker &A9A9A9quickly flees&r&7 and stops following for a while; &r"
		""
		"&7If the bite misses: the Hungry Walker keeps trying to attack until it lands one; &r"
		""
		"&7If a player or other creature &FF4500attacks&r&7 the Hungry Walker: &r"
		""
		"&7It becomes &FF0000enraged&r&7, immediately treats them as a hostile target, and relentlessly &DC143Cpursues&r&7 and attacks until one of them dies; &r"
		""
		"&7After that, its attack animation changes to a &808080arm-swing attack&r&7 (only cosmetic—damage and effects are identical); &r"
		""
		"&7All of the above attacks can be blocked by shields. &r"
	]
	quest.6A8313927B15ECEE.title: "Hungry Walker"
	quest.6ABFDDD6E155A37F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Shadow Snail&r&7"
		"&7A passive creature in the Starlight Dimension with &cextremely slow&r&7 movement."
		""
		"&7When damaged, it &bshells up&r&7 in place:"
		"&7While shelled and after, it cannot move, and &areceives 85% damage reduction from all damage types&r&7."
		"&7If it receives no further attacks for a few seconds, it emerges and resumes normal behavior. &r"
	]
	quest.6ABFDDD6E155A37F.title: "Shadow Snail"
	quest.6AC481C1ADA516D4.quest_desc: [
		"&7Creatures struck by a &#FFCC44Scythe&7 have their &#88DDFFsouls&7 briefly exposed. If they die during this exposure, they drop special items."
		""
		"&7Similarly, creatures struck by &#CC99FFspells&7 also have their &#88DDFFsouls&7 exposed, with the same effect."
		""
		"&7Which creatures drop which materials can be found on the next page."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7Summary:"
		""
		"&7Zombie flesh condenses into &#66BB66Putrid Essence&7"
		""
		"&7Skeleton bones crystallize into &#888888Chilled Bone Stone&7"
		""
		"&7Phantom wings twist into &#66CCFFStarlight Fabric&7"
		""
		"&7Breeze essence persists as &#FFDD55Wind Core&7"
		""
		"&7Enderman magic solidifies into &#CC66FFDistorted Energy Flow&7"
		""
		"&7Illager bones erode into &#AA4AFFSoul of Night"
		""
		"&7Mages and village guards' energy sanctifies into &#DD88FFSoul of Light"
	]
	quest.6AC481C1ADA516D4.quest_subtitle: "Leaking Magic"
	quest.6AE4DE3DC4964CB6.quest_subtitle: "Provides both armor and minor spell stats—very popular"
	quest.6AF6ADCEE5546549.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#FFD700Totem Base&7 serves as the base block for totems. Right-click to start or stop a spirit ritual. When active, a &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect the number of totem poles in the structure."
		"&7The material of the &#FFD700Totem Base&7 and totem poles (&#FFAA33Runic Wood&7/&#888888Soulwood&7) must match. Totems built with &#888888Soulwood&7 perform corrupted versions of rituals."
		""
		"&7Totem poles are inscribed by right-clicking a &#FFAA33Runic Log&7 or &#888888Soul Log&7 with &#66FF99Essence&7, which is consumed. The emblem type matches the &#66FF99Essence&7 used."
		"&7The direction of multiple totem poles must be consistent. Direction is determined by the facing direction when inscribed, not the log's orientation."
		"&7Right-clicking a totem pole with an Axe removes the emblem, returning the log (essence is not refunded)."
		"&7When the totem is inactive, using a &#88DDFFTotem Staff&7 toggles the emblem's active state for decoration only."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Ritual ranges are generally centered on the &#FFD700Totem Base&7, except for directional effect blocks. Holding a &#88DDFFTotem Staff&7 displays the ritual range."
		""
		"&7Totems of the same spirit ritual interfere with each other. If a ritual range includes another &#FFD700Totem Base&7, or another ritual's range includes this base, the first activated totem will be deactivated."
		""
		"&7Blocks crafted from &#888888Tainted Stone&7 or &#9966CCCorrupted Stone&7 are immune to spirit rituals."
	]
	quest.6AF6ADCEE5546549.quest_subtitle: "&6Miracles Manifest in the World"
	quest.6AF6ADCEE5546549.title: "Totem Magic"
	quest.6B03AFED832B87A7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starlight Sea&r"
		"&7The most common marine biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Unlike the Overworld's oceans, the Starlight Sea has a &aflatter&r&7 seabed."
		"&7&#9ACD32Abyssal Fruit&r&7 plants and &#87CEEBSea Ball Flowers&r&7 are the main vegetation."
		"&7Areas near land or the Abyss biome may feature dense &#FF6B6Bcoral reefs&r&7 (similar to Overworld warm oceans)."
		""
		"&7Aside from &#483D8BTower Squid&r&7, most aquatic creatures spawn in other marine biomes."
		"&7Non-aquatic creatures can only spawn dozens of blocks below the Starlight Sea."
	]
	quest.6B03AFED832B87A7.quest_subtitle: "A star falls from heaven!"
	quest.6B03AFED832B87A7.title: "Starlight Sea"
	quest.6B49DEF95C8C0D96.quest_desc: ["&7Sprinting while holding consumes durability to increase &FFAA33movement speed&7. Wait, it doesn't consume durability when you're not sprinting—how does that work?"]
	quest.6B49DEF95C8C0D96.quest_subtitle: "Travel Tool"
	quest.6B5F16B4F3E12902.quest_desc: ["&r&5Arcana (0%–100%): &r&7Determines the chance of \"rare enchantments\" appearing. When Arcana reaches 100%, some common enchantments (like Sharpness) become rare."]
	quest.6B82BD57F8A68CEE.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.6B97738CD8E10A57.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Self-Care"
		"&7Hunger is the loss of self.&r&cAt low hunger, health loss accelerates dramatically"
		"&7Celebrate, enjoy good food, and cleanse the soul.&r&aFood restores more saturation&r&aEating food removes negative effects"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_self_care.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6B97738CD8E10A57.quest_subtitle: "Nurturing the Self"
	quest.6B97738CD8E10A57.title: "Pact of Self-Care"
	quest.6BC39E8AB37961DD.quest_desc: ["Simple, honest stats—gets the job done."]
	quest.6BC39E8AB37961DD.quest_subtitle: "Simple and Honest"
	quest.6BE787CD7C0F7128.quest_subtitle: "Kill Kill Kill"
	quest.6BE9E4190B1E6A4C.quest_desc: ["Right-click to clear invasions for a period of time, including future ones"]
	quest.6BE9E4190B1E6A4C.quest_subtitle: "Tired of annoying invasions?"
	quest.6BF48D5C9D1B191A.quest_desc: [
		"&7Once you craft a &#66DDCCDisk&7, a new storage option becomes available: the &#66CCFFPortable Terminal&7. This terminal requires charging via a &#FFD700Tesla Coil&7."
		""
		"&7Unfortunately, it can only hold one &#66DDCCDisk&7, so its capacity for stackable items is lower than a &#66DDCCSophisticated Backpack&7. However, it's quite good for storing non-stackable items."
		""
		"&7Even if you just craft it without using the reward's &#FFAA3364K disk&7, it's still worth it ("
	]
	quest.6BF48D5C9D1B191A.quest_subtitle: "Portable Space"
	quest.6C0395DDA06A6B98.quest_subtitle: "Used for Casting Plates"
	quest.6C33A7DFF72E3C76.quest_desc: [
		"Summon by placing a Carved Lunaris Cactus Fruit on top of an Aethersent Block."
		""
		"&6Behavior&r"
		"&7Anti-air utility creature that only targets &ca small subset of airborne hostile creatures&r&7."
		"&7When attacking, it has &aextremely high&r&7 attack speed, &aextremely long&r&7 range, and &aextremely wide&r&7 area damage. However, its attacks &ccannot harm&r&7 non-airborne creatures."
		""
		"&7When no &eMeteors&r&7 or valid targets are nearby, &6Aethersent Golems&r&7 will not retaliate even if attacked."
		""
		"&6Intercepting Aethersent Meteors&r"
		"&7When an &6Aethersent Golem&r&7 is on the surface during a &cMeteor Shower&r&7, it will shoot down falling &eMeteors&r&7 mid-air."
		"&7Shot-down &eMeteors&r&7 still drop their corresponding items."
		"&7&cComet Creepers&r&7 are also prevented from spawning if the meteor is destroyed."
	]
	quest.6C33A7DFF72E3C76.quest_subtitle: "Planetary Protection Policy"
	quest.6C33A7DFF72E3C76.title: "Aethersent Golem"
	quest.6C8EF5FE6AB70D3B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Aircraft are excellent travel tools. Different models offer different performance for different tasks—some are extremely fast for scouting structures, others are stable for building. If you're willing to invest some materials, there's one that can help."
		""
		"&7Just be careful not to crash..."
	]
	quest.6C8EF5FE6AB70D3B.quest_subtitle: "Bring Feather Falling—there's some turbulence ahead"
	quest.6C8EF5FE6AB70D3B.title: "Set Sail for the Skies"
	quest.6C9DC507DF212214.quest_subtitle: "Quickly create Silent Gear material compatibility"
	quest.6CA6DCCDEB5167BD.quest_desc: [
		"&6&#55AAFFStarlight Dimension&r"
		"&7A dreamscape isomorphic yet alien to the Overworld. &#55AAFFStars hang low&r&7, plants flourish, and &#55AAFFcelestial phenomena are breathtaking&r&7—as if sinking into an eternal dream."
		""
		"&6Dimension Log: &r"
		"&7Elevation distribution is similar to the Overworld. Most naturally generated blocks correspond to the Overworld, but surface blocks and vegetation are mostly &#55AAFFblue-toned&r&7, while the sky is a blend of purple starfield and &#FFAA00warm twilight orange&r&7."
		"&7Divided at &cY=0&r&7 into the upper &8Grimstone Layer&r&7 and lower &8Voidstone Layer&r&7."
		"&7Decorative plants are far more varied and lush than in the Overworld."
		"&7In addition to regular weather, unique phenomena like &dMeteor Showers&r&7 and &dAuroras&r&7 occur."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Basic Rules: &r"
		"&7Teleportation & Coordinates: Scale is &a1.0&r&7, matching Overworld coordinates 1:1."
		""
		"&7Time & Sky: Time is frozen at eternal &FFAA00twilight&r&7 (12900), with a custom &dpurple starfield&r&7 and &FFAA00warm orange canopy&r&7."
		""
		"&7Lighting Rules: No day-night cycle; sky provides light. Base ambient light is &c0&r&7. Monsters spawn at light levels &c0–7&r&7."
		""
		"&7Buildings & Respawning: Height range &b-64 to 384&r&7. &aBeds&r&7 and &aRespawn Anchors&r&7 work safely."
		""
		"&7Ecology & Threats: Raids cannot trigger. &cPiglins&r&7, &cPiglin Brutes&r&7, and &cHoglins&r&7 from the Nether become &8zombified&r&7 here."
	]
	quest.6CA6DCCDEB5167BD.quest_subtitle: "Days Gone By"
	quest.6CA6DCCDEB5167BD.title: "Eternal Starlight"
	quest.6CC1EDF75BF739C0.quest_desc: ["&7Boosts both mana cap and attack speed—both are essential stats. Extremely cheap to craft."]
	quest.6CC1EDF75BF739C0.quest_subtitle: "Holy Cow, Ice"
	quest.6CE4032D222E50F3.quest_desc: ["&7Look at these numbers—this is how you know it's &#FF6666overpowered&7."]
	quest.6CE4032D222E50F3.quest_subtitle: "Theoretical Best"
	quest.6CF68E9E0A3CB0E7.quest_desc: [
		"&7Natural Quartz, as the name suggests, is a naturally occurring equivalent to &6Nether Quartz&r&7. It has most of the same uses."
		""
		"&eIt is quite rare&r&7 and can be found deep underground, often forming &6geodes&r&7."
	]
	quest.6D0D20A34E2B3703.quest_desc: [
		"&7When right-clicked in the &bStarlight Dimension&r&7, it switches the current weather to a &cMeteor Shower&r&7 after a short delay. Very useful for players seeking &eAethersent&r&7 resources."
		""
		"&7Using it outside the Starlight Dimension will &cfail&r."
	]
	quest.6D0D20A34E2B3703.quest_subtitle: "Make a Wish"
	quest.6D571AC85912D827.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune Base&r"
		"&7The foundation for crafting all other runes. Found in small quantities in some &bvanilla structures&r&7, and more commonly in &cIron's Spells & Spellbooks&r&7 structures. Each type of mage drops a rune of its corresponding school upon death (except Necromancers).&r"
		""
		"&8\"A pale foundation crystallized from the final embers of a mage's soul, anchoring all runic laws.\""
	]
	quest.6D571AC85912D827.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Material"
	quest.6D7E037569A98460.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the High Priest"
		"&7Overbearing control brings harm.&r&cInteraction distance bonuses go on cooldown after being hit&r&cMovement speed reduced while the buff is on cooldown"
		"&7The whole world is yours.&r&aBlock interaction distance increased by one fifth, entity interaction distance increased by one tenth"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_high_priest.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6D7E037569A98460.quest_subtitle: "Extending the Self"
	quest.6D7E037569A98460.title: "Pact of the High Priest"
	quest.6D895DFB1144DF16.quest_desc: [
		"&6Yeti Fur&r&7"
		"&7Obtained by killing Yetis or shearing them with Shears (drops &#F5F5DCWhite Yeti Fur&r&7); &r"
		""
		"&7Yeti Fur is a flammable building block similar to Wool; &r"
		""
		"&7Creatures landing on it take no fall damage and bounce up (like Slime Blocks); &r"
		""
		"&7Yeti Fur can also block sound detection by &8Sculk Sensors&r&7 / &8Sculk Shriekers&r&7; &r"
		""
		"&7Yetis are white by default and cannot be dyed like sheep. Non-white variants must be crafted manually. &r"
	]
	quest.6D895DFB1144DF16.title: "Yeti Fur"
	quest.6D937711826032A4.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6D937711826032A4.quest_subtitle: "Absolute Power! The Solitude It Brings, Who Taught Him Its Value Is..."
	quest.6DB8BE45F81F4357.title: "Discover the Blaze Arena"
	quest.6E0EE5297B295288.quest_subtitle: "&eAll neutral mobs will be hostile to you"
	quest.6E0EE5297B295288.title: "&e\"The defiled body is no longer pure\""
	quest.6E25E82DBD18D2C8.quest_subtitle: "&cThe world will be plunged into eternal night"
	quest.6E25E82DBD18D2C8.title: "&c\"Eternal journey under the endless night\""
	quest.6E7D9FC91B09210C.quest_desc: ["Though it has solid stats, Ghost Form prevents damage from regular weapons—best paired with special attack methods."]
	quest.6E7D9FC91B09210C.quest_subtitle: "Immortal Rebirth"
	quest.6E995B7F0867CE19.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.6F1B0D7041FBCD4B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of the Great Rock's Protection&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of the Great Rock's Protection functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bGreat Rock's Protection&r&7 effect, slightly reducing &adamage&r&7 taken, with increased effect when unarmored.&r"
	]
	quest.6F1B0D7041FBCD4B.quest_subtitle: "Protective Pulse"
	quest.6F5E956AAA173600.quest_subtitle: "Used for Casting Ingots"
	quest.6F6ACDE9BCEFD6A5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Cloudskipper"
		"&7What you rely on will ultimately destroy you.&r&cFall damage doubled"
		"&7Gravity—the hardest force to defy.&r&aWind propulsion is increased and grants lift&r&aLift enhances airborne capabilities"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_cloudskipper.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6F6ACDE9BCEFD6A5.quest_subtitle: "Soaring Above All"
	quest.6F6ACDE9BCEFD6A5.title: "Pact of the Cloudskipper"
	quest.6F7643BD60F5534F.quest_desc: ["&7Mines &FFAA333×3×3&7 areas of dirt."]
	quest.6F7643BD60F5534F.quest_subtitle: "Big Scoop"
	quest.6F7DF3491AA2E9DF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Parasite"
		"&7Your vulnerabilities remain significant.&r&cHealing received reduced by two fifths"
		"&7Surplus confidence flows into the mind; pain no longer matters.&r&aHarvesting essence grants damage absorption"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_parasite.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6F7DF3491AA2E9DF.quest_subtitle: "Borrowing Shields to Support Yourself"
	quest.6F7DF3491AA2E9DF.title: "Pact of the Parasite"
	quest.6FA8C31F0875CB8E.quest_desc: [
		"&7The most common use is for restocking Totems of Undying. Filling your offhand with totems and carrying a full backpack of them lets you achieve \"How are you still alive?\" status. But don't ask me how to get a backpack full of totems..."
		""
		"&7Can also be used in other cases to automatically fill your hotbar with items for convenience."
	]
	quest.6FA8C31F0875CB8E.quest_subtitle: "I Only See Endless Totems of Undying"
	quest.6FDF4D8E43BF594B.quest_desc: [
		"&7As a fundamental material, it is widely used in &#FFAA33Rune crafting&7, &#66CCFFEssence Crucible&7 mineral multiplication, &#CC99FFEssence Altar&7 item crafting, &#88DDFFRepair Pylon&7 tool restoration, and &#FFD700Totem rituals&7."
		""
		"&7Using weapons with the &#CC6666#malum:soul_hunter_weapon&7 tag (including but not limited to all types of &#FFCC44Scythes&7, &#66DDCCSoul-Stained Steel&7 tools and weapons, and &#CC6666Malevolent&7 weapons) applies the &#88DDFFSoul Shatter&7 effect to specific creatures. Killing them during this effect yields &#66FF99Essence&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7In most cases, &#66FF99Essence&7 is obtained as follows:"
		""
		"&#88DDFFHoly Essence&7 can be obtained by killing passive creatures"
		"e.g., &66DD88Cows&7, &66DD88Dolphins&7"
		""
		"&#CC6666Malevolent Essence&7 can be obtained by killing hostile creatures"
		"e.g., &CC6666Zombies&7, &CC6666Spiders&7"
		""
		"&#CC99FFArcane Essence&7 can be obtained by killing creatures with special attack patterns"
		"e.g., &CC99FFSkeletons&7, &CC99FFBlazes&7"
		""
		"&#DDA0DDEldritch Essence&7 can be obtained by killing rare creatures"
		"e.g., &DDA0DDEndermen&7, &DDA0DDEvokers&7, &DDA0DDElder Guardians&7"
		""
		"&#66DDCCVoid Essence&7 can be obtained by killing mounts and flying creatures"
		"e.g., &66DDCCCats&7, &66DDCCBats&7"
		""
		"&#66BB66Earth Essence&7 can be obtained by killing ground-based creatures"
		"e.g., &66BB66Zombies&7, &66BB66Iron Golems&7"
		""
		"&#FF6633Infernal Essence&7 can be obtained by killing Nether or special creatures"
		"e.g., &FF6633Blazes&7, &FF6633Piglins&7, &FF6633Creepers&7"
		""
		"&#3399FFAquatic Essence&7 can be obtained by killing aquatic animals"
		"e.g., &3399FFDolphins&7, &3399FFDrowned&7"
	]
	quest.6FDF4D8E43BF594B.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Components"
	quest.6FE5B91598B5393A.quest_desc: ["Early on, nothing beats raw base stat bonuses."]
	quest.6FE5B91598B5393A.quest_subtitle: "Excellent Base Damage Bonus"
	quest.6FF16C84BFDC23B4.quest_desc: ["&7Top-tier traits and stats. Offers solid base values and good damage scaling. Obtained after defeating the Fire-Receiver. A key component in any build, and synergizes well with Gobber Ingots and Nether Gobber Ingots."]
	quest.6FF16C84BFDC23B4.quest_subtitle: "May Your Journey Be Filled with Curses and Blessings"
	quest.701467707AD4CCE8.quest_subtitle: "Used for Casting Gems"
	quest.70195B5ED5D18F70.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Skybreaker"
		"&7Bloody vengeance must be repaid with destruction.&r&cKnockback taken is doubled"
		"&7Gravity—the strongest force imposed on others.&r&aFall damage automatically attacks nearby creatures&r&aDealing fall damage ignores distance and hits the target"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_skybreaker.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.70195B5ED5D18F70.quest_subtitle: "Bringing Down All Things"
	quest.70195B5ED5D18F70.title: "Pact of the Skybreaker"
	quest.70A16F668336C964.quest_desc: [
		"The Enchanting Module brings a more powerful and progressive enchanting experience to Minecraft."
		"Here, enchantment outcomes are no longer determined solely by enchantment level. Instead, they are influenced by five attributes: &a&lEterna&r&r, &4&lQuanta&r&r, &5&lArcana&r&r, &e&lStability&r&r, and &3Enchantment Hints&r."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"In the current version, the specific values and meanings are as follows:"
		"&a&lEterna&r&r: Represents the source of power, ranging from 0 to 100. It indicates the minimum level required for the highest enchantment tier. Like vanilla, higher levels yield better enchantments."
		"&4&lQuanta&r&r: Represents entropy/chaos, ranging from 0% to 100%. It affects the upper and lower limits of enchantment outcomes. Higher values cause greater fluctuation in the actual enchantment level. For example, with &a&lEterna&r&r 100 and &4&lQuanta&r&r 90%, using the third row to enchant any enchantable item results in a final enchantment level range of [10, 190]. Default is 15%."
		"&l&5Arcana&r&r: Represents the gift of mystery, ranging from 0% to 100%. It determines the chance of obtaining &brare enchantments&r. Certain enchantments require a minimum Arcana value to appear (e.g., Miner's Fervor). To prevent important vanilla enchantments from being crowded out at high Arcana, when Arcana reaches 100%, important enchantments like Sharpness become rare."
		"&l&eStability&r&r: Represents world stability, provided by the Geode-Sealed Stable Bookshelf. It eliminates Quanta's negative impact on the lower limit. With Stability, the above Quanta example yields a range of [100, 190]."
		"&3Enchantment Hints&r: Represents the sight of truth. The value indicates how many rows of enchantment results can be previewed before enchanting. Some advanced bookshelves affect this value. Default is 1 hint."
	]
	quest.70A16F668336C964.quest_subtitle: "Enhanced Enchanting Power"
	quest.70A16F668336C964.title: "Apotheosis—Enchanting Module"
	quest.70B6CF3213A607ED.quest_desc: [
		"Never imagined I'd find someone in the group chat willing to help with server testing and setup."
		""
		"They helped Cod with server testing for a long time (and shout-out to everyone who played on that server and gave feedback!)"
	]
	quest.70B6CF3213A607ED.quest_subtitle: "Server Testing + Setup"
	quest.70F085FC6F1CAAF2.quest_desc: [
		"&7Before you leave, a reminder: &rThe modpack has a clear stage progression. You can check the &dQuest&r chapter for specific boss stages. Before defeating a stage boss, bosses from later stages cannot be challenged."
		""
		"&7They have placed an invisible curse on the ores they claim, meaning you must defeat them to unlock those ores—otherwise, you'll never find them even if you mine to the center of the earth."
		""
		"&7The main quest line unfolds through story segments. Aside from the beginning, other story parts are scattered across additional nodes. You can skip them, but just a heads-up: the main quest order follows the story's chronological progression."
	]
	quest.70F085FC6F1CAAF2.quest_subtitle: "It's Time..."
	quest.70F085FC6F1CAAF2.title: "Set Off"
	quest.713CA5306C2B86A2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Connector&r"
		""
		"&7Place two Connectors facing each other. With a &eCopper Wire Spool&7, right-click each connector. A powered wire appears between them, consuming the spool and returning an empty one. Energy can then flow between them.&r"
		""
		"&8Removing either Connector breaks the wire, dropping four Copper Wires.&r"
		""
		"&7Pull, connect—with one wire, energy flows.&r"
	]
	quest.714645D7B7F4C7BA.quest_desc: [
		"&7Can be crafted into &#A020F0Shadow Snail Shell Dust: &r&7"
		""
		"&7Obtained by decomposing &#A020F0Shadow Snail Shells&r&7 in a crafting grid; &r"
		""
		"&7Works like Bone Meal—can be used to advance crops to their next growth stage; &r"
		""
		"&7Also works on saplings, mushrooms, and other plants that Bone Meal can affect; &r"
		""
		"&7Can also be crafted into Black Dye. &r"
	]
	quest.71944D592D710B99.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.71944D592D710B99.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.71B24EEAADB29F3A.quest_desc: [
		"&7Use a &#FFD700Reforging Hammer&7 on the &#CC99FFweapon&7 whose stats you want to change, then reforge it on an &#66DDCCAnvil&7 to reroll its &#FFAA33stats&7."
		""
		"&7You can obtain three types of &#FFD700Reforging Hammers&7 by trading with villagers, or craft them yourself—much more convenient."
		"&7You can reforge &#CC99FFweapons&7, &#66CCFFarmor&7, tools, and trinkets. For melee &#CC99FFweapons&7, the best affix is usually &#FFD700Legendary&7; for ranged, it's &#66CCFFEthereal&7; trinket and armor affixes cover various aspects."
		""
		"Best trinket affixes:"
		"&#66FF66Blessed&7: +&#FFAA332&7 armor"
		"&#FF6666Menacing&7: +&#FFAA334%&7 attack damage"
		"&#FFD700Lucky&7: +&#FFAA332%&7 crit chance"
		""
		"&7Since base crit multiplier is only &#FFAA33150%&7, &#FFD700Lucky&7 is rarely better than &#FF6666Menacing&7—not recommended."
		""
		"&7Reforging comes with risks. In the early game, don't go overboard—good enough is fine."
		"&7Reforging often consumes a lot of &#66DDCCAnvil&7 durability; you can use the &#FFD700Anvil Upgrade&7 from the &#66CCFFSophisticated Backpack&7 to save iron ingots."
	]
	quest.71B24EEAADB29F3A.quest_subtitle: "Because Too Many People Asked, It's in the Main Quest Now"
	quest.71B24EEAADB29F3A.title: "Mastering the Craft"
	quest.71C2AB4CCFAA1C59.quest_desc: ["&7Increases the spawner's spawn range. Each upgrade adds 2 blocks, up to 48 blocks. Can be combined with Quartz to reduce spawn range for tighter concentration."]
	quest.71C2AB4CCFAA1C59.quest_subtitle: "Factory Expansion Required"
	quest.71EB7660FA903627.quest_subtitle: "Magical Material"
	quest.7220F1709920A6DC.quest_desc: ["&7A base trinket that only provides a small amount of &#FF8844armor&7. A necessary prerequisite for crafting its higher-tier variants."]
	quest.7220F1709920A6DC.quest_subtitle: "Trinket Base"
	quest.72387868BC05D119.quest_desc: ["&7The Nether seems to have changed... more &#FF6666dangerous&7 than usual... Proceed with caution."]
	quest.72387868BC05D119.quest_subtitle: "Everything Is Terrifying!!!"
	quest.72387868BC05D119.title: "Gate to the Inferno"
	quest.7241681266CB77A7.quest_desc: [
		"&7Now you can truly make spellbooks from &#66CCFFIron&7."
		""
		"&7The &#CC99FFspell slots&7 are determined by the material, as is the &#CC99FFspell power boost&7."
	]
	quest.7241681266CB77A7.quest_subtitle: "Iron! Magic"
	quest.727B996FAE26B0BB.quest_desc: [
		"&7Use a &#FFD700Seer Orb&7 to right-click the portal frame and activate the &#CC99FFFissure&7."
		""
		"&7After the chaotic &#CC99FFFissures&7 gradually closed, the power to open them was sealed within the &#FFD700Seer Orb&7. Only heroes recognized by the Gatekeeper can enter the &#CC99FFFissure&7."
		""
		"&7The Gatekeeper gave you some seeds, hoping you would go to the &#66CCFFStarlight Forest&7 and feed the &#FFAA33Starbirds&7 there. He hasn't returned to the &#66CCFFStarlight Forest&7 in a very long time."
		""
		"&7&#FFAA33Starbird&7 nests are usually found high in the canopy of the &#66CCFFStarlight Forest&7. Place seeds in the nests and feed nearby &#FFAA33Starbirds&7 to breed them. The &#FFAA33Starbirds&7 will reward you with random items, including special &#66DDCCforge materials&7."
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"[Click to Jump]\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"6CA6DCCDEB5167BD\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.727B996FAE26B0BB.quest_subtitle: "&mSwing Umbrella, Step into the Mud, Open!&r"
	quest.727B996FAE26B0BB.title: "Open the Door"
	quest.729E08704E144DC7.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"In the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-click\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" with this item and it will turn into a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"map\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" pointing to a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Castle structure\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.729E08704E144DC7.quest_subtitle: "How Does Smearing Materials on This Tell Me Where the Castle Is?"
	quest.72C552BE02BA433D.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Apotheosis Spawner Module provides players with more powerful and customizable spawners, along with convenient automation solutions for mob farms."
		""
		"&7Though there are many spawner attributes, they are straightforward. Here, they are introduced by their consumable materials."
	]
	quest.72C552BE02BA433D.quest_subtitle: "Super Mob Factory"
	quest.72C552BE02BA433D.title: "Apotheosis—Spawner Module"
	quest.72EADB2FF95D25B3.quest_subtitle: "Lower defense than other armor, but specializes in spell-related stats"
	quest.7306BEC7A3E98304.quest_subtitle: "Undead"
	quest.731473A765D3B6B6.quest_desc: [
		"&7When searching for traces of &darcane energy&r&7 across the land, the most commonly found is &bVoid Arcane Energy&r&7."
		"&7All &eweather phenomena&r&7 carry faint imprints of Void Arcane Energy; but essentially, they do not have the form of essence—only the &8residual memory&r&7 of their effects on the world."
		"&7Their influence has faded, but with a little effort, it can be restored."
		""
		"&7Everywhere, there are remnants of these &bwind memories&r&7—they have lost the power of wind and can only drift about."
		"&7However, by infusing them with &eVoid Arcane Energy&r&7, these memories can be rewoven with the flow of &darcane energy&r&7, restoring them to their former state."
		"&7They can once again affect the world."
		"&7Building on existing uses, with &eWind Charges&r&7 and &aWind Cores&r&7, I have found two new applications for this effect."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Wind Exciters"
		"&7Wind Charges carry scattered memories. They are chaotic in nature, releasing upon impact."
		"&7When activated by Redstone, a Wind Exciter weaves a &bstrong gust&r&7, pushing everything outward."
		"&7The intensity and shape of this effect can be configured with a Wrench."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Wind Tunnels"
		"&7Wind Cores are captured from strong winds—they are more powerful and directional."
		"&7When activated by a connected Wind Exciter, a Wind Tunnel continuously weaves an upward &ewind column&r&7, capable of moving most objects and creatures."
		"&7The distance and direction of this effect can be configured with a Wrench."
	]
	quest.731473A765D3B6B6.quest_subtitle: "Channeling Winds"
	quest.731473A765D3B6B6.title: "Wind Weaving"
	quest.732853B6E9D536CC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Aurora Antler&r&7"
		"&7A special drop obtained without killing the Aurora Deer; &r"
		""
		"&7Players need to &FFA500attack&r&7 the Aurora Deer to provoke it, then make its &00FFFFcharge attack&r&7 hit the side of &808080hard blocks&r&7 like stone, giving it a chance to drop &#FFA500Aurora Antlers&r&7. &r"
	]
	quest.734CF87743FF73AB.quest_desc: ["&7A base trinket that only provides a small amount of &#FF8844armor&7. A necessary prerequisite for crafting its higher-tier variants."]
	quest.734CF87743FF73AB.quest_subtitle: "Trinket Base"
	quest.737A6C878749DFB1.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#66FF66Wisps&7 search for nearby &#55D5D5Soul Sand&7, hide inside, and transform it into &#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7."
		""
		"&7&#66FF66Wisps&7 will remain hidden in &#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 for a very long time before emerging, converting it into &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7."
		""
		"&7The resulting &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7 inherits the appropriate archeology loot table based on the biome/structure it is in."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Soul-Infused Soul Sand created by players or naturally generated in some cases does not have this conversion property."
		""
		"&7Applying &#FFD700Honeycomb&7 to &#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 disables its conversion ability (it can no longer become &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7)."
		""
		"&7Only tools with &#66CCFFSilk Touch&7 will drop the correct item when broken."
		""
		"&7Holding a brush and long-pressing right-click on &#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 that contains a &#66FF66Wisp&7 will force it out of the block, turning it into &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7."
	]
	quest.737A6C878749DFB1.quest_subtitle: "Strange Souls"
	quest.737AC021C2A2CF1D.quest_desc: [
		"&2During travels, you often encounter well-enchanted gear that you can't use—truly a pity."
		""
		"&6This Disenchantment Lexicon can be used on an anvil to transfer half (rounded up) of random enchantments from an item into books. It consumes (number of enchantments × 10) levels of experience to produce enchanted books, destroying the original item in the process."
		""
		"&eCan also be used repeatedly on marked equipment to reroll the enchantments that will be extracted."
	]
	quest.737AC021C2A2CF1D.quest_subtitle: "Recycling"
	quest.73E6FF96B1846AF3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Fortress"
		"&7The majestic exterior and the weary nature are inseparable.&r&cSoul shield recovery rate halved"
		"&7The compressed form of the soul shield—grand and precise.&r&aIncreases soul shield capacity&r&aSoul shield stability increased by half"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_fortress.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.73E6FF96B1846AF3.quest_subtitle: "Standing Firm"
	quest.73E6FF96B1846AF3.title: "Pact of the Fortress"
	quest.7458C276CADE77AC.quest_desc: ["Functions like a vanilla Shield."]
	quest.7458C276CADE77AC.quest_subtitle: "Better Defense"
	quest.746B034A029684EA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Smart Filter&r"
		"&7Offers more complex control over output and input filtering.&r"
		"&7Right-click to open the configuration GUI. Items can be marked in the top slots. Buttons from left to right: Blacklist/Whitelist, Match/Ignore NBT, Clear, Confirm.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7If a List Filter or Attribute Filter containing info is marked, the filter logic uses it (OR logic between marks; blacklist uses NOT).&r"
		"&7Example: Filter A is a List Filter with Iron Sword and Gold Sword on blacklist. Filter B is an Attribute Filter marking \"not full durability.\" Filter C marks A and B as blacklist, simplifying to (Iron Sword OR Gold Sword) AND full durability.&r"
		"&7Filters can be nested for more complex filtering.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Attribute Filter&r"
		"&7Filters based on item '&eattributes&r&7' for greater flexibility, delivering smarter results in automated processing (though basic filters are still irreplaceable).&r"
		"&7Right-click to open the GUI. Place a reference item to see its attributes. Scroll through them, then click [&a+&r&7] or [&c+!&r&7] to add as a positive or negative condition. Multiple conditions can be added, with matching logic configurable in the lower-left corner.&r"
	]
	quest.746B034A029684EA.title: "Filter"
	quest.746FA8AC7777829D.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 is a block that players can pass through."
		""
		"&7Except for players, no other creatures can pass through &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 (they will also avoid it in pathfinding)."
		""
		"&7&#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 only has collision on its top face."
		""
		"&7Players can stand on top of &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 normally, but sneaking players will fall through."
		""
		"&7These properties make &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 an excellent choice for doors or \"elevators\" in player shelters."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Players passing through &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 have reduced movement speed; wearing equipment with the &#66CCFFSoul Speed&7 enchantment can negate this effect."
		""
		"&7Using a &#FFD700Flint and Steel&7 or &#FFD700Fire Charge&7 on &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 will change its texture and emit light (light level: &#FFAA3312&7) while retaining all other properties."
	]
	quest.746FA8AC7777829D.quest_subtitle: "Phasmophobia"
	quest.7494DCB39DEAF4F5.quest_desc: [
		"&7This should be considered an improved terminal. I removed its reliance on &#66DDCCDisks&7, sacrificing some functionality for maximum storage space."
		""
		"&7Requires charging before use. Sneak + Right-click the &#66CCFFTerminal&7 to bind it. Once bound, you can access its contents remotely at any time. Use a &#FFD700Tesla Coil&7 to recharge it."
	]
	quest.7494DCB39DEAF4F5.quest_subtitle: "Remote Storage"
	quest.74F6BCC9482F2FD6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Reciprocation"
		"&7Only &cstruggle&r&7 remains within you.&r&cDisables natural soul shield recovery"
		"&7A metamorphosis—a new mechanism of denial."
		"&r&aDealing magic damage restores soul shield&r"
		"&aSignificantly increases soul shield capacity&r"
		"&aSoul shield recovery amount doubled"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_reciprocation.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.74F6BCC9482F2FD6.quest_subtitle: "Double the Payback"
	quest.74F6BCC9482F2FD6.title: "Pact of Reciprocation"
	quest.7501056B288C71E1.quest_subtitle: "Food Value > 8"
	quest.7535B9010BCF5E06.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Flame Embrace&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Flame Embrace functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting a burning wearer a half-strength &bFlame Embrace&r&7 effect, extinguishing &cflames&r&7 and providing &aconstant healing&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.7535B9010BCF5E06.quest_subtitle: "Extinguishing Pulse"
	quest.754B74CB9D6E7C5A.quest_desc: [
		"&7Allows the spawner to spawn mobs even when no players are nearby."
		""
		"&7Use with caution..."
	]
	quest.754B74CB9D6E7C5A.quest_subtitle: "Unmanned Factory Overrun"
	quest.756DE36F8CEBB947.quest_subtitle: "Star Traveler"
	quest.75DF4040BA1F636B.quest_desc: ["&7Spawns mobs on fire."]
	quest.75DF4040BA1F636B.quest_subtitle: "Proper Heat Treatment"
	quest.75EB87C487763166.quest_desc: [
		"By placing all five runic logs above a Totem Base with Arcane Essence inscribed, the &bRelease Ritual&r can be activated. This ritual significantly alters the nearby environment and spawns Soul Saplings."
		""
		"&7After further study, I found that the &6Soul Trees&r&7 produced by the &bRelease Ritual&r&7 have become a separate species, completely different from the original &eRunic Trees&r&7. Their growth patterns and traits are different..."
		""
		"&7It seems the &dessence scar&r&7 that created them affects more than just color and magical properties. The most notable differences are form and leaf color. Soul Trees are taller and thinner than Runic Trees, with sickly purplish-red leaves instead of the bright orange-yellow of Runic Trees. Still, their uses are largely the same."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Soul Tree Study: Growth"
		"&7Like &8Corruption&r&7, their saplings respond to &dessence arcane energy&r&7 and common fertilizers like Bone Meal, with similar results."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Soul Tree Study: Corruption"
		"&7Another notable difference is their effect on surroundings. For instance, they reproduce the &bDirectionless Ritual&r&7 with their growth energy, transmuting surroundings into Corruption. It's best to plant them in a safe, controlled area."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Soul Tree Study: Resin"
		"&7The viscous sap of Soul Trees seems to accumulate more easily than Runic Trees. The resulting resin is also corrupted in effect. &cCursed Resin&r&7 doesn't restore my vitality—instead, it enhances it, increasing attack power and providing damage resistance."
	]
	quest.75EB87C487763166.quest_subtitle: "Twisted Saplings"
	quest.760AED607B00C7CA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Arcanophage"
		"&7The soul resides in the form for a reason.&r"
		"&7-Half of all damage taken becomes magic damage&r"
		"&7-Soul shield stability halved&r"
		"&7A part of your soul leaks out to attract arcane energy.&r&aShattering souls yields extra arcane energy&r&aHarvesting essence improves most magic stats"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_arcanaphage.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.760AED607B00C7CA.quest_subtitle: "Beyond the Self"
	quest.760AED607B00C7CA.title: "Pact of the Arcanophage"
	quest.76418D5CB8DDA0B1.quest_desc: ["You only truly realize how many bugs there are to fix once you actually start playtesting..."]
	quest.76418D5CB8DDA0B1.quest_subtitle: "Guinea Pig"
	quest.7655A85408A81AA1.quest_desc: [
		"If you encounter a wild familiar, you may be able to gain its assistance by offering Arcane Essence."
		""
		"&eYou may also use the Summoning Ritual to summon familiars."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Familiar Basics&r"
		"&7Familiars can be tamed with &bArcane Essence&r&7. Right-click a familiar with a stick to set it to &astay&r&7, keeping it stationary and preventing attacks. Tamed familiars can be &asummoned/dismissed&r&7 by selecting them in the familiar selection interface. The selection interface can be opened via the corresponding keybind, after which you can use the summon/dismiss hotkey to control your selected familiar. Once you acquire the '&cLearn Necromancy&r&7' advancement, familiars will avoid death at the cost of &emana&r&7—but if your mana runs out, they will still die.&r"
	]
	quest.7655A85408A81AA1.quest_subtitle: "Finding Familiars"
	quest.7655A85408A81AA1.title: "Eternal Companions"
	quest.768F736B2B18FA1B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of the Overkeen Eye"
		"&7The perception in your soul makes you prepared.&r"
		"&7-&cSpell shot&r&7 recovery rate halved&r"
		""
		"&7An arcane-seeking eye fused into the soul.&r"
		"&7-&eStaff projectiles&r&7 &atrack&r&7 targets&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_the_overkeen_eye.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.768F736B2B18FA1B.quest_subtitle: "A Hundred Steps, One Shot"
	quest.768F736B2B18FA1B.title: "Oath of the Overkeen Eye"
	quest.76B78E211A0AEC85.quest_subtitle: "Higher armor stats than regular armor, at the cost of mana-related stats"
	quest.76BD72A25B241E0C.quest_desc: ["&7Using the light of Glowstone, I improved the Nether Bookshelf. It now provides additional &4Quanta&7 along with a small amount of &5Arcana&7. Though still not as good as the Ocean Bookshelf, every bit counts."]
	quest.76BD72A25B241E0C.quest_subtitle: "A More Balanced Nether Bookshelf"
	quest.76BD72A25B241E0C.title: "Chaos Expansion"
	quest.771C9B9ADDCDA5E6.quest_desc: ["A dragon has treasures all over its body—provides excellent armor and base attack bonuses."]
	quest.771C9B9ADDCDA5E6.quest_subtitle: "You're a Dragon Too, Huh"
	quest.773AC14F2AF8822B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Nether Quartz is the most unique adjustment item. When used, it must be paired with other adjustment items (it itself is not consumed, similar to a wrench). Quartz reverses the magic of the paired adjustment item, producing the &eopposite&r effect of using the item alone."
		""
		"When using Quartz, place the other adjustment item in your offhand."
	]
	quest.773AC14F2AF8822B.quest_subtitle: "Reverse Adjustment"
	quest.7779D406142005D6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Study: Void Salt"
		"&7After passing through the &dWeeping Well&r&7, &8Spirit Ash&r&7 transformed into what I call \"&8Void Salt&r&7.\" This dark powder is chemically similar to Spirit Ash, but contains no carbon, so it can no longer be called \"ash.\""
		""
		"&7It seems to be composed of an unknown unstable metal bonded with some caustic substance I cannot identify. Its physical properties are also puzzling. Carbon is the basis of life, yet this substance without carbon... seems to move? I could not confirm this in my experiments, but I am almost certain this substance is alive—and mobile."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Re-examining: Void Salt"
		"&7&cNon-existence&r&7 giving rise to &aexistence&r&7—this is the manifestation of &8Shadow Arcane Energy&r&7. It may &creally&r&7 be alive... but its life is defined by the void, not by material existence. By extension, could there be more complex life in the void?"
	]
	quest.7779D406142005D6.quest_subtitle: "Clues to the Essence of Souls"
	quest.77A67AF0D408E4DC.quest_desc: [
		"&7Holding a &#66DDCCTuning Fork&7 displays the &#66FF99Essence Crucible's&7 stats."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/tuning_fork.png width:140 height:140 align:center}"
		"&7Right-click the &#66FF99Essence Crucible&7 to toggle between default or selecting a stat."
		""
		"&7The selected stat gains &e20%&7, while all others lose &e10%&7. Weakest attribute tuning and tuning strength are unaffected. If the &#66FF99Essence Crucible&7 is loaded with a &#FFAA33Celestial Mechanism&7, the gain and loss are doubled."
		""
		"&7For negative stats like &#FF6666destabilization risk&7, the change is inverted—a &e10%&7 reduction means its value increases by &e10%&7."
	]
	quest.77A67AF0D408E4DC.quest_subtitle: "Adjusting the Tuner"
	quest.77A67AF0D408E4DC.title: "Crucible Enhancement"
	quest.77CA1E58A49F362C.quest_desc: [
		"&eBasic fuel, found everywhere."
		"&6Average consumption, but low power and speed."
		""
		"⚡ Speed: 0.5x | ♨ Temperature: 1500 | ⏳ Consumption: 0.2"
		""
		"&aTip&r&7: &f♨ &r&7Temperature determines the tier of materials that can be processed, ⚡ Speed affects processing time, and ⏳ Consumption represents fuel longevity."
	]
	quest.77CA1E58A49F362C.quest_subtitle: "Classic Fuel"
	quest.7807160BB2108E79.quest_desc: ["&7Very low entry barrier—&#66CCFFQuartz Ore&7 can be mined in the Overworld with a smooth progression. Great stats, and its trait \"&#FFAA33Critical Strike&7\" is an excellent damage amplifier. A cost-effective offensive material."]
	quest.7807160BB2108E79.quest_subtitle: "Critical Choice"
	quest.78294B68D04E42A9.quest_desc: [
		"&dA blind warrior stands guard over the ancient city..."
		""
		"&7A symbol of pure strength with devastating melee capabilities. Fighting from a distance with spells or ranged attacks is a safer strategy. The Sculk Tendrils it drops are an important material for Echoing Sculk Bookshelves."
	]
	quest.783683CB8A00E9B7.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#88DDFFArcane Pylon&7 increases the effect level of simple rituals. Placing it next to a totem and providing the corresponding &#66FF99Essence&7 for the totem ritual increases the corresponding effect level."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/arcana_pylon.png width:200 height:140 align:center}"
	]
	quest.783683CB8A00E9B7.quest_subtitle: "Superior Obelisk"
	quest.783683CB8A00E9B7.title: "Aura Enhancement"
	quest.784CD820CEC6F25B.quest_desc: [
		"Move your mouse to the top-left corner of the quest selection box and look for the arrow. Click it to see the following:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/ftb_kjs3.png width:120 height:80 align:center}"
		""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"Click again to view the prerequisite quests. Select one to jump directly to it."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/ftb_kjs4.png width:120 height:80 align:center}"
		"You can also click the right arrow in the top-right corner of a quest to open a dropdown menu listing all its dependencies."
	]
	quest.784CD820CEC6F25B.quest_subtitle: "&mHow Do I Complete This Godforsaken Quest"
	quest.784CD820CEC6F25B.title: "View Prerequisites"
	quest.789A0AD70CA77553.quest_desc: [
		"&7People often use &6Gold&r&7 as a base for mystical research—its natural conductivity makes it quite useful. Essence arcane energy is no exception. By using &bholy arcane energy&r&7, gold's magical conductivity can be enhanced."
		""
		"&7Hallowed Gold's physical properties are similar to gold. Infusing the alloy with pure arcane energy allows other arcane energies to flow smoothly—Hallowed Gold is an excellent conductor for my research. It can also be used to craft several stylish item stands."
	]
	quest.789A0AD70CA77553.quest_subtitle: "In Rhythm"
	quest.78E0C869F2BB2516.quest_desc: [
		"&7As a tip upgrade, provides &#FFAA331.5&7 luck. Extremely powerful. It's recommended to &#FFD700max out&7 Lapis Lazuli on tip upgrades early on—it drastically increases loot from chests."
		""
		"&7Recommended part: &#66DDCCTip Upgrade&7"
	]
	quest.78E0C869F2BB2516.quest_subtitle: "I! AM! SO! LUCKY!"
	quest.78FE7E1CD8810721.quest_subtitle: "As the title says"
	quest.791787D97B46619C.quest_desc: ["&7The modpack includes a &#66DDCCNature's Compass&7 for locating specific biomes, but no &#66DDCCStructure Compass&7. In the early game, it's recommended to explore the Overworld first—entering the Nether too early is &#FF6666not advised&7."]
	quest.791787D97B46619C.quest_subtitle: "Did You See the Gremlin? Where?"
	quest.791787D97B46619C.title: "Exploration"
	quest.79244245C1776777.quest_desc: ["&7Pure human power—consumes a stack of steak per 100km. Can hover, and speed is decent. No notable strengths or weaknesses."]
	quest.7924CE833E734123.quest_desc: [
		"&7Holding a &#88DDFFTotem Staff&7 displays the ritual range of totems."
		"&7Right-clicking an inactive totem pole toggles its emblem's active state."
		""
		"&7A totem is a structure composed of a &#FFD700Totem Base&7 and multiple totem poles, capable of performing &#CC99FFEssence Rituals&7."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/totemic_staff.png width:160 height:160 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7924CE833E734123.quest_subtitle: "Understanding: Rituals"
	quest.7924CE833E734123.title: "Totem Resonance"
	quest.7964EFBEAA0F5D57.quest_desc: ["&7Click &a√&r&7 to unlock the next quest."]
	quest.7964EFBEAA0F5D57.quest_subtitle: "As You Can See, This Is a Quest"
	quest.7964EFBEAA0F5D57.title: "Guide"
	quest.7995CC0B134AEC55.quest_subtitle: "Wow, Golden Legend"
	quest.799B92FBA8B69A02.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Orichalcum Ingots\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" dropped by Skeletron are very useful, commonly used as a source for crafting various \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Silent Gear\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" equipment.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Once you have Orichalcum Ingots, you can also defeat some bosses to obtain their unique weapons and use them as bases for crafting \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Silent Gear\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" equipment.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"&#7EE344Chlorophyte Ore&r&7 replaces mud blocks in jungle underground above Y=0."
		""
		"&#770808Dreadstone&r&7 generates in the Overworld at depths from -64 to 0."
		""
		"&#DD660ASolar Core&7 generates in the Nether at depths from -64 to 80."
		""
		"&#E9FAFFZenith Ore&r&7 will generate."
		""
		"&#FF1C45Nether Gobber&r&7 generates in the Nether."
		""
		"&#7EE344Chlorophyte Ore&r&7's traits and stats are not outstanding, but it provides spell power and healing received—good for spellcasters."
		""
		"&#770808Dreadstone&r&7 is used to craft Dreadsteel and Shadow Ingots. The former increases Cataclysm geas count and healing received; the latter increases geas count and spell power but reduces healing received. Choose based on your needs."
		""
		"&#DD660ASolar Core&7 currently has no use."
	]
	quest.799B92FBA8B69A02.quest_subtitle: "Versatility"
	quest.799B92FBA8B69A02.title: "It's Time!"
	quest.799C21A4DB6DA05C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each &#66FF99Essence&7 harvested while equipped grants &e30&7 * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 seconds of &#FF8844Gluttony&7, or increases current &#FF8844Gluttony&7 by &e1&7 level (up to &eX&7)."
		""
		"&7When consuming &#FFAA33Gluttonous Gel&7, each equipped &#CC6666Famine Belt&7 increases &#FF8844Gluttony&7 level by +&e1&7 and duration by +&e10&7 seconds."
	]
	quest.799C21A4DB6DA05C.quest_subtitle: "Endless Hunger"
	quest.79B12E63C90B3C61.quest_desc: [
		"Can provide a temperature of 3000°C. Requires an Electric Furnace to function."
		""
		"&eA furnace is not limited to just one of these—multiple can be placed in the same furnace to supply fuel consumption."
	]
	quest.79B12E63C90B3C61.quest_subtitle: "Sustained Output"
	quest.79B7BF074539AA91.quest_desc: [
		"&6Smart Fluid Pipe&r"
		"&7Features a filter slot that can be marked with items or filters (using bucketed or bottled fluids).&r"
		"&7Only allows fluids meeting the condition to pass.&r"
		"&7Place Smart Fluid Pipes as close to the fluid source as possible to prevent &cclogging&r&7 from other fluids being extracted first.&r"
	]
	quest.7A1141EE7A34D62F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of Unsighted Resistance"
		"&7The oath dulls the edge of malevolent slashes.&r"
		"&7-Restoring &cmalevolent shelter&r&7 reduces &cmalevolent critical&r&7 damage&r"
		""
		"&7Etched into the malevolent soul-reaper's runes.&r"
		"&7-&6Malevolent criticals&r&7 charge &amalevolent shelter&r&7&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_unsighted_resistance.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7A1141EE7A34D62F.quest_subtitle: "Bound by Slaughter"
	quest.7A1141EE7A34D62F.title: "Oath of Unsighted Resistance"
	quest.7A3C6671435E2BA9.quest_desc: [
		"&eA furnace that requires materials to operate."
		""
		"&eFuel can be input via fluid pipes, etc.&r"
		"Although it requires material input to burn, higher-tier materials release significantly more heat, making it irreplaceable in certain processes."
	]
	quest.7A3C6671435E2BA9.quest_subtitle: "Thermal Smelting"
	quest.7A4449338F885205.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
		"Upon defeat, unlocks End Gobber Ore."
	]
	quest.7A4449338F885205.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2 — Unlocks Stage 3 upon defeat"
	quest.7A4D91266571EC0F.quest_desc: ["&7The &#88DDFFSoar&7 enchantment launches targets into the air, but &88DDFFSoar&7's cooldown is extended."]
	quest.7A4D91266571EC0F.quest_subtitle: "Scythe Authority"
	quest.7A63B4E0381D9BA4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Patience Repaid"
		""
		"&7Long pain is worse than short.&r&cBuffered damage becomes magic damage, and its intensity increases by one fifth when released"
		"&7Disperse impact, slow damage.&r&aBuffers half of the damage taken, converting it to damage over time&r&aBuffered damage cannot cause death"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_patience_repaid.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7A63B4E0381D9BA4.quest_subtitle: "Diluting Pain"
	quest.7A63B4E0381D9BA4.title: "Pact of Patience Repaid"
	quest.7AF763EC94AE76CA.quest_desc: ["&7Increases the enchantment storage level cap, but offers no other improvements..."]
	quest.7AF763EC94AE76CA.quest_subtitle: "Bigger Library"
	quest.7AF858E2ECF74FAD.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via altar. Search \"Generate: XXX\" in EMI to view the corresponding recipe."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7AF858E2ECF74FAD.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.7B098F5DB49DB51F.title: "Nightfall Spider"
	quest.7B2DD9D8E6237F68.quest_desc: ["The skull, representing blood sacrifice, is connected to the Nether, providing additional Quanta."]
	quest.7B2DD9D8E6237F68.quest_subtitle: "Minor Quanta Growth"
	quest.7B2DD9D8E6237F68.title: "Primitive Chaos Offering"
	quest.7B470F04445F5D8B.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I can now distinguish the composition of \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Malevolent Lead\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", which makes it easier to design its uses. Just as \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Shadow Arcane Energy\",\"color\":\"dark_gray\"},{\"text\":\" is strange, alloys made from it have special properties. When \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Deepslate Gold\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" is degraded, it produces Malevolent Lead—this \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Pewter\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" craves outward action. It longs to erode, dismantle, and erase human progress.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"This property does have mundane uses—as a weapon that further damages armor while hurting and shattering souls. Its occult applications are also significant. Malevolent Pewter is not magically inert; rather, magic seems unable to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"form\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" around it—a symbol of the decline of the pursuit of knowledge.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"This metal is quite tough and sharp, but wearing \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Anti-Magic Armor\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" certainly brings challenges... and new capabilities. I have a rough idea for crafting an armor set from it that should be extremely powerful, leveraging the metal's unique properties.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Malevolent Fortress Armor\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Malevolent Pewter\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" repels magic, so from a mage's perspective, wearing it is an odd choice. Yet I \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"am\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" a mage—and the fortress armor I crafted is incredibly powerful.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Beneath the Malevolent Pewter plating, the armor is the opposite of \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Soul-Stained Steel Armor\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\"—my soul is not protected; instead, the flow of arcane energy is disrupted by this metal. It twists arcane energy outward, disrupting incoming damage. When wearing a full set of Fortress Armor, the damage that ultimately reaches my soul is reduced to half.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"This armor affects not only incoming magic. The wearer's own arcane circuits are also affected. Their pathways to the soul are disrupted, stolen, and twisted. Yet in this dissolution of arcane energy, energy still remains. The armor reacts to this energy and grows stronger as a result.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Two key points emerge from this effect. First, the armor's magic absorption process should be called \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Malevolent Conversion\"\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\". It intercepts arcane energy destined for the soul and absorbs the resulting energy. Second, the armor weaves the stolen energy into new forms and intentions. This process should be called \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Malevolent Shelter\"\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Malevolent Shelter\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" functions as a powerful shield, directly negating almost all damage types. As the armor continuously absorbs magic, its capacity, recovery rate, and recovery bonuses grow—depending on the attributes absorbed. According to my research, this is the most powerful ability of the Malevolent Fortress Armor.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.7B470F04445F5D8B.quest_subtitle: "Evolution No Longer"
	quest.7B6F7BDF000CF379.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fusion Consciousness&r"
		""
		"&7The future holds many mysteries... but you can learn some of them in advance.&r"
		"&7-Throwing an Iron Block into the &eWeeping Well&r&7 creates &bAnomalous Constructs&r&7. Throwing a completed Construct into the Weeping Well creates a Fusion Consciousness.&r"
	]
	quest.7B6F7BDF000CF379.quest_subtitle: "A Blueprint for the Past and Future"
	quest.7B8819152EE73E21.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fruit of Life&r"
		"&7Consumables used to increase the familiar's &ahealth&r&7. Has 3 tiers, each with a usage cap.&r"
	]
	quest.7B8819152EE73E21.title: "&6Fruit of Life&r"
	quest.7BACE6601BC4DFED.quest_desc: [
		"&7Used for carrying items. Can be upgraded with &#66DDCCMineral Upgrades&7 in the order of &#FFAA33Iron&7 → &#FFD700Gold&7 → &#66CCFFDiamond&7 → &#CC99FFAlloy&7. Each upgrade expands the &#66DDCCstorage space&7. You can craft multiple backpacks if one isn't enough—never worry about carrying &#FFAA33loot&7 again. If you can't find a place to settle down, you can even carry large amounts of items in backpacks."
		""
		"&7The top-left corner of the backpack shows the slots available for &#66DDCCupgrades&7. Different upgrades have different uses; only the most common ones are covered here. Explore the rest yourself."
		""
		"&7The top-right &#FFD700settings&7 allow you to modify specific backpack options, such as &#66CCFFdisplaying items in a specific slot&7 or &#FFAA33restricting a slot to a specific item type&7. This lets you keep essential items in designated spots, unaffected by sorting, making daily storage more convenient."
	]
	quest.7BACE6601BC4DFED.quest_subtitle: "Ran Out of Space? Try a Dimensional Bag"
	quest.7BD9DC7DB2278AA5.quest_desc: [
		"&7Found in Ancient City loot chests. Offers high attack damage but no special traits—best used for alloying weapon parts."
		""
		"Recommended part: Weapon"
	]
	quest.7BD9DC7DB2278AA5.quest_subtitle: "Simple High Damage"
	quest.7BF7E53DAB408397.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" might give you a headache, but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.7BF7E53DAB408397.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.7C09F05734B44F6A.quest_desc: ["&7Hold right-click to fire a &#CC99FFVoid Grenade&7—&#FF6666damages both enemies and allies&7."]
	quest.7C09F05734B44F6A.quest_subtitle: "Ha~ji~ma~ru~yo~"
	quest.7C19C7795643C67E.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Soul-Tainted Lesion is a block that can be sliced to mass-produce &#55D5D5Soul-Tainted Flesh&7."
		"&7Right-click to \"slice\" it."
		"&7Each slice drops &#FFAA3316&7 Soul-Tainted Flesh, and it can be sliced up to &#FFAA33four&7 times."
		"&7This block is not limited to single-use production."
		""
		"&7When there are still remaining slices, it will &#66CCFFvery slowly&7 regenerate one slice for another harvest."
		"&7Once fully regenerated to &#FFAA33four&7 slices, &#FF6666growth stops&7 until it is sliced again."
		""
		"&7As long as you leave at least one slice, you'll have an &#66FF66slow but steady&7 source of Soul-Tainted Flesh."
	]
	quest.7C19C7795643C67E.quest_subtitle: "Is This Meat Fresh?"
	quest.7C227ABAEC91DA58.quest_subtitle: "Lower defense than other armor, but specializes in spell-related stats"
	quest.7C78F44CB8587BCB.quest_desc: ["&7A ranged-specialized rod material. If your weapon doesn't need to handle melee damage, it's an excellent fit—fully dedicated to ranged amplification, making every shot more threatening."]
	quest.7C78F44CB8587BCB.quest_subtitle: "*Beeeep"
	quest.7C7A1613FB9C97E8.quest_subtitle: "How did you know..."
	quest.7C7A1613FB9C97E8.title: "Caught 64 Fish"
	quest.7C7C7734793AB866.quest_desc: [
		"&6Prismarine Focusing Lens&r"
		""
		"&7Sometimes, simplicity is the answer. The Prismarine Focusing Lens refracts arcane energy rather than light, significantly reducing the &cdestabilization risk&r&7 of the &eessence focusing&r&7 process. However, stability only prevents additional wear to the Runes.&r"
	]
	quest.7C7C7734793AB866.quest_subtitle: "Stabilizing"
	quest.7CACDAC57F697371.quest_desc: ["&7Right-click to consume some durability and &#66CCFFhighlight&7 nearby &FFD700ores&7."]
	quest.7CACDAC57F697371.quest_subtitle: "Off means On?"
	quest.7CB11EBD34BA84FB.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If you wish, you can even \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"defeat\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" creatures that are \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"far weaker\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" than you...\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"&7Of course, be careful—as you defeat &cBOSSes&7, your &6rank&7 will also increase..."
		""
		"&aConsuming a &6Good Apple&a can reduce your &6rank&7 by &c1 level&7 (provided you have one)."
	]
	quest.7CB11EBD34BA84FB.quest_subtitle: "In short, before facing the bosses, let's pick a few unlucky ones to practice on."
	quest.7CB11EBD34BA84FB.title: "Practice"
	quest.7CDF0A87C605E833.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.7CE0C7EC4D46C170.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.7CEF4D8E514066A7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Tower Squid&r&7"
		"&7A common marine creature in the Starlight Dimension, smaller than vanilla squid; &r"
		""
		"&7Cannot survive out of water (completely loses mobility and slowly takes damage over time); &r"
		""
		"&7Right-click a Tower Squid with a water bucket to store it as an item (&#1E90FFTower Squid Bucket&r&7). &r"
	]
	quest.7CEF4D8E514066A7.title: "Tower Squid"
	quest.7CF77F3C6D4073BD.quest_desc: [
		"&7Essences have been successfully infused into items—they have tangibly altered the nature of objects. By manipulating these items, I can indirectly channel the power of the essences."
		""
		"&7Using these materials as a foundation, I have focused my research in three directions: Soul, Body, and the World."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7Essences are born from souls, so using their power to influence souls is straightforward. However, because they originate from souls with their own will, they cannot be fully controlled by my will alone—this often results in negative side effects."
		""
		"&7I call these essence-granted powers with negative aspects \"&4Geases&r.\""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Making essence creations affect the body is more complicated. After repeated experiments, I believe they still require a \"carrier\" to function."
		""
		"&7I call these carriers that allow essences to affect the body \"&4Runes&r.\""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7For essences to affect the world, brute force is needed—greatly increasing their power output. Since they are not acting on living beings, I have more freedom in my experiments. Bold experiments have yielded many results, mostly practical tools."
	]
	quest.7CF77F3C6D4073BD.quest_subtitle: "Inspiration Burst"
	quest.7CF77F3C6D4073BD.title: "Infinite Possibilities"
	quest.7D0410D74877C78A.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"To use \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Refined Storage\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" to store items, you need three components: \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"a Controller, a Terminal, and Storage\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The Controller powers all connected components. The \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Alternator\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" from the quest reward can be placed next to the Controller to power it. The Alternator only needs a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Large Water Wheel\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" to run.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The Terminal is where you access your storage. You can deposit and withdraw items here. The \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Terminal\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" also includes crafting functionality. The left side of the Terminal interface has many additional features for sorting items, etc.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Storage determines how many items you can hold. Each unit of storage represents one item, so a stack of cobblestone takes up 64 storage units.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"A more detailed setup example is on the next page.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"As shown below, you can place the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Controller\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Storage Terminal\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Storage Block\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" together to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"connect\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" them, while also \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"powering\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" the Controller.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/refinedstorage1.png width:180 height:100 align:center}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"size\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"number\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" of connected \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Storage Blocks\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" determine your total \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"storage capacity\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"You can also use \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"cables\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" to connect them, which will include all blocks connected by the cable network.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/refinedstorage2.png width:180 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7D0410D74877C78A.quest_subtitle: "Basic Tutorial"
	quest.7D0410D74877C78A.title: "Tips: Basic Usage"
	quest.7D237676ED4A865D.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Apotheosis Enchanting Module introduces a new crafting method—&bInfusion&7. Infusion is similar to normal enchanting but imposes certain restrictions. Almost all items have a minimum &aEterna&7 requirement, while almost none have an upper &aEterna&7 limit ("
		""
		"&7Special and powerful items may impose restrictions on &4Quanta&7 and &5Arcana&7. Some powerful items have &6very strict&7 requirements. Therefore, learning to choose and balance bookshelves is crucial."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"I will mark my &brecommended infusion bookshelves&r with gear icons as a guide."
	]
	quest.7D237676ED4A865D.quest_subtitle: "Strengthening Magic with Magic"
	quest.7D237676ED4A865D.title: "Understanding Infusion Operations"
	quest.7D271783CE2A7614.quest_desc: ["Provides early-game DoT damage and poison-type damage bonuses."]
	quest.7D271783CE2A7614.quest_subtitle: "!? Poison?!"
	quest.7D2FD37CB2502689.quest_subtitle: "Legendary Tank"
	quest.7D628BA502AB05E5.quest_desc: [
		"&7Skeletron must be summoned using Cataclysm's Soul Altar. Make sure to summon it at night—during the day, it will immediately enrage and deal massive damage capable of one-shotting players."
		""
		"After defeating Skeletron, you can take on various Cataclysm bosses to obtain their special weapon templates."
	]
	quest.7D628BA502AB05E5.quest_subtitle: "Doo Doo Da Doo Da"
	quest.7D628BA502AB05E5.title: "Target: Skeletron"
	quest.7D6295CE0F8D8951.quest_desc: [
		"&6Alternator&r"
		""
		"&7Converts rotational stress into electrical current—the reverse of the &eElectric Motor&7, which turns electricity back into rotational force. It accepts stress on one end and outputs power on the other.&r"
		""
		"&7A minimum of &c32 RPM&7 is required to operate. It has an internal energy buffer of &c5 kFE&7.&r"
		""
		"&7Through it, you can turn mechanical kinetic energy into &eElectrical Energy&7 for easier storage and remote transmission, then use Electric Motors to drive mechanisms again. Note that some energy is lost in each conversion.&r"
	]
	quest.7D98C82FDB5C8642.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FF6666Blaze Iron&7 is a rare material that can only be used in crafting."
		"&7When dropped as an item, it is &#FF6666not destroyed by fire/lava&7."
		""
		"&7Can be found with a chance in &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7 from the &#FFD700Soul Sand Valley&7 biome."
		""
		"&8It may be used as a Silent Gear material in the future... but I don't want to add more new materials in version 1.0—balance is already driving me crazy."
	]
	quest.7D98C82FDB5C8642.quest_subtitle: "It's Starting"
	quest.7DC30B49569B363E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of the Oak Grove's Might&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of the Oak Grove's Might functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bOak Grove's Might&r&7 effect, providing a fixed amount of &adamage boost&r&7, with increased effect when unarmed.&r"
	]
	quest.7DC30B49569B363E.quest_subtitle: "Strengthening Pulse"
	quest.7DDA9820D328CC3F.quest_desc: ["&7Functions like a vanilla &#66CCFFPickaxe&7. Can be crafted by placing a vanilla &#66CCFFPickaxe&7 in a crafting table to convert it into an &#66DDCCSilent Gear Pickaxe&7."]
	quest.7DDA9820D328CC3F.quest_subtitle: "Dear Friend"
	quest.7E11D3149C613671.quest_desc: [
		"&7Can accept liquids from the drain. Remember to place a mold on the Casting Table before importing liquid, or it won't solidify and will waste materials."
		""
		"&7If a mold is present, importing a certain amount of liquid will start the cooling process, turning it into different items based on the mold. You can connect a hopper to automatically collect the cooled products."
		""
		"To craft a mold, place the &6corresponding shaped item&r on the empty Casting Table, then import &6Molten Steel&r through the drain. For example, to make an ingot mold, place any ingot on the empty Casting Table, then open the drain and import 360mB of Molten Steel."
		""
		"&7Molten Steel is crafted in the furnace by smelting coal and iron in a 1:1 ratio—four coal and four iron yield 360mB of Molten Steel."
	]
	quest.7E11D3149C613671.quest_subtitle: "Casting Fluid into Items"
	quest.7E59A0E6979C8FF1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Blazing Fire"
		"&7The nature of fire is undeniable.&r"
		"&7-Forcibly extinguishing fire subjects you to a &cblast of infernal arcane energy&r"
		""
		"&7Nothing can withstand flame.&r"
		"&7-&eFire effects&r&7 on enemies are more powerful&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_prospector.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7E59A0E6979C8FF1.quest_subtitle: "Adding Fuel to the Fire"
	quest.7E59A0E6979C8FF1.title: "Pact of Blazing Fire"
	quest.7EB97CBE6483FCF7.quest_desc: ["But I still have to remind you—the Dorm Manager only spawns when you have a regular sleep schedule now..."]
	quest.7EB97CBE6483FCF7.quest_subtitle: "Sleep Well"
	quest.7EF077D05E3E3B7E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Tenacity&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Tenacity steadies the wearer's stance, nullifying all &cknockback&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.7EF077D05E3E3B7E.quest_subtitle: "Withstanding the Unstoppable"
	quest.7F0DAB4DB433FC15.quest_desc: ["Grants Resistance when used for armor, though it also applies Weakness. Early on, pairing it with flying swords might yield unexpected results."]
	quest.7F0DAB4DB433FC15.quest_subtitle: "High-Value Protection"
	quest.7F11174C00472167.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starlight Forest&r"
		"&7A surface biome in the Starlight Dimension—the most ordinary and common."
		""
		"&7The main tree is the &eMoonlight Tree&r."
		"&7Compared to its variant (the &8Dense Starlight Forest&r&7), Moonlight Trees here generally grow &ataller&r."
		"&7Trees are spaced &afurther apart&r&7, and the ground under the canopy is relatively &amore open&r."
		""
		"&7Besides &eStarlight Berry&r&7 vines hanging from leaves, there are also unique plants: &8Starlight Flowers, Starlight Torch Flowers, Yellow Ridge Grass, and more&r."
		"&7Some &alight-emitting plants&r&7 also reduce monster spawning on the surface."
	]
	quest.7F11174C00472167.quest_subtitle: "Perfectly Ordinary"
	quest.7F11174C00472167.title: "Starlight Forest"
	quest.7F2C0291CE6F6B66.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Lust\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When attacking:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Each attack applies 1 stack of \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Rose\"\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\" to the target (max once every 0.5 seconds).\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The attacker takes \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"1 additional damage\",\"color\":\"red\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\"Rose\"\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\" reaches 7 stacks, trigger effect:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The attacker \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"restores 15% of max health\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Apply a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"random debuff\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" to the target for 10 seconds.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"All debuffs on the target have their \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"stack count increased by 1\",\"color\":\"yellow\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Passive: You \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"cannot die from bleed damage\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\"; bleed damage will leave you with at least 1 health.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.7F2C0291CE6F6B66.quest_subtitle: "Lust Erosion"
	quest.7F2C0291CE6F6B66.title: "Lust Erosion"
	quest.7F578E1D8C765465.quest_desc: [
		"&7Essence rituals mostly share common traits. Simple rituals manifest their effects by seeking &#DDA0DDritual sites&7, while more complex rituals—those that aim to affect the world without a specific target—manifest through solid &#DDA0DDritual sites&7."
		""
		"&7When solid ritual sites form, they drift in the direction indicated by the totem. I measured their movement speed as precisely four blocks per second, and they can activate their carried effect up to eight times before dissipating."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7Tainted Stone has a unique negative effect on magic. It disrupts the flow of arcane energy, eventually dismantling it entirely. Without any special structure, the only concern is this disruptive property. When a ritual site passes through &#888888Tainted Stone&7, it does not activate its effect and therefore does not dissipate."
		""
		"&7Finally, ritual sites are intangible—they have no mass, are unaffected by gravity, and can pass through any solid matter."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7The &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 is a device that can guide and enhance drifting ritual sites. By embedding &#CC99FFessence arcane energy&7 into it, a flight path is established, influencing all sites that pass through. The arcane etching technology used for the path is sensitive, so the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 does not function when affected by Redstone."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/rite_anchor.png width:200 height:90 align:center}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Site Speed"
		"&7Embedding &#66DDCCVoid Essence&7 into the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 grants speed bonuses, accelerating the site's movement. Each site can accept this effect twice, doubling speed each time."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Site Strength"
		"&7Embedding &#3399FFAquatic Essence&7 into the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 grants strength bonuses, enhancing interactions with certain ritual anchor etchings. Each site can accept this effect twice, doubling strength each time."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Site Effect"
		"&7Embedding &#66BB66Earth Essence&7 into the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 grants effect bonuses, increasing the intensity of each activation's effect. Each site can accept this effect twice, doubling effect each time."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Site Range"
		"&7Embedding &#FF6633Infernal Essence&7 into the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 grants range bonuses, allowing the site to travel farther before dissipating. Each site can accept this effect twice, doubling range each time."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Site Repair"
		"&7Embedding &#88DDFFHoly Essence&7 into the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 grants self-repair, extending the site's lifespan and enabling it to travel farther. Each site can accept this effect four times."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Site Resurrection"
		"&7Embedding &#CC6666Malevolent Essence&7 into the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 forces the site to sacrifice existing elemental bonuses for immediate repair. It has the same limit as Holy Essence."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Site Guidance"
		"&7Embedding &#CC99FFArcane Essence&7 into the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 changes the site's flight path without consumption or side effects. Arcane Essence is pure energy without direction, so its effect is fittingly simple."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Site Splitting"
		"&7Embedding &#888888Shadow Essence&7 into the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 splits the site into two independent but identical copies. Each site can accept this effect four times. Copies are monochrome and cannot be split further."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Ritual Study: Elemental Bonuses"
		"&7A site is a primitive arcane construct with no specialization, so its functions are limited. This can be solved by using the &#66CCFFRitual Anchor&7 to deliver elemental essences—but I need to document the specific effects."
		""
		"&7When a ritual site passes through a ritual anchor with &#66DDCCVoid&7, &#3399FFAquatic&7, &#66BB66Earth&7, or &#FF6633Infernal&7 etchings, it receives an elemental bonus. Only the first two within each group take effect. Since the site is structurally simple, it can receive at most four bonuses total."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Ritual Study: Site Resurrection"
		"&7A site is a primitive arcane construct. My prototype only required that the etchings be effective and the site mobile. Later, I added self-sustenance to the key features. Not quite self-regeneration like a living thing, but it can maintain itself."
		""
		"&7When receiving a command from &#CC6666Malevolent Essence&7, the site forces self-sacrifice. It abandons all existing elemental bonuses. Speed is least important and is sacrificed first, followed by strength, then effect. Range is most important and is only sacrificed when no other bonuses remain."
	]
	quest.7F578E1D8C765465.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Energy in Motion"
	quest.7F578E1D8C765465.title: "Site Management"
	quest.7F921AB47163D20E.quest_desc: [
		"&7This item modifies the maximum spawn delay. Each item affects 20 ticks. Typically used with Sugar."
		""
		"&7The minimum and maximum spawn delays combine to determine the spawn interval, which randomly falls between the two values."
	]
	quest.7F921AB47163D20E.quest_subtitle: "MADE IN HEAVEN"
	quest.7FB5C401A36A72B5.quest_desc: ["&7Base stats are unremarkable—relies on the &#FFD700Feast&7 mechanic to stack up. When fully stacked, the bonuses are solid—a potential-heavy material worth investing in."]
	quest.7FB5C401A36A72B5.quest_subtitle: "Feast Core"
	quest.7FD6941949B8C8F4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Crafter&r"
		"&7A component that automates item crafting.&r"
		"&7Stress consumption: &c2 su/RPM&r"
		""
		"&6Usage&r"
		"&6Crafting Items&r"
		"&7The Mechanical Crafter can perform '&eAutomatic Crafting&r&7' and '&6Mechanical Crafting&r&7' recipes.&r"
		"&7'Automatic Crafting' automatically matches any vanilla Crafting Table recipe; 'Mechanical Crafting' uses special Create-added recipes.&r"
		""
		"&6Placement and Adjustment&r"
		"&7To craft items, place multiple Crafters in a shape matching the recipe, forming a &ecrafting structure&r&7.&r"
		"&7Then use a Wrench to adjust internal paths, connecting the Crafters' crafting pathways.&r"
		"&7After connecting, an &aitem output&r&7 must be set, or crafting cannot complete.&r"
		""
		"&6Material Input and Power&r"
		"&7Players can right-click the front of a Crafter to insert items, or input from any side via logistics. Crafters are also valid Mechanical Arm targets.&r"
		"&7Crafters are driven by stress input via a gear on the side. They transmit power internally, so only one connection is needed per structure.&r"
		""
		"&6Operation&r"
		"&6Triggering&r"
		"&7A crafting structure starts automatically when all Crafters are filled. To force-start an unfilled structure, apply a Redstone signal to any Crafter.&r"
		"&7Installing a '&eCrafter Slot Cover&7' on a Crafter prevents it from storing items, but counts it as filled. The structure starts when all other Crafters are filled.&r"
		""
		"&6Crafting Process&r"
		"&7When active, materials move step-by-step from the end to the output. Each step takes &c1000/RPM ticks&r&7.&r"
		"&7When all materials reach the end, the recipe completes after one step, ejecting the product.&r"
		"&7If the end Crafter points to a container, the product goes there.&r"
		"&7If the recipe isn't valid, all materials are ejected at the last step.&r"
		""
		"&6Connecting&r"
		"&7Right-click the seam between two same-facing Crafters with a Wrench to connect them. When one Crafter is filled, items are evenly distributed among all connected Crafters.&r"
		"&7Right-click the same seam again to disconnect.&r"
		""
		"&6Crafting Speed&r"
		"&7Speed is primarily determined by RPM, but steps needed also affect it. A more optimized path reduces steps and improves efficiency.&r"
		""
		"&8This manuscript feels sticky—you wonder what the owner was crafting.&r"
	]
	quest.7FF37718528D1FB5.quest_desc: ["&6Compared to the previous two lexicons, the Extraction Lexicon is especially valuable—it can completely extract enchantment energy from an item without damaging it.&r"]
	quest.7FF37718528D1FB5.quest_subtitle: "Recycle... No! Reuse!"
	quest.7FFEDC8A8DA45A2F.quest_desc: [
		"# &6Font Preferences &r"
		""
		"### &eAvailable Fonts &r"
		"&fThe modpack provides two fonts by default:"
		"&7- Path: &e\\\\kubejs\\\\assets\\\\ &r"
		"&7- &6ChironGoRoundTC &r (default)"
		"&7- &6Maple_UI.ttf &r"
		""
		"### &bHow to Switch Fonts &r"
		"1. Press &4Ctrl + K &r to open the modern UI control panel"
		"2. Click &ePreferences &r"
		"3. &eScroll right &r in the interface"
		"4. Select your preferred font"
		""
		"### &3Custom Fonts &r"
		"&7- You can download other font files"
		"&7- Place the font file in any directory and call it directly"
		"&7- &aAll default fonts are free for commercial use—no copyright risk &r"
		""
		"&7- Default font: &6ChironGoRoundTC .ttf &r"
	]
	quest.7FFEDC8A8DA45A2F.quest_subtitle: "Don't Like the Modpack Font!"
